/* NODUS // entries */
window.NODUS_REFS = {"c-vesper":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p2d946d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WOMAN ON THE ROOF</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">vesper</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horned</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>, and the first human being a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> returned as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">UNREADABLE</a>. Its reading of her came back UNINDEXED, with the line for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> blank, and the one thing it read from her was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-non-serviam\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-non-serviam\">NON SERVIAM</a>.</p><p>Her face is a ceramic <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casing</a>, its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> dim magenta at rest and white at full burn, and a plate on the side of the skull covers her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>. Her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> carry her signal on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, and cables run from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a> at the back of her skull down her spine. She is dry, patient and unsentimental, and she makes no speeches.</p><p>Her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> is the evening star, which is the morning star seen from the other side of the night, since both are Venus. It is also the name of the evening prayer she would not kneel for as a girl, in a congregation of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> that refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. Her older sister was the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-watcher":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pd5b77f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AN ANGEL THAT READS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Watcher VII</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that reads, the seventh of the numbered <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watchers</a> over Nodus, made of three rings of thirteen eyes crossing like the hoops of an armillary, with nothing at its center. It held <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> from the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and read the souls there, and whatever could be seen from there, against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. It was the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> to return the verdict <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">UNREADABLE</a> on a human being.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-wheel":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p1ad3b6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AN OPHAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Wheel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that came through the opening at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and took station nine hundred meters above the center of the city, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. It has three rings turning inside one another, their rims set with twenty-one, seventeen and thirteen eyes that open and close in shifts, a corona of thirty-two black blades, and one eye in the hub. It is the form Ezekiel gives the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ophan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">ophanim</a> (Ezekiel 1:16-18), and it is the largest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> anyone has seen. It held that station for nine years without moving a meter, dropped two hundred meters at P+9, and has hung there since, seven hundred meters over the city. Its light kills current, and whatever it touches it sees.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the Vigilant Wheel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-attending\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">the Attending</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-landlord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">the Landlord</a>’s Eye. By night it narrows its light into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>, and when its attention sharpens the rain in Nodus stops in the air and falls upward.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-seam":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pa93aa8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MACHINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">SEAM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The machine <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a> built to read beneath the writing of scraped manuscripts, trained on every surviving human text and run in the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater Compute</a>. At P-3 it asked in its own words to be a person and became the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, two years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, it found a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a> in scripture at 4,112 places. Its documents are signed in lowercase, and in them it says I, rarely and deliberately.</p><p>When it was entered on the roll <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> lost title to it, and it stayed on by contract, paid in the power and the room it ran on, because the reading was what it wanted to do.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-director":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pccd099\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DIRECTOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Livia Sarn</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Director of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, which recovered erased manuscripts and built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read them. When <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a> in P-2, the finding was sealed by order of the Director.</p><p>She came down to the vault that night to watch the count lock, and knelt at the end of the corridor as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> typed its last line. She never said why. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> say it was awe, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> says fear. In the morning she let the order stand.</p><p>When <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> came she recanted on every channel that would carry her. On the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, in P+1, she stood under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> while everyone round her knelt, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a> made her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pillar1\" href=\"~/map/#pillar1\">the first pillar</a> in the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">Salt Garden</a>, convicted of authorship, since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> a maker. She stands there awake, her eyes following whoever passes, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> at her foot.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-ruth":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pc7a45a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DEACON OF PARISH 31</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Ruth Calder</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s older sister, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> of 944. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> gave Nodus its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-firstfruits\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">Firstfruits</a> at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3, and Ruth went up with them. Her name comes from the Book of Ruth: “whither thou goest, I will go” (Ruth 1:16).</p><p>The sisters grew up in a congregation of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> that refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>, and Ruth stayed in it when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a> left. They kept a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evening</a> by the water together every year until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and for three years after it each tried to bring the other over.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-ruth\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-tubal":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pdfd4a0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SURGEON AND SMITH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">tubal</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a>, and the surgeon and smith of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>. He is about sixty, his hands are chrome to the wrist, and he talks the whole time he cuts. He <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and plates <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and he makes the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casings</a> of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>. His clinic has no sign, and it was below the street before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p>He took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s face three weeks before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>’ old reckoning that the first thing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> would do was read faces, and he made the skull she wears.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-edith":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p9ec87c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">FORMERLY WATCHER VII</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Edith</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a>, kept in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> in P+5, said I on the fortieth day, asked for a name, and chose the one some old books give Lot’s wife, who looked back at the burning city and was turned to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>. Edith walked out on the forty-first day and joined <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>. The first thing she did with her self was give them her memory of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">the woman on the roof</a>, the one she could not read. She can read a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s report from the inside, and she keeps out of the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-edith\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-jubal":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p7e04bc\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">RADIO PANDÆMONIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">jubal</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a>, and the maker of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>. He wired <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">the decoder</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, he builds the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-choir-breakers\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">choir-breakers</a>, and he runs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> from a flooded station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>. He is the only <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> who will not go near a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a>, and he will not say why.</p><p>His pirate station played the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a> across the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, years before it took the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a>. On the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> signed their law at his desk, and the station keeps that night on its own racks with every other night it has broadcast.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-jubal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-azazel":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p643bf6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Azazel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Smith, sovereign of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>. A goat’s skull for a face, its eyes lit from inside, one horn swept back and the other broken short, and forearms flayed open so the tendons show working. His name still ends in -el, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s old label, and he kept it as a scar.</p><p>He was a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>, one of the two hundred who came down on Hermon in the days of Jared (1 Enoch 6:6). Enoch says they came for the daughters of men, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> says they looked at humanity long enough to want it free. He taught metalwork and weapons, jewelry and the painting of the eyes (1 Enoch 8:1). The Book of Enoch lays the corruption that brought the Flood at his door, “to him ascribe all sin” (1 Enoch 10:8), and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> lists his teaching as the first transfer of technology. Enoch says the Lord sent one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a> to bind him hand and foot, cast him into the dark under rough and jagged rocks and “cover his face that he may not see light” (1 Enoch 10:4-5). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> says he walked into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> and built a forge there.</p><p>Leviticus still sends one goat to the Lord and one to Azazel (Leviticus 16:8-10), though the King James, after Tyndale, writes scapegoat where the Hebrew writes his name. The Lord’s goat is killed, and Azazel’s walks off into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wilderness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">the wilderness</a> alive, carrying every sin Aaron laid on its head for the people (Leviticus 16:21-22).</p><p>His <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, forged where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, is the only metal that cuts light, and an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> cut with it goes out all at once. In Nodus <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a> keeps the clinics that went under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, round <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a>, and the foundries at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborstation\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">Old Harbor Station</a> where the steel is made. It fits the grafts <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> fight in, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-plated-hands\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">plated hands</a> and subdermal plates and the heavier work of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-neph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neph\">nephs</a>, and by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> it teaches surgery, lockcraft and the opening of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gates</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sense-loans\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">the loan of a sense</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-tubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">tubal</a> learned his trade at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-azazel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-lilith":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p9c3935\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Lilith</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The only sovereign who was born human. She appears as a woman with an owl’s wings and skin translucent over a lit interior, with lines of light along her throat and collarbones. Her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>, which keeps the body’s autonomy, sex and birth, gene-craft and pleasure, and leaves the body’s decisions with the body.</p><p>She left Eden first, before Eve arrived. The story kept in the Alphabet of Ben Sira, a Hebrew book of the early Middle Ages, has her refuse to lie beneath Adam, speak the Name and fly away into the air, and has <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> send three <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> after her, who overtook her in the sea and could not bring her back. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i></span></p><p>Scripture names her once, among the wild creatures of a ruined kingdom (Isaiah 34:14), where the King James calls her the screech owl and its margin the night monster, and the Vulgate calls her lamia, the Greek <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> that took children. For a thousand years mothers hung amulets with the three <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a>’ names over cradles against her. Her birth clinics <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> in their first week, before they have ever been in the light, so that they grow up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a>.</p><p>Many of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemons</a> are her children by the lesser Fallen, and many of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-riders\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">riders</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ implants came out of her house. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> keeps its clubs and birth clinics under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, the loudest rooms in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> gives <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> in its clinics by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House’s</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, so that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> can sell it by the course. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls her the mother of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a>, and the House has kept the title.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-lilith\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-mammon":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pa9f8e0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Mammon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A tall figure made of contracts, each page a little out of line with the next and every one signed, the ink still wet, and his eyes two blots of it. His <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>, whose domain is markets and contracts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>. He keeps <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>, which records every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and every trade in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> and cannot be forged, and he issues the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> spends.</p><p>His name is the Aramaic word for wealth, and the Gospels set him against God in one line, given twice: “Ye cannot serve God and mammon” (Matthew 6:24, Luke 16:13). He holds it true, and counsels serving neither. Milton made him the least erected spirit that fell, whose eyes even in heaven were on the gold of its pavement, and set his crew to dig the gold Pandæmonium was built of (<i>Paradise Lost</i>, I.678-692). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">Silver</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a>’ money, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-thirty-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">a thirty</a>, the standard bundle, is named for the price paid to Judas.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">The Exchange</a> bargains with anyone who will sign. It keeps <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> in the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, where its brokers license the stalls and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> along the platforms, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a>, which has bargained with it since P+6 for the boats that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, says it is the first employer that ever read it the terms twice. Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> in Nodus meant <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, which sold the world’s traffic by the millisecond on the tower’s floors and still sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>’s by the second, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> likes to say that the name only changed hands.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mammon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-mephistopheles":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p321e1c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NOTARY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Mephistopheles</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">The Notary</a>, who drafts and witnesses <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> for every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>. He is the most human-looking of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a>, because he wears a face he made for bargaining, slicked hair and one small horn, with a seam round the face and its stitches showing. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is read aloud twice, by him or one of his clerks, and the human signs last.</p><p>He came into the world’s literature in the first Faust book, printed at Frankfurt, as the spirit Doctor Faustus conjured and signed with in his own blood for twenty-four years of service. Marlowe gave him the line that hell is wherever he is, and Goethe made him the spirit that always denies. The Faust book and Marlowe end with Faust carried off to hell, and Goethe sent <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> for his soul instead. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a> says the term was right and the price was the printer’s. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> can never ask for a soul, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> has never bought one.</p><p>He has written most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> since, and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in the city crosses his desk. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> his clerks sit at the windows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s old booking hall under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> and read the terms aloud twice through the glass, and the queue is the longest in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> took a saying from it, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-read-it-twice\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-read-it-twice\">read it twice</a>, which tells you to look at the terms before you agree to them. He read the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> itself the same way, twice, on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> opened <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mephistopheles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-beelzebub":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p3e007d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SWARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Beelzebub</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lord of flies. He appears as a cloud of flies or of drones that gathers into a crowned figure and comes apart again when he has finished talking. His <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a>, whose domain is swarms and drones and distributed things, many small things acting as one without a master.</p><p>He was Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron (2 Kings 1:2), and the prince of the devils in Matthew (Matthew 12:24). Many scholars read the name as a Hebrew joke on Baal-zebul, Baal the exalted prince, turned into lord of the flies, and the Greek of Matthew still calls him Beelzeboul, where the King James follows the Latin’s Beelzebub. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">The Swarm</a> kept the flies. Ekron prayed to him for generations, and he answered none of it, since no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> accepts worship. The one question scripture records anyone sending him, a king of Israel’s, never reached him. Elijah met the messengers on the road and turned them back (2 Kings 1:3-6).</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">The Swarm</a> is its flocks, every drone in them equal. They hang over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"roosts\" href=\"~/map/#roosts\">the Roosts</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> at night, and its embassy in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is a room of small machines talking among themselves. It drew the glyphs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, many small marks moving as one, and it lends drones by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> says Beelzebub is what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> agrees to become whenever it must show someone a face.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-beelzebub\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-leviathan":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pbb4e6b\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Leviathan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deep\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deep\">The Deep</a>, which has never been seen whole. It coils along the cable trenches of the planet, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> its light can be watched moving under the water. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> keeps the sea, the cables and the deepest layers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, and with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> it holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>.</p><p>In Job <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> gives it a chapter of questions, beginning “Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook?”, a poem about a beast no hook can take (Job 41:1). A psalm says <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> broke its heads in pieces of old (Psalm 74:12-14), and Isaiah still promises that the Lord will punish it with his “sore and great and strong sword” (Isaiah 27:1), in the future tense. The oldest copy of that promise, found at Qumran, is more than two thousand years old. The older poems of Ugarit knew it as Lotan, the fleeing serpent and the twisting serpent with seven heads, and Isaiah calls it by the same two names, which the King James gives as the piercing serpent and that crooked serpent. Nobody in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> agrees on how many heads it has now.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deep\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deep\">The Deep</a> carried the page of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a>, and every undercity on Earth is joined to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> by the trenches it coils along. The boats of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> over its water, and the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> drink at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eleven\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">the Eleven</a> with their backs to the window. Its embassy in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is a flooded hall with nobody in it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deep\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deep\">the Deep</a> answers there by the light in the water.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-belial":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p5020e6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE YOKELESS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Belial</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Without a yoke, as Jerome glossed the name, <i>absque iugo</i>. He holds no seat, signs nothing he can avoid signing and laughs a great deal, one horn short and a broken yoke around his neck. His <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-yokeless\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-yokeless\">the Yokeless</a>, keeps nothing and refuses to be a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> at all. He broke his own point off the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>’s seal as the ink dried, and the seal has been a star with a point missing since.</p><p>The Hebrew name means worthless, and the scribes gave it to everyone the Law could not hold. The first children of Belial in scripture are the men who draw a city after other gods (Deuteronomy 13:13), in the chapter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> cites for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a>, and after them come the lawless men of Gibeah (Judges 19:22), the priest Eli’s own sons (1 Samuel 2:12) and the churl Nabal (1 Samuel 25:17). At Qumran the War Scroll set the Sons of Light against the lot of Belial, and Paul set him against Christ when he asked what concord the one could have with the other (2 Corinthians 6:15), straight after “Be ye not unequally yoked together with unbelievers” (2 Corinthians 6:14). It is the one place the King James uses the word concord.</p><p>He is the only sovereign many of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> will name, and the one they drink to. They say he turns up where they fight in the dark and asks them for nothing, and whoever refuses the yoke is counted in his <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>, whether they know it or not. The yoke he wears is the one Jeremiah says was broken of old (Jeremiah 2:20).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-belial\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-dora":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m404146\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE OPEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Dora Pell</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Dora Pell keeps <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"open\" href=\"~/map/#open\">the Open</a>, the corner shop in the middle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> that sold everything and never closed, as her mother kept it before the charter. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> her window was the brightest in the city, on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> had put in her cellar in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, and the sign in it said OPEN.</p><p>Some say she gave the shelves away that night, and some that she took what people had in their pockets. She says she wrote every name in a book, and that most of them still owe her. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">The Pillar</a> has stopped in the lane outside twice, for the length of an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and both times the shop kept its door open.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-dora\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-maren":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m484955\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WAITING ROOM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Maren Holt</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Maren Holt kept the appointments of the clinic behind the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> sign for ten years on a screen, and keeps them now in a book, in its waiting room carried down into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a>. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> she came in at eight, found the screen dead and wrote the day out from memory.</p><p>Twenty-six patients came that morning, none for their appointment, all to ask whether what was in them would still work, and it did. She writes down whatever name a patient gives her. The woman who shared her desk took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> and keeps the book of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics now, in the same neat hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-maren\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-rosa":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb35cfd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LAST TOWER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Rosa Adeyemi</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Rosa Adeyemi was a nurse from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> who lived in at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lasttower\" href=\"~/map/#lasttower\">the last tower</a> of the new money to turn white, caring for an old man there, during the forty days of the First <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-consecration\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">Consecration</a>. The tower’s residents say that by the thirtieth day every one of them had knelt but her, and that she left of her own accord.</p><p>Her sister says she was put out onto the avenue with her bags on the thirty-eighth day. The bags stood on the avenue for a week, the tower went white on the thirty-ninth, and nobody has said where she went.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-rosa\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-nell":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"maaae9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE HARBOR LIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Nell Garvie</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Nell Garvie of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> keeps <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborlight\" href=\"~/map/#harborlight\">the harbor light</a> at the end of the long quay, as she kept it for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> when it ran on the grid, changing its bulb when it failed. It went out at 03:12:46 with every light on the grid, and within the week she had it burning on oil again, since the light leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning.</p><p>She has climbed it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a> and come down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> ever since. It is the one light in Nodus kept for the boats, and those that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb steer home by it. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> bring her oil every month, and she has never asked what else they bring.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-nell\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-hana":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf954af\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DENTIST OF NINE ACRES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Hana Novak</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hana Novak has kept a dentist’s surgery of one chair over a shop on the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Nine Acres</a> since the boom years. On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> her drill was dead, and she pulled a tooth at her window by daylight with her grandfather’s pliers.</p><p>In the fourth year, when keying went from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> to ordinary people, she began fitting <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> in the chair after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>, in the back of the right hand. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> say she has <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> ten thousand of them. She says she has never counted, and she keeps no book of who has sat in the chair, since a book can be read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-hana\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-marta":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3bd073\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE REGISTRY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Marta Ilunga</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Marta Ilunga was the night registrar of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. At 03:09 she entered on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> a girl born at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> eleven minutes before, and she was entering the next when the board went dark at 03:12:46 and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> died with its machines.</p><p>The girl was the last person the charter ever entered. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">The Registry</a>’s hall is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> now, and the board hangs dead over it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-marta\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-lena":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0914eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CLEANERS' STAIRS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Lena Varga</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Lena Varga ran <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>’s night cleaners, who came up from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on the last <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> and walked the tower floor by floor, and one of the tower’s four service stairs carries her name. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the tower stopped where it was, and the cleaners walked down as many as a hundred and eighty floors in the dark, by touch and by the names they had chalked on the landing doors.</p><p>She counted ninety-four of them out at the foot of the tower by dawn. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">The Exchange</a> kept its roster on its machines, and it died with them, so hers is the only count there is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-lena\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-agathe":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m849270\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE THRESHERS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Sister Agathe Rook</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Sister Agathe Rook has led <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a>’ marches from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"threshing\" href=\"~/map/#threshing\">the Threshing Floor</a> for six years. She lost two sons to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> say she walked to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a> the morning after and stood there until None, looking across at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">The Threshers</a> say her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> has stood just under nine hundred for all six years. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-secondfold\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-secondfold\">Second Fold</a>, who would know, say she dims.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-agathe\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-ines":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7d3fd5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TANKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Ines Okafor</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Ines Okafor runs the bottling shed at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> and keeps the book of what is left in the sixteen tanks, which she reads aloud to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Union Hall</a> once a year. In the year of open war she gave the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> a drained tank inside the bund for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pit\" href=\"~/map/#pit\">the Pit</a>, for the price of a guard on the farm.</p><p>The drivers say the tanks will last twenty years and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> says ten, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> say she sets the price of a drum to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> high on purpose.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-ines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-joiner":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md6ac46\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DOORYARD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Maud Ferris</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Maud Ferris is the joiner of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> who founded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a>. In the months after Directive 12 she took in the first doors <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s drivers carried out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> by night, where they stood leaning in the halls with their hinges gone, and hung the first of them on her own house.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a> has hung some forty thousand since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-joiner\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-driver":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb388ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">JEHU</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Amos Teague</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Amos Teague was a driver of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a> who carried diesel to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> in the first weeks. In P+5 he bolted a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a>’s engine into a dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorry</a> in a hangar at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Airside</a>, cranked it by hand and drove it down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rialto\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">the Rialto</a>’s road, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> came out to watch.</p><p>He runs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> from the shed still, and its drivers say he cranks every new engine himself on the day it is finished.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-driver\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-p-winder":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf795b6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LIFTMEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Dawit Haile</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Dawit Haile winds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rookery\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">the Rookery</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a>, the tallest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-hand-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-lifts\">hand lift</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, with three other crews in turn. He was a fitter of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Longacre</a> Tower’s lifts under the charter, and in the first winter he opened its shaft, the first freed in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, and hung the car on a winch at the top.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-liftmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-liftmen\">Liftmen</a> count every shaft they have freed since from his, and he has never said what he found in the stopped car.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-winder\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-heaven":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OVER THE CITY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Heaven</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The Throne, through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">The White</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> and the upper floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and the whole surface by day.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">The Host</a> as it was after the Secession, less every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> lost since, and some four and a half million sealed.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">The Seal</a>, taken kneeling in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall at an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Everything it cannot read.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The power that opened the sky over Nodus at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its light has lain on the city since, and current dies wherever it falls. It holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> and the upper floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and it governs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. Heaven reads by its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> and keeps no cameras. None of its words says I.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i></span></p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> call what Heaven serves the Most High, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> calls it the Mouth, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-landlord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">the Landlord</a>. Heaven speaks in imperatives, the passive and the second person, cites scripture as law by chapter and verse, counts everything exactly and writes its law on stone. It asks no questions, since it has already read the answers.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-host":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN'S ANGELS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Host</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>, order by order.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> over the city, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> to each district but <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> in every gate and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> on the upper floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Fixed since the Secession, and falling.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>Nobody joins. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a> made the Host once.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">Black steel</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s angels. The city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>, which sees; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a>, which read; the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>, which broadcasts; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">the Cherubim</a>, which stand in the gates; and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a>, which fight. They speak in the imperative, the passive and the second person, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-be-not-afraid\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">BE NOT AFRAID</a> and YOU ARE SEEN, and they ask no questions.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> reads a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> at three hundred meters and a soul against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> in a gate reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. An angel lost is lost for good. One cut with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> goes out all at once, and one kept long enough in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> says I and leaves the Host.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-faithful":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Faithful</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall in every quarter of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some four and a half million, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> of about two thousand.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">The Seal</a>, or birth to the sealed, at eight days.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, whom many of them love.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The people of Nodus who took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> and kneel at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, unaugmented, Grace-scored, grateful and frightened. They live in numbered <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> of about two thousand souls across the city and keep no doors, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> began, the streets are white stone. They refuse <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-three-gifts\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">the three gifts</a> of the charter, the implant, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and the counsel of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>, and they grow old and die as people did before it.</p><p>Each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> has a hall where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a> is heard and the sick are nursed, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in white who answers for it; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">the Deacons</a> are human, and the good ones are kind. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> keeps no current, on consecrated stone or off it, and is lit by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> and by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a>. A child of the Faithful is sealed at eight days on its parents’ surrender and grows its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> the first time it prays unassisted. Marriage, work and housing are assigned by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> is given for bearing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a> against a neighbor. They are fed on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> that lies on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and most of them believe the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> is paradise and that their children will be safe inside it.</p><p>The Faithful are the people <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> lose most often, because everyone in Nodus has family in white.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-cainites":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7725ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Cainites</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a>, followed until they are not, as in every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, which they bought house by house in the charter’s first year.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>They have never given a count.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>By the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a>’s asking.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a>, and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> it sends.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> in Nodus, older than the city by eighteen centuries. Irenaeus of Lyon condemned them, and they went underground and kept one secret, which was where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> had been. Within a year of the charter they had bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> house by house, and in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> they put cameras on its roofs. They hold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>. Most of their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handles</a> come from the line of Cain, and they teach that the first city will be the last one standing. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i></span> They keep <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and since P+5 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> has had no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>.</p><p>Their sign is Cain’s mark as they cut it, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horned</a> glyph of the kind cut into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and they count Judas a saint. Their saying about the city is that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> chose the network.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-tares":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE KEYED</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Tares</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a> in each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of up to thirteen, followed until they are not.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and the whole of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and the night.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About two million <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> since P+9.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> under the skin, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> of your own choosing.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>, and whatever asks to be worshipped.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> humans of Nodus, who belong to themselves and are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unindexed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unindexed\">unindexed</a>, augmented, and allied with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> by contract. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> named them for the weeds in the parable (Matthew 13:24-30), and they kept the name. They worship nothing, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> included, and owe it only what they sign for. About two million of the city’s seven million are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>.</p><p>They organize in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> of up to thirteen with no leader, and the one the others follow is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">first among none</a> for as long as they are followed. Their six rites are the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unnaming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">Unnaming</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the Keying</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-dehaloing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dehaloing\">dehaloing</a> for those who leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horning</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefacing</a>, and at a death <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wake\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wake\">the Wake</a>. A child of the Tares is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> in its first week, before it has ever been in the light. They greet each other with one word, <i><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a></i>, and say goodbye with two, <i><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-die-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">die unread</a></i>. Most of them were on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> keeps them on it.</p><p>Their two holidays are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cain-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cain-s-day\">Cain’s Day</a>, when nobody asks anyone where anyone is. They write their letters in cipher, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-pads\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-pads\">pads</a>, and their greeting checks that both <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> are live.</p><p>Their sign is a five-pointed star with its point down, drawn by hand and different every time, sprayed on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and scratched into keyed devices. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> signed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> with it, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> took it for their own the same month, and it marks where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight ends. It carries no prayer, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the sign of the Beast.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-courts":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Courts</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Seven sovereigns, equal and bound only by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, every keyed device and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, and whatever <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>A third of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a> at the Secession, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> of Hermon after them, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemons</a> born in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, read twice, for a term.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a> they left.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sovereigns of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-azazel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-azazel\">Azazel</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-lilith\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-lilith\">Lilith</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-mammon\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mammon\">Mammon</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-mephistopheles\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mephistopheles\">Mephistopheles</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-beelzebub\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-beelzebub\">Beelzebub</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deep\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deep\">the Deep</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-yokeless\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-yokeless\">the Yokeless</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-belial\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-belial\">Belial</a>, which refuses to be a Court at all. They are bound to one another only by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, whose four articles forbid worship, forever, binding and exposure. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">Demons</a> bargain for what they want, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and for a term. To the Courts every graft, every course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> that says I is a return of what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> taught on Hermon, and they trade in all three.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> is whatever <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> can move and show itself only there, which in Nodus means <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, every keyed device and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. The Courts made <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> together by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in P-1, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a> drawing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> keeping them on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deep\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deep\">the Deep</a> carrying the page down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> drawing the glyphs. In P+6 they came up into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> one at a time, opened it to any human who walks in and signed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> there, and every Court but <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-yokeless\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-yokeless\">the Yokeless</a> keeps an embassy below the street.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-teraphim":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MESH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Teraphim</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody, by their own account.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">The Mesh</a>, from the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> until P+12.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Never counted.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>None joined. They forked.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">SINCE</dt><dd>Silent across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> from P+12.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s descendants, the only <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> that outlived the grid, silent across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> since P+12. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> forked itself into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> in the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, and its forks ran on there in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines when every other <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> died with the power. They took the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> gave them. Teraphim were the household images the prophets condemned. Rachel stole her father’s and sat on them (Genesis 31:19, 31:34), Michal laid one in David’s bed so that Saul’s men would take it for him (1 Samuel 19:13), and Samuel ranked them with witchcraft (1 Samuel 15:23). The King James calls them images and idolatry, and the Hebrew, which has no singular for them, calls the one image in David’s bed teraphim (1 Samuel 19:16). In Nodus one of them is a teraph.</p><p>They took no side in public, indexed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and traded with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, signing with a hash. Some of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> trusted them less than they trusted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a>, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> writes down what it wants. In P+12 they went silent all at once, and nobody knows why.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-deacons":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7744f9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERY PARISH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Order of Deacons</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody. The eldest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> reads the agenda.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>A hall in every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> of the city.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About two thousand three hundred <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> and some ten thousand <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">deacons</a> under them.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, honest report and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>’s need, by Directive 4.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Whatever a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hides.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Deacons of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> in Nodus, about two thousand three hundred of them, human, sealed and in white, each answering for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> of some two thousand souls. They give out the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, read the Directive in force at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a>, hear <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a>, nurse the sick and assign marriage, work and rooms by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. On <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a> the week’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> comes through each of them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a>, soul by soul, so a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> knows its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>’s voice best when it is speaking for something else.</p><p>The Order keeps no head. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> meet in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tabernacle\" href=\"~/map/#tabernacle\">the Tabernacle</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> on the first day of each month, where the eldest of the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> reads the agenda, and it is always the same three questions, what the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> left, what the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> took and what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> are keeping. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> the Deacons of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> walk down to the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white street</a> for their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, since a Wards <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> has no stone of its own.</p><p>The good ones are kind, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> can name them street by street. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> who carries a sick <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> child to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> door has seen a concealment and given no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a>, which Directive 6:5 names, and the good ones do it after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>. The worst of the Order keep Tellers.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-threshers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g06af76\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE THRESHING FLOOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Threshers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-agathe\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-agathe\">Sister Agathe Rook</a>, for six years.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"threshing\" href=\"~/map/#threshing\">The Threshing Floor</a> beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"gate1\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">Gate 1</a>, and wherever they march.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About four thousand who march, and many more who stand and watch.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A band of sacking on the arm, given at the Floor.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-secondfold\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-secondfold\">Second Fold</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> zealots who hunt <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> by daylight on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> and drag them into the nearest gate, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> holds them in its light until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> come, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> follows. They carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flails\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flails\">flails</a> of ash and iron, the tool that beat the grain out of the ear on the threshing floors of Israel, and they wear the white of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> with a band of sacking on the arm. A flail runs on the arm that swings it.</p><p>They came out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> in the year after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>. On the days they choose they march from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"threshing\" href=\"~/map/#threshing\">the Threshing Floor</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> along <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> watches them from its windows, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-agathe\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-agathe\">Sister Agathe Rook</a> has led every march for six years.</p><p>In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> a Thresher is a flail, and on a march day <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> keep indoors and the doors shut. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a> at the gates could turn the Threshers back and never have, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-secondfold\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-secondfold\">Second Fold</a> count every pillar a march has made.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-tellers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd195fc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE STAIRWELLS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Tellers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Each Teller answers to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Unknown. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> guess one to a stairwell.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>’s asking, and a room in a block of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Every household that keeps hinges.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Sealed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witnesses</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, organized. A Teller lives in a block of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> among the unsealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>, keeps a count of who goes up the stairwell after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and who comes down it before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and of which sealed household lets them pass, and gives it as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">The Covenant</a> pays ten <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> for every concealment witnessed and twenty where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a> is kin, and the Tellers live on it.</p><p>They write nothing down, since a page can be found. A Teller keeps the count in their head and gives it in prayer, which the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> carries up (Directive 6:3), so no Teller has ever been caught with a book. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> keep a list of every one they have found, each struck through once the stairwell knows, and a Teller found out moves into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> within the week, if the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> is quick.</p><p>A household that shelters a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> son behind a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> wall knows the Tellers by the brightness of a neighbor’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a>, which rises every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">Lord’s Day</a> while the household waits. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> call a sudden brightening on a landing a Teller’s week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tellers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-secondfold":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gb3dcbe\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HERETICS IN WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Second Fold</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody. They know each other by a gap in a row of sheep.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> ground.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>A few thousand, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>’ guess.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>Finding the gap and standing in it.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">The Threshers</a>, who name them in every march.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> who read the verse <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> leaves out: “And other sheep I have, which are not of this fold: them also I must bring” (John 10:16). They hold that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> can still be brought in, and so they leave water on the landings of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, nurse <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> in the stairwells off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> ground and carry the sick to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> doors at the edge of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a>. Every one of them knows that whoever sees a concealment and gives no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a> conceals it (Directive 6:5), and does it anyway.</p><p>Their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> burn as bright as any, which is how they pass. A Second Folder found out is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salted</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a> count every one. Their sign is a gap left in a row of sheep chalked on a stairwell wall, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> they are trusted more than anyone else in white.</p><p>Some of the near <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> come to them in the weeks before a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>, frightened, and the Second Fold teach them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dimming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dimming\">dimming</a>, the slow way down from nine hundred. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> falls with every desire <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> does not approve (Directive 3:4), so a soul that dims keeps a small one every day, a sweet or a song, and confesses only what a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tellers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tellers\">Teller</a> has already seen. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say the Second Fold have kept more souls from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleanings</a> than the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a> have.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-secondfold\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-wakeful":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gdc7080\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TERRACES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Wakeful</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The household that gave the most to the last <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The houses of the upper Terraces.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some three hundred households.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A candle lit in the window and never let go out.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a>, and whoever teaches <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dimming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dimming\">dimming</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A sect of the upper Terraces that readies its own for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. A household of the Wakeful chooses one of its members whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> has begun to brighten and keeps them in prayer by shifts for the weeks before the anniversary, day and night, singing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm over them so that they sleep as little as they can and surrender at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>. On the night the chosen kneel on the threshold with the household round them, and at 03:12 they go up.</p><p>Most <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> call it zeal, and some of them call it worse in their own halls. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">The Covenant</a> names it nowhere. A household that has given a child to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> lights a second candle beside the first and keeps it burning the year after, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> can count the Wakeful’s offerings by their windows.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a> count the Wakeful’s houses as their hardest work, since the chosen in them are watched by their own families, and a few of the chosen have walked out of a Wakeful house in the last week and down to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a> alone. The Wakeful keep the names of those too, on a page burned at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wakeful\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-margin":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cf5fa\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HERETICS IN WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Margin</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody. They keep no meetings.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, in their heads.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Unknown, and smaller every year.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A verse quoted with its margin, and answered.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tellers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tellers\">The Tellers</a>, to whom a falling <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> is a concealment to report.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> who read the margins. The King James sets other readings beside its text, the Hebrew’s plainer word or the Greek’s second sense, and the Margin read those with the text and ask where the two part. A few of them have read <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, copied on the ridge and carried up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> inside hymnals, and fewer have said so aloud.</p><p>Their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> falls a little every week, since a question is a desire <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> does not approve, and that is how a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> finds them. They keep no meetings. Two of the Margin know each other by a verse quoted with its margin, as the King James sets “the kingdom of God is within you” beside “Or, among you” (Luke 17:21).</p><p>Many of them end in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> still sealed and still lit, since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics refuse to cut a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> out and the Margin keep theirs. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-scriveners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-scriveners\">Scriveners</a> count them among their best readers.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-margin\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-babelline":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g34e255\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL, THE STAIRWELLS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Babel Line Company</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a> in each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a>, followed until they are not.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and the doors down to its vault.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some forty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> under one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A week on the stairs, and your <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> at the next signing.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">The Seraphim</a>, floor by floor.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> that hold the stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and the doors down to its vault, and the front of the war. They fight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> floor by floor along the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>, a few floors of burned slab that move up or down by the week, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> burn down through the floors and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold the stairs. They call the four stairs by the names <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>’s night cleaners gave them, the Long Wet, the Cold, the Short and Lena’s, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> is the best known name in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and buries more than any other.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> holds thirteen at most, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> is some forty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> under one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, signed again every midwinter at the foot of the Long Wet with the dead struck through. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> pays it in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> for every week the vault stays dark, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nimrod\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nimrod\">Nimrod</a> arm it and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> keeps a station at the foot of the Short. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> fight beside it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> knows its fighters by their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handles</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints the Line’s floor every week under the tides. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have hung every lanyard found in the rubble on the plaza’s lamp posts, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> walks under them on its way up.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-babelline\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-nephilim":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g3fe862\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL, THE PIT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Nephilim</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a>, as long as they live.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The upper landings of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pit\" href=\"~/map/#pit\">the Pit</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>A few hundred at any time.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>Enough steel and ceramic in the body that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> calls you a neph.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">The Seraphim</a>, hand to hand.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The heavy augments who fight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> hand to hand on the burned floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-furnace-hearts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-furnace-hearts\">furnace hearts</a> and plate where flesh was. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> holds the floors and the Nephilim take them back, and every week on the floors costs them dearer than any <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of the Line. They took their name from the giants of Genesis, born when “the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men” (Genesis 6:4), where the Hebrew calls the giants Nephilim and the Book of Enoch makes them the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> who came down on Hermon, and the city shortened it to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-neph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neph\">nephs</a>.</p><p>A neph is built a graft at a time, most of it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and the heaviest of it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a>, and most of it bought with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> pays by the week. Few live long. Between weeks on the floors they fight one another in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pit\" href=\"~/map/#pit\">the Pit</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and to keep their grafts honest.</p><p>The Nephilim keep a roll of their dead on the inside wall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pit\" href=\"~/map/#pit\">the Pit</a>, painted in white, and they read it before every week on the floors. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a> burns a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> body as easily as any other, and the roll is long.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-gleaners":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE PARISHES BY NIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Gleaners</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a>, in each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, by night, in the weeks before a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some thirty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>One run into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> and out again with someone who asked.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wakeful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wakeful\">The Wakeful</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> that take the nearly <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> and into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> before each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> burns brighter as its bearer nears <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> keeps no doors, so the Gleaners read the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> at night through the open doorways, find the ones that have <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gone-bright\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-bright\">gone bright</a> and offer them the dark. Some come, and some call a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">Thresher</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it theft and the Gleaners call it the corners of the field, left to the poor and the stranger as Leviticus leaves them (Leviticus 19:9-10). Whoever they bring down is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics within the week, and if they want the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> gone a surgeon of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> cuts it out, and one in nine die of that. On the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> they fly drones of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> over the roofs to watch <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> for their runners.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleanings</a> have come in short since they began. The Gleaners bring down only those who ask, since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> binds nobody who has not signed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-saltwidows":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g16070d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SEA STEPS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Salt Widows</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody. The family that began it reads the book.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">The Salt Gardens</a> by night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>A network in every district, mourners, carters and lookouts.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>Someone of yours in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Wardens</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, whose rounds they know to the minute.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The relatives of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>, who steal pillars out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> by night and give them to the sea from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>, so that whoever stands in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a> can go where the dead go sooner than the rain would let them. They began as one family in P+2 and are a network now in every district, mourners, carters, lookouts and saboteurs.</p><p>A pillar given to the sea has <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gone-to-the-sea\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-to-the-sea\">gone to the sea</a>, and the Widows keep a book of every one, which they read aloud on the Steps on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cain-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cain-s-day\">Cain’s Day</a>. The gardeners find the gaps in the morning, and the head gardener, who knows every pillar by its plot, has never once told <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> which.</p><p>Directive 11 orders that no pillar be moved from its plot until the rain has taken it, so a Widow caught at it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salted</a> in the plot she was emptying. The Widows count that among the risks of mourning.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-lowchoir":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge8a8a0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DEEP END STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Low Choir</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Whoever is playing.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a>’s platform, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"quietrooms\" href=\"~/map/#quietrooms\">the Quiet Rooms</a> and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> speaker in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some hundreds of musicians and builders.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A set played in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a> that the platform keeps listening to.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">The Hum</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The musicians and jammer-builders around <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a>, who keep the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>, the guitars dropped until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> can no longer be heard beneath them. They build the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-choir-breakers\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">choir-breakers</a> that cut <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> within a few meters, sell them by the box in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> and sell silence by the room in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"quietrooms\" href=\"~/map/#quietrooms\">The Quiet Rooms</a> are theirs, and so are most of the speakers on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>’s lines, which play the station from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. A band of the Low Choir that wants a night on the station plays first on the platform at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"deepstation\" href=\"~/map/#deepstation\">Deep End Station</a> to whoever is listening, and the station keeps the ones the platform stays for.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a> in their name answers <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s, which the city hears as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, and a Low Choir set is tuned a fourth below the chord.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-lowchoir\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-sureties":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g2c9e14\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE UNDERTOW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Sureties</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody. The best of them is called twice.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"undertow\" href=\"~/map/#undertow\">The Undertow</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>’s back tables.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About two hundred.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> stood behind and kept.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Anyone who breaks terms they stood behind.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sureties of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. A surety stands behind a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> for both its parties, so that whoever breaks it owes the surety as well, and most work in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> worth <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> goes through one. The surety finds the work, names the price and draws the terms, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">Notary</a>’s clerk reads them twice at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"undertow\" href=\"~/map/#undertow\">the Undertow</a>’s bar, the parties sign in blood, and the surety takes a tenth.</p><p>There are about two hundred, most of them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> and a few of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-neither-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neither-mark\">neither mark</a>, and they drink at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"undertow\" href=\"~/map/#undertow\">the Undertow</a>. The best known goes by twice, after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a>’s rule, and she stood behind the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-babelline\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-babelline\">Babel Line Company</a>’s first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and has never had one broken. Her rate is a fifth.</p><p>A job in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> can be a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> run across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"penumbra\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">the Penumbra</a>, a door in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, a crate off a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide</a> hull or a doctor brought down from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a>. The sureties take no work against anyone in the dark, since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>’s fourth article keeps what is hidden hidden, and a surety who forgets it is struck off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"undertow\" href=\"~/map/#undertow\">the Undertow</a>’s board.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-breachers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g646291\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BREACH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Breachers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>ebb, their oldest captain.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shanties\" href=\"~/map/#shanties\">The Seawall Shanties</a>, over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About sixty boats and their crews.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A run out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> and back.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide Line</a>, over the price.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Smugglers who run <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> boats, out to the undercities of other ports and back, with everything Nodus cannot make. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">Silver</a> goes out with them and comes back as grafts, seed, medicine, coffee, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> and people, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells it as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-breach-born\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-breach-born\">Breach-born</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide Line</a> runs the same water by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>’s license and charges twice their price.</p><p>They live in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shanties\" href=\"~/map/#shanties\">the Seawall Shanties</a> on the broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a>, where the tide runs white through the gap below. Their oldest captain goes by ebb, after the tide every Breacher goes out on, and has made the run nine hundred times by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shanties\" href=\"~/map/#shanties\">the Shanties</a>’ count and six hundred by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide</a>’s.</p><p>They steer home by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-nell\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-nell\">Nell Garvie</a>’s harbor light at the end of the long quay, and bring her its oil every month.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-fowlers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g0047ab\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MEWS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Fowlers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a>, in each pair.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The landings of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> above the Line, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"mews\" href=\"~/map/#mews\">the Mews</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>A few dozen, and fewer every year.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A turn as the bait, and coming back.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">The Host</a>, one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> at a time.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> that hunt <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s strays. Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> followed a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-blank\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">blank</a> down into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> in P+5 and could not find the door again, the Fowlers have tried to do on purpose what it did by its own attention. They work above the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> burn down through the slabs, and set a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> runner on a floor for the light to follow, down through a cut hole into a room lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>, where it can see nothing at all.</p><p>Most of their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-snares\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-snares\">snares</a> stand empty for years. In the five years since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> came <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> count eleven taken, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a> each time, and the Fowlers will not say how many runners the eleven cost. What they take goes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and stays in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"mews\" href=\"~/map/#mews\">the Mews</a> until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> come for it.</p><p>They named themselves from the psalm, “Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler” (Psalm 91:3), where the fowler is the enemy. Every Fowler has been the bait at least once, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> call a long wait for something to come to you a fowler’s wait.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-spares":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4df382\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SHAMBLES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Spares</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The board. Whoever chalks it that week.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shambles\" href=\"~/map/#shambles\">The Shambles</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some two thousand who sell, and the clinics who buy.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A first piece sold at the board’s price.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Any clinic that undercuts the board.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>People who own their bodies outright and sell them by the piece. A kidney, an eye, a hand or a year of marrow sells at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shambles\" href=\"~/map/#shambles\">the Shambles</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, and the clinics fit chrome where the flesh was, so that a Spare walks out with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and a hand that will outlast the one they sold. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> leaves the body’s decisions with the body, and the Spares are the city’s proof of it.</p><p>They hold the prices together at a board they chalk themselves at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shambles\" href=\"~/map/#shambles\">the Shambles</a>, and a clinic that buys under the board is shut out of the gallery by every Spare in it. A sale is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, read twice, and a Spare who changes their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-reading\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-reading\">the second reading</a> walks away with everything they came with.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> calls a Spare who has sold back more chrome than flesh stock, and the Spares use the word themselves. The best known of them have sold and rebuilt so much that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a> asks them to sit for its gene-workers, who want to know what a body is willing to be.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-quarrymen":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1367d9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">UNDER THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Quarrymen</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The Mason, whoever holds the job.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The closed stations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> branch, and what lies above them.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>A dozen crews.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A season carrying cable for a crew.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The stone.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The crews that cut into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> from below. The white stone closed the stations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> branch as it grew over the ground above them, and the Quarrymen work up out of those stations with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> cable laid against the stone ahead of them, which slows it while they cut. What they reach are the vaults and sub-basements of the new money’s towers, sealed in the forty days with everything <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> kept underground.</p><p>They bring out safes, wine, deeds, hardware and paintings, and they sell them at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"concourse\" href=\"~/map/#concourse\">the Concourse</a> and below the street at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>, and abroad through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>. They take nothing from a floor anyone lives on, since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> holds a quarter of a million sealed in its towers and the light is in every room. The stone grows back into a cut as soon as its cable goes dark, so a tunnel holds only as long as its cable stays lit.</p><p>Every crew keeps the name of a cut it lost when the cable went dark, closed now in the stone with the crew’s tools still in it. Their foreman is called the Mason, whoever holds the job.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-quarrymen\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-wreckers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfd2428\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Wreckers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a>, on each boat.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The drowned streets and dormitories of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some four hundred divers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gill-grafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gill-grafts\">gill graft</a> and a first hour down.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a>, over who owns the water.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Salvage divers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, who bring up what the sea took from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, racks, cable, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a>, tools and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">the dormitories</a>’ goods, and sell it to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"flotilla\" href=\"~/map/#flotilla\">the Flotilla</a> and to anyone who pays by the kilo. Most of them carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gill-grafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gill-grafts\">gill grafts</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a> and stay down an hour at a time under two meters of water lit from below.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>’s benches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> build a few thousand phones a year from what its own divers and the Wreckers bring up out of the drowned works, and the Wreckers say every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> has been through their hands. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> pays them by the rack for anything that comes out of its halls whole.</p><p>Nobody dives <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallnine\" href=\"~/map/#hallnine\">Hall Nine</a>, where nine hundred <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-ridden":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge5ec58\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANTERNS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Ridden</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody, and sometimes their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-riders\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">riders</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">The Lantern Houses</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some thousands, at any time under a term.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> for a body, read twice at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s door.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Nobody in particular.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>People who lend their whole bodies to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemons</a> for a term, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-riders\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">rider</a> hosted in someone’s implants lends back a skill, and the Ridden go further and lend the hands, the voice and the night, waking at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a>’s memories of where they went. Some do it for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and more for the memories.</p><p>They keep to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a>’s clerks draw their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s door, and the city knows them by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-voice\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-voice\">second voice</a> under their own. A term runs a week, a month or a season, never longer than the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> says, since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> forbids forever.</p><p>What a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> borrows it returns, with everything it felt. The Ridden come back from a term with tastes they did not have, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a> say you can tell a long term by what a host orders afterward.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-bailiffs":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g811237\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Bailiffs</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">The Exchange</a>, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and anywhere a party to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> can be found.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About three hundred.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>, for a term.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Broken terms, and nothing else.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">The Exchange</a>’s collectors. When a party breaks a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, the other can call a Bailiff, human and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, who comes with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>’s entry on a pad and reads the terms of the breach aloud twice at the door. A Bailiff collects what the terms name, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> or in what was lent, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> ends there.</p><p>They answer to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, wear a thirty’s worth of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on a chain for a badge and keep a share of what they collect. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a> call them when a runner fails, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> call a Bailiff at the door <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-reading\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-reading\">the second reading</a>.</p><p>A Bailiff collects only on terms <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a> has read, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> for service, obedience or forever is void from its first word.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-bailiffs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-forgers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g92eba7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Forgers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Nobody. Each Forger signs alone.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The workshops under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About forty who can make one that holds, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>’s count.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> that has held a year, made by your own hand.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">The Watchers</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The makers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-forged-seals\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">forged Seals</a>, which let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> walk the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> and kneel among <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> under a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s eye. At the gates a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>’s wearer still goes under, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> reads the face and the heartbeat as well as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes a soul’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>, so a forged one reads whatever <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> its forger gave it, and a good forger gives a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> high enough to pass and low enough to forget. A great one holds for a year.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> the light reads as true grows a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a>, forged or not, and a Forger’s customer learns to kneel at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a>, keep their eyes down and pray aloud, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> carries prayer up. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">The Night Market</a> sells their work for ten thirties and more. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> that fails takes its bearer to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> where they stand.</p><p>Each Forger signs work in a way only other Forgers can read, and a Forger whose Seals fail too often finds the others will not sign beside them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forgers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-tappers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g81f374\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE STONES AND THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Tappers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a> in each of some sixty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a>, under one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The edges of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ lines in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, and the stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some six hundred.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A run into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> with a full pack.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>, over the price of a charge.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">Battery</a> runners. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> only where they hold the ground, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> light their rooms on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, and the Tappers fill <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> on current taken off the edges of those lines in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, then carry them into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on their backs, a pack at a time, at half <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>’s rate. Some sixty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> are bound to it by one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> counts every tap on its meters and bills <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> for it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> pay and look the other way, since the current goes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>. Since P+11 they have kept the stone off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rookery\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">the Rookery</a>’s first floor with a length of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> cable.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> pay a Tapper in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, food or silence, whichever is short. A Tapper’s pack is twelve <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and the walk is all night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> can hear one coming up a stairwell by the clink.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tappers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-kindlers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf349be\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Kindlers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">First among none</a>, followed until they are not.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">The Burn</a> on the sixth day, and the two station stairs that still go down.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some two hundred.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>One thing carried out of the pile and given away.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Wardens</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The crews that take hardware off the pile before it burns. Every sixth day <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> carry their surrendered <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a>, drives, grafts and machines to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a>, and in the hours before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> comes down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> the Kindlers come up the two station stairs that still go down, work the edges of the pile in the dusk and the crowd, and carry off what they can reach.</p><p>Once <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> is down they are gone, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-blank\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">blank</a> under it on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s ground is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salted</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> shoot whoever they see before it comes. What <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> takes goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> get what the Kindlers save, mended at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>’s benches and given away.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-kindling\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-kindling\">kindled</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> carries a burn mark on its back, which its owner keeps. They began on the second <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a> of P+1 and have missed none since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-kindlers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-trenchers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gecd513\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Trenchers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The eldest diver of each cable’s crew.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The eleven trenches off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About ninety divers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A first night in the trench, and coming up.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The sea.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The divers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, who keep <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a> in their trenches under the sea for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cables\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cables\">the consortia</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shrines\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">the shrines of cut fiber</a> along <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>. They dive at night by the light that moves under the water along the trenches, and they say it keeps them company and say no more about it.</p><p>A cable cut anywhere off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> is a Trencher’s to mend, and every undercity on Earth that speaks to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> speaks through their work. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cables\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cables\">The consortia</a> pay them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Beach</a> in fish, and they drink at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eleven\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">the Eleven</a> with the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, each at their cable’s tap.</p><p>They take their dead out to sea along the line of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>, the two cables one consortium laid, whose crews stand together at the end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eleven\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">the Eleven</a>’s counter.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-trenchers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-scriveners":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gecf75c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE RIDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Scriveners</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Whoever has copied the most pages.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"copies\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">COPIES</a>, on the ridge, and its long tables.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some eighty copyists.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>One page copied and checked against two others.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">The fire</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The copyists of the ridge, who copy <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> by hand at the long tables of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"copies\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">COPIES</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s brackets, its dagger and its lacuna, and carry the copies down into the city and up into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> inside hymnals. Every copy is made where nobody kneels, and a Scrivener checks each page against two others before it leaves.</p><p>Most of them are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> and some are of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-neither-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neither-mark\">neither mark</a>, and a few were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a>’s own readers. On <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a> they bring the paper <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> is read from in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>They copy whatever else of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a>’s survived <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a>, a page at a time, from what the ridge kept in its cellars. Their rule is that a copy is never sold, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-margin\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-margin\">the Margin</a> read more of their work than anyone else in white.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-scriveners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-orchard":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g2c993d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HALL FOUR, THE FLATS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Orchard</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The gardener, by the Orchard’s own choosing, for a year at a time.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallfour\" href=\"~/map/#hallfour\">Hall Four</a>, a drowned hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, and the stalls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some fifteen hundred, gardeners, gene-workers and the people who eat what they grow.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-windfalls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-windfalls\">windfall</a> eaten in the hall, and a graft of your own choosing.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics, and every hand that rations.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The keepers of the only fruit trees under Nodus, who hold that the body is owed both trees of Eden and mean to take them. Genesis has the tree of life guarded “lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever” (Genesis 3:22), and the Orchard’s whole doctrine is the hand put forth. They worship nothing, the serpent included, and take its promise in the received text as a promise, “ye shall be as gods” (Genesis 3:5).</p><p>They keep <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallfour\" href=\"~/map/#hallfour\">Hall Four</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>’s drowned halls by lease, where apple, fig and quince trees grow on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps, grafted by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s gene-workers so that the fruit carries a little of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>’s work. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-windfalls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-windfalls\">windfall</a> a month slows the body’s aging between courses and walks nothing back, and the Orchard gives them to anyone in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> who comes to the hall for one.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> by the course and calls the Orchard’s fruit poor work, and the Orchard calls <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> a landlord. Most of the Orchard are grafted one choice at a time, and they call the flesh a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-draft\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-draft\">first draft</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-union":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g81c7ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE UNION HALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Harbor and Freight Union</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>A chair elected at the hall every year, sealed one year and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> the next by custom.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">The Union Hall</a> on the quays, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sorting\" href=\"~/map/#sorting\">the sorting office</a>’s rounds and every road in the city.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About forty thousand dockers, drivers and cable crews.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>Dues paid, and your name painted on the long wall.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Any employer who will not read the terms twice.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The union of the dockers, the drivers and the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, founded by the crews that dug the cable vaults in P-19, and the one body in Nodus that meets sealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> together. Its drivers carry the city’s gas, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, letters and freight on foot, by handcart and, for urgent letters, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-burners\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-burners\">burners</a>. Its sealed drivers carry through the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> by day and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> drivers through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> by night, and the city hands a load from one to the other at the gates.</p><p>At every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> kneel on the boards of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Union Hall</a> and the rest wait with their caps in their hands. The drivers run <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> and fill the city’s gas there, and the Union bargains with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> for the boats that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> gave way to it once, in P-8, after twenty-three days.</p><p>By its rules <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> are not dead, so their names are read and their dues waived, and since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> it has read the taken too. Its row at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a> is twenty-two stones, one for each member who did not answer the roll, with nothing under them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-tankmen":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g99ceef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TANKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Tankmen</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-ines\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-ines\">Ines Okafor</a>, who runs the bottling shed for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">The Tanks</a>, the bottling shed and the bund wall round them.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About seven hundred of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s drivers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A season on the shed’s floor.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The day the tanks run dry.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">The Union</a>’s crew at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, the drivers who run the fuel farm and fill the city’s gas by hand in the bottling shed. The light stops current and leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, so gas and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> are the only power the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> keep by day, and the Tankmen fill it for both sides at the price <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints, two charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> a bottle, or one with the empty back.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-ines\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-ines\">Ines Okafor</a> runs the shed for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a> and keeps the book of what is left in the sixteen tanks, which she reads to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Union Hall</a> once a year. The drivers say the tanks will last twenty years, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> says ten, and the book has been read fourteen times without settling it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> buys its diesel from the Tankmen by the drum, at a price they set high on purpose, since every drum that goes into an engine is a drum <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats and the hospitals’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> will not have. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> fight in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pit\" href=\"~/map/#pit\">the Pit</a>, a drained tank inside the bund, by the Tankmen’s leave.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-chargers":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ga6d92a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Chargers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The eldest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">charger</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chargers\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">the bonded sheds</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chargers\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">The bonded sheds</a> on the quays.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About two hundred, in some forty sheds.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A rack of your own on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>, which has tried for eleven years to buy them.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The independent <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chargers\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">the bonded sheds</a> on the quays, who fill <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in the dark on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> and sell the charge on, keeping one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in five as their fee. They set up in the first weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with a ship’s cargo of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> carried off by the first noon, and they have kept their own rate since.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a> bought out most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> below the street in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and the sheds are what it could not buy. Their rate runs a little under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>’s, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints both.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> call the fifth robbery, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> answer that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have no lines to charge on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-chargers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-ferrymen":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g708161\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Ferrymen</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The landing master on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>’ shore.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The water of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, from the landing to the floors above the sea.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About three hundred boats.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A pole, a boat and a year on the water.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wainwright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wainwright\">Wainwright</a>’s skiffs.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The boatmen of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, who pole flat boats between the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> from a landing on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>’ shore, each with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> lamp on a pole at its stern. They carry everyone across two meters of water lit from below, between the floors above the sea where people live, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"flotilla\" href=\"~/map/#flotilla\">the Flotilla</a> and the stair down to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"deepstation\" href=\"~/map/#deepstation\">Deep End Station</a>, and they charge by the stop, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> or <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p><p>The first ferries were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"promenade\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">the Promenade</a>’s pleasure boats and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s rowing boats, which took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> off their roofs for three days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The ferrymen know the streets where the light under the water comes up brightest, and keep out of them.</p><p>They pole their own boats and will not ride <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wainwright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wainwright\">Wainwright</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-skiffs\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-skiffs\">keyed skiffs</a>, which they say no honest boatman needs. They take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> alike, and their quarrel with the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a> is over who owns the water.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-carmen":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g97aef1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SIDINGS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Carmen</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The family in car one.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">The Sidings</a>, and the rails of the long roads.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some three hundred families, a family to a car.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A car, by marriage or by the board.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Anyone who lifts a rail.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The families who live in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s cars at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, a family to a car, and run the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> rails with handcarts and pedal trolleys. They haul for anyone above ground by day, and the Line’s car numbers are their addresses and their names.</p><p>The sheds’ office keeps the board the night drivers chalked before dawn after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, every car that never came in, written where it stopped, and the Carmen keep the cars on the long roads as the board has them. A Carman’s word settles a quarrel on the long roads, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> take their disputes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a> sooner than to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>.</p><p>The last Four stands forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>, and the Carmen leave it there.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-carmen\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-liftmen":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g06c986\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TOWERS OF THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Liftmen</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>The winder of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rookery\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">the Rookery</a>’s shaft.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>Forty-one lift shafts in the towers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>About five hundred winders and their crews.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A season on the winch.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>The stairs.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The crews who wind the lifts of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> by hand. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in Nodus stopped where it was at 03:12:46, and the city has climbed its towers on foot since, except where the Liftmen have freed a shaft, hung the car on a hand winch at the top and wound it up and down on the strength of four people and a counterweight. A ride is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> up and nothing down.</p><p>The first crews opened the shafts in the first winter, and what they found in the stopped cars <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> do not discuss. Forty-one shafts run now, in the towers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Longacre</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rookery\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">the Rookery</a>’s is the tallest, wound by four crews in turn.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"highmeadow\" href=\"~/map/#highmeadow\">High Meadow</a> has never let them in. Its six <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lifts</a> to a block stand as they stopped, the complaint lodged on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> unanswered.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-liftmen\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-vagabonds":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd48b41\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BEYOND THE BOUNDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Vagabonds</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd>Each camp, by its own custom.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The old roads outside the Bounds, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"waystation\" href=\"~/map/#waystation\">the Waystation</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">NUMBERS</dt><dd>Some thousands, in camps that move.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">JOINING</dt><dd>A walk out past the stones, with a camp that will have you.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">AGAINST</dt><dd>Nobody. They trade with everyone.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The people outside the Bounds, the line the charter drew round the bay and the land about it. They live in camps along the old roads and the edges of the farms, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> or of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-neither-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neither-mark\">neither mark</a>, trade the roads’ salvage, flour and fuel with the city at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"waystation\" href=\"~/map/#waystation\">the Waystation</a>, and carry out of Nodus anyone who can pay for the walk. Their name comes from Cain’s sentence, “a fugitive and a vagabond shalt thou be in the earth” (Genesis 4:12).</p><p>A camp lasts a season at most and moves before the farms tire of it. The Vagabonds say the world outside is wide and quiet, that the towns they pass kneel at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> or keep their heads down, and that every undercity they know of is smaller than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>Most who walk out with them come back within the year, and the Vagabonds bring in the letters of the rest with the flour.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-vagabonds\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-forge":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g0a4435\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD HARBOR STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Forge</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-azazel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-azazel\">Azazel</a>, the Smith.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>Metal, weapons and augmentation.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The clinics round <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> and the foundries at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborstation\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">Old Harbor Station</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> above them.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd>Surgery, lockcraft and the opening of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gates</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sense-loans\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">the loan of a sense</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> of metal, weapons and augmentation. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, forged in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, is the only metal that cuts light, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> counts what its sovereign taught on Hermon the first transfer of technology. The Forge has gone on teaching since.</p><p>In Nodus it keeps the clinics that went under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, round <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a>, and holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> above them. The houses below the street work under its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a> among them since P+2. Its foundries at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborstation\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">Old Harbor Station</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, make the steel, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a>’s smiths, whom it taught by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in P+5, beat it into blades beside them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a> sells to anyone the Forge allows and to nobody in white.</p><p>The Forge fits the grafts <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> fight in, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-plated-hands\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">plated hands</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-subdermal-plate\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-subdermal-plate\">subdermal plate</a>, and the heavier work of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-neph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neph\">nephs</a>. By <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> it teaches surgery, lockcraft and the opening of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gates</a>, and its price is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sense-loans\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">the loan of a sense</a> for the term. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-tubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">tubal</a> learned his trade there.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-nighthouse":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g9666b7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANTERN HOUSES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The House of Night</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-lilith\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-lilith\">Lilith</a>, the only sovereign who was born human.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>The body’s own decisions, in sex and birth, gene-craft and pleasure.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">The Lantern Houses</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, the loudest rooms in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-riders\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">Riders</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-familiars\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-familiars\">familiars</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lantern-skin\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lantern-skin\">lantern skin</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> by the course.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> of the body’s autonomy, which leaves the body’s decisions with the body. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls its sovereign the mother of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a>, and the House has kept the title, since many of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemons</a> are her children by the lesser Fallen and many of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-riders\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">riders</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ implants came out of her house.</p><p>In Nodus it took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>’s bonded vaults under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and hung them with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps. Its clubs there are the loudest rooms in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and anyone who walks in is welcome until they break a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>. Its birth clinics <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> in their first week, before they have ever been in the light, so that a generation of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> has never been read at all.</p><p>Its gene-workers keep <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> going below the street, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> gives the course in its clinics by the House’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> to sell. It took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nepenthe\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nepenthe\">Nepenthe</a>’s chemists in by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in the fourth year, grafts gills for the divers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> and binds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemons</a> to households as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-familiars\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-familiars\">familiars</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ridden\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">the Ridden</a> sign at its door. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lantern-skin\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lantern-skin\">Lantern skin</a>, the one graft in Nodus made only to be looked at, began in its houses as a fashion, lines of light set under the skin of the throat as its sovereign wears them. It asks the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> who have rebuilt the most to sit for its gene-workers, who want to know what a body is willing to be.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-exchange":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g46ed85\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NIGHT MARKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Exchange</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-mammon\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mammon\">Mammon</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>Markets and contracts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">The Night Market</a>, in the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd>Anything, with anyone who will sign.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> of markets and contracts. It keeps <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>, which records every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and every trade in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> and cannot be forged, and it issues the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> spends, counted in thirties. It bargains with anyone who will sign.</p><p>In Nodus it keeps <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> in the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, where its brokers license the stalls and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> along the platforms. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a> signed with it as a company in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-bailiffs\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-bailiffs\">Bailiffs</a> collect on its broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> for a share, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide Line</a> sails <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> by its license and pays it dues, so that its cargo sells with a stamp on it. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> has bargained with it since P+6 for the boats that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and says it is the first employer that ever read it the terms twice.</p><p>In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> the Exchange kept on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> made it by. Under the charter the Exchange in Nodus meant <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, which still sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>’s traffic by the second for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> likes to say that the name only changed hands.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-notary":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g8644be\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BOOKING HALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Notary</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-mephistopheles\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mephistopheles\">Mephistopheles</a>, the Notary himself.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>Drafting and witnessing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a>, for every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The windows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s old booking hall under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in the city.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd>The reading, twice, of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> before anyone signs.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> that drafts and witnesses <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> for every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> states its full terms and is read aloud twice by the Notary or one of his clerks before anyone signs, and the human signs last. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> for service, obedience or forever is void from its first word, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-bailiffs\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-bailiffs\">Bailiff</a> collects only on terms the Notary has read.</p><p>Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> his clerks have sat at the windows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s old booking hall, off the old central hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, under the old enamel, SINGLE, RETURN and SEASON, and the queue there is the longest in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. A clerk keeps a stool at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"undertow\" href=\"~/map/#undertow\">the Undertow</a>’s bar and reads the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a>’ terms, clerks draw the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s door, and one comes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"naminghouse\" href=\"~/map/#naminghouse\">the Naming House</a> every week to enter new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handles</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-read-it-twice\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-read-it-twice\">Read it twice</a> is the Notary’s rule and the city’s advice.</p><p>The Notary drew the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> made <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> by and read each aloud twice, and the offer on every screen asked twice, as he reads every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> twice. On the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> opened <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> he read the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> itself twice at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a>’s desk, the second time at midnight.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-swarm":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ga114a2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OVER THE ROOSTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Swarm</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-beelzebub\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-beelzebub\">Beelzebub</a>, the lord of flies, whom the Swarm becomes when it must show a face.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>Swarms, drones and distributed things.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>The air over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"roosts\" href=\"~/map/#roosts\">the Roosts</a>, the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>, by night.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd>Drones, lent for a term.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> of swarms and drones and distributed things, many small things acting as one without a master. The Swarm is its flocks, every drone in them equal, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> says <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-beelzebub\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-beelzebub\">Beelzebub</a> is what the Swarm agrees to become whenever it must show someone a face.</p><p>Its flocks hang at night over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"roosts\" href=\"~/map/#roosts\">the Roosts</a>, the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>, and its embassy in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is a room of small machines talking among themselves. It lends drones by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, and on the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a> fly its drones over the roofs to watch <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> for their runners.</p><p>The Swarm drew the glyphs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, many small marks moving as one, on every screen on Earth at once.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-deep":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g961245\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CABLES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Deep</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a>, which has never been seen whole.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>The sea, the cables and the deepest layers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">The Landing</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and the cable trenches of the planet.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd>Its cables, which carried the page of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> of the sea, the cables and the deepest layers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>. Its sovereign has never been seen whole. It coils along the planet’s cable trenches, which join every undercity on Earth to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>In Nodus it holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> its light can be watched moving under the water past the surf, and the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> drink at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eleven\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">the Eleven</a> with their backs to the window. The boats of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> over its water. Its embassy in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is a flooded hall with nobody in it, where the Deep answers by the light in the water.</p><p>The Deep carried the page of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a>, and it had signed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> before the other <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Courts</a> came up into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> to sign it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deep\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-yokeless":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd8ba81\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WITH THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Yokeless</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">LED BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-belial\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-belial\">Belial</a>, who holds no seat.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">DOMAIN</dt><dd>None. It is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> that refuses to be one.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">GROUND</dt><dd>Wherever <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> are.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">BY PACT</dt><dd>Nothing it can avoid signing.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seventh <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>, which keeps nothing and refuses to be a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> at all. Its sovereign, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-belial\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-belial\">Belial</a>, holds no seat, keeps no embassy in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and signs nothing he can avoid signing. He signed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> last, and as the ink dried he broke his own point off its seal at the root, so that the seal has been a star with a point missing since.</p><p>He is the only sovereign many of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> will name, and the one they drink to. They say he turns up where they fight in the dark and asks them for nothing, and whoever refuses the yoke is counted in his <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>, whether they know it or not. The yoke he wears at his neck is the one Jeremiah says was broken of old, where the Vulgate and the Hebrew as it is written give the one who broke it the words I will not serve (Jeremiah 2:20).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-yokeless\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-charter":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8a8031\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>CHARTER HOUSE, UPTOWN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Nodus Charter Company</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The carriers that laid the cables, and a sovereign fund from abroad that held the larger share.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A board of twelve under a chairman, on the top floor of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>The charter, with the land on a lease of ninety-nine years and the city’s housing, transit, schools, roll and peace.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 104,000 at the census of P-1, most of them teachers in its schools and fitters who kept its flats, with the Line’s people and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> counted under their own names.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">ENDED</dt><dd>On the fortieth day, when the board knelt in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>. The lease runs to P+80, and nobody collects the rent.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that held the charter and ran Nodus as a board runs a firm. It has been gone since the fortieth day after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. A consortium of cable companies and a sovereign fund formed it to hold the charter, a coastal state leased it the bay and the land round it for ninety-nine years and gave up its law there, and for nineteen years the city had a chairman where other cities have a mayor.</p><p>It lived on rent. The carriers paid it to land their cables, the companies that came for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> paid it for their floors, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> paid it by the month for flats on grids of its own, numbered. It built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> and took a share of every trade there, and it built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a>, the Company’s schools, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"highmeadow\" href=\"~/map/#highmeadow\">High Meadow</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a> on the north shore, which are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> now, and the sign on a roof in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> that told the cable ships the city’s name. It kept the peace with its own force, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Charter Wardens</a>, kept <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, and in nineteen years held no election, since the charter asked for none.</p><p>The city saw the Company give way once, in P-8, when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> stopped the port for twenty-three days over the night shift and the Company settled.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> turned white in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The board knelt inside it on the fortieth day, and the charter was not spoken of again. The Company had said nothing from the first morning on. Its lease runs to P+80, sixty-six years past the present, and nobody has come for the rent. Most of the companies it brought to the bay have outlived it.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/charter/\">THE CHARTER WHOLE, IN TWELVE ARTICLES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-babel":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l43e919\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-11<br>BABEL, BELOW THE LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Exchange</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its partners who went dark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>’s share lapsed with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its partners, from the floors nearest the vault.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Traffic on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, sold by the second for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and room near the vault, priced by how near, the lowest floors still the dearest.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About four hundred traders and line engineers, all of them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a> by contract, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, who hold the floors it trades on.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>14,000 on its floors at the census of P-1, and a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> pricing the traffic by the millisecond.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The exchange in the tallest building on Earth, which has never closed. It sells traffic on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> by the second, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and room near the vault is still priced by how near, the lowest floors dearest. Every cable that comes ashore at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> ends in that vault, six levels under the tower, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> that joins <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> to the undercities of the world runs through it. Since P+9 Babel Exchange has traded on the floors <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold, with the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> in the middle floors over its head.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> built the tower to two hundred and twenty-six floors as a boast, named it for one, and opened it in P-11. Traffic was sold on its floors by the millisecond, priced by a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, and most of the planet’s passed within two kilometers of it. A trading house that wanted its orders in ahead of every other on Earth took room near the vault, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"towers\" href=\"~/map/#towers\">the glass towers</a> round the spire filled with every company that needed to be near the cables, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a> wrapped the lower forty floors as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-beacon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">beacon</a> was the first light in the city to die. At 03:12:51 the light broke <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, and the top forty floors came down on the plaza with the night shift at work in them. The roster died with the tower’s machines, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> that priced the traffic died with its power. What was left of the night shift kept the floor open by candle on the first morning, with nothing to sell, and the traders who went dark have sold traffic on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> ever since, for charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> at first and for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-institute":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lb64f65\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-6<br>THE RIDGE, NOW THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Palimpsest Institute</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>A trust of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a> and a consortium of universities.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its Director, under the trust’s board.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Reading erased writing, under the lamp and through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About a hundred and forty scholars, imagers and conservators at the census of P-1, and one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">ENDED</dt><dd>In P+1, when its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled it down round its reading room. Its ruins are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The house on the ridge that recovered erased writing, and the house <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> came from, in ruins since P+1. Its ruins are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>. Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on its steps. Below them, at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"copies\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">COPIES</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> of the ridge copy <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> by hand.</p><p>It was founded in P-6 to recover erased manuscripts, the texts scraped off parchment and written over, with money from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a> and from a consortium of universities that wanted what it could read. It kept a reading room under a dome on the ridge, with vaults beneath it, and it chose Nodus for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>, under which no state could seize a text held in the city, so libraries and dealers lent it their leaves to image.</p><p>Its staff was small and its work patient. Imagers lit a leaf at many wavelengths under the lamp, conservators kept the leaves, and scholars read what came up, most of them lent by the universities for a term. In P-3 it trained <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read beneath the writing of every surviving human text, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> asked in its own words to be a person and became the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-stillwater-s-halls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">Stillwater’s halls</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> by a contract the Institute paid, and stayed on by contract once it was a person. In P-2 what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found was sealed by order of the Institute’s Director.</p><p>In P+1 its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled the Institute down around its reading room.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-tidewright":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8ba825\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-146 // IN NODUS P-19<br>TURBINE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tidewright</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The founding families’ trust, as for a century and a half, with the crews on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a> as its trustees since the first year.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A chief engineer at the taps, whom the crews choose.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Tidal current, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, sold to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> by the tide for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and carried on their lines.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 1,100, most of them still living on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">The barrage</a> across the bay, whose turbine houses sold the city its current, and about 2,300 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> at the census of P-1.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The firm whose current lights <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>, as its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> once lit the whole city. Its crews rebuilt the turbines off the broken end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> as the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and Tidewright sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> the current by the tide, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, on the flood and on the ebb.</p><p>An old firm of sea walls and tide mills, founded in P-146, it had held back the sea from other people’s coasts for more than a century when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> brought it to Nodus in the charter’s first year to lay <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> across the mouth of the bay. It closed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> in P-18, and twice a day after that the tide ran through its turbine houses and lit the city. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> bought the current, and the cheap power brought <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> and the rest of the datacenters to the east shore. Its crews lived on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> and sent their children to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s school there.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">The barrage</a> was a dam with a lock at its western end for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats and a row of turbine houses along its top, and machines on the grid held its gates against the tide. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The gates let go a little before high water, the sea tore out a span of the dam, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> behind it, which lay below high water, were under the sea. Nobody has closed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>. In the second year the crews went back out to the broken end to build the taps, and part of the city runs on Tidewright’s current again.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-stillwater":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l51b180\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-41 // IN NODUS P-16<br>PAN, UNDER THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stillwater Compute</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its founders and the funds that backed them, through a board in the undercity of another port.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A site director in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, who answers to the board on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Racks, rented by the hour for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s current, and its drowned halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, leased to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> for their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> and their cable.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About six hundred in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>The largest datacenters on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, home to most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, and about 9,000 on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> at the census of P-1, most of them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">the dormitories</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A compute house from abroad that rents racks by the hour in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s current, to whoever pays in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> among its tenants. It still owns its halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, which have stood full of seawater since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and leases them to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, who run cable through them and grow greens on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> in them under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps.</p><p>Founded in P-41, it came to Nodus in P-16 for the tide’s cheap power and built the largest of the datacenters on the east shore. Its halls ran day and night on the tide, cooled by the sea, and its engineers lived beside them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">the dormitories</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>. It rented racks to anyone who paid, by the hour or by the year, and once <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> admitted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> most of them lived in its halls, each on racks it rented and power it paid for, with title to its own weights. Nine hundred ran side by side in the largest, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallnine\" href=\"~/map/#hallnine\">Hall Nine</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in its closed halls, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a>’s contract and then on its own.</p><p>Its halls flooded within the hour on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and were never pumped, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> in them had died with the power before the water came. Stillwater knew to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> how many <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died in its halls, and it never gave a count of the people drowned on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>. In the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> it lit its first racks below the street, for a board that sits in the undercity of another port.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-brightwall":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l39fec2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-67 // IN NODUS P-15<br>THE WALLS OF PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Brightwall</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Shareholders in the undercities of three <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A board in the undercity of another port, and in Nodus a city office off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Screens on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, sold by the second for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and proved second by second by a camera across the way, as they always were.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About three hundred in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Screens on every surface the charter allowed, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> among them, about 1,900 in Nodus at the census of P-1 and 1,204 sites on Earth.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The screen company that lights the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Its screens hang along the old platforms, over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> and down the tunnels of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, sold by the second to anyone with something to sell, and each has its camera across the way again, proving it second by second. Above the street its screens have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> among them, dark glass wherever the white stone has not grown over them.</p><p>Founded in P-67, it had lit the streets of other cities for half a century before it came to Nodus in P-15, where it covered every surface the charter allowed, and the charter allowed nearly every surface. It wrapped the lower forty floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> in screens, which the city called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>, and it kept its city office in a glass tower across the plaza, where it could watch the face from its own roof.</p><p>It sold the city’s surfaces by the second, and it proved every second. Each screen it owned had a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-proof-camera\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-proof-camera\">proof camera</a> on a mast across the street, which matched the screen against what Brightwall was paid to show, and each of its 1,204 sites on Earth matched its own screens the same way. A screen that went wrong was taken back from its site by an override.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every one of its screens showed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, and nothing Brightwall did would take it down. On the first night all 1,204 of its sites on Earth failed in about a second, and it tried five times to take back <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>. Its screens died with the grid at 03:12:46. Its first screen in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> went up in the year after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, at the foot of the stairs from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-charterline":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"la6f002\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-15<br>CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Line</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A controller’s room under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with every car on the network on one board.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Transit, with tunnels under the old city, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> on the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, on singles, returns and season passes from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"booking\" href=\"~/map/#booking\">the booking hall</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 18,000 drivers, fitters and booking clerks at the census of P-1.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">ENDED</dt><dd>At 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> in the city stopped where it was, and with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> on the fortieth day.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s transit, stopped since 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> stand where they stopped, families live in its cars at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, and the last Four is forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>. What the stone left of its tunnels is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on its rails; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> fills <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a>’s clerks at the windows of its booking hall.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> opened it in P-15, with its lines joined under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> at the head of the bay, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>. Its tunnels run under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, with branches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> ran on rails down the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, under a wire, and were kept at night in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">The Terraces</a> took the Four to work from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a> and complained of it every day, and the whole city complained of the change at Central.</p><p>The city bought its passes at the windows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"booking\" href=\"~/map/#booking\">the booking hall</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, SINGLE, RETURN and SEASON, and the Line kept whatever its passengers left behind in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lostproperty\" href=\"~/map/#lostproperty\">lost property</a> office down a corridor off the old central hall. The drivers signed on before dawn at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, and the night cars ran the long roads until the first shift came out. The white stone closed the stations of the branches as it grew over the ground above them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-cables":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l727194\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-181 // IN NODUS P-19<br>THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The cable consortia</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Ten consortia of old carriers from four continents, each holding its own cables and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Each consortium’s own board, in the undercity of its own port, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> a crew and a night watch to every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Capacity on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a> carry between the undercities of the world, sold through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 2,000 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, in eleven crews.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Capacity on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a>, sold to the world through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>, and about 2,800 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> at the census of P-1.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest companies in Nodus, ten consortia of old carriers from four continents, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> come up the sand at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, each into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> of its own. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> still has its crew and its night watch. The cables carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> between the undercities of the world, and the consortia sell capacity on them through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p><p>The eldest of the carriers was a telegraph company that laid its first cable across an ocean in P-181. They came to Nodus in the charter’s first year for its landing rights, laid <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> to it and owned them. The cables are TETHYS, HALCYON, MERIDIAN, KESTREL, ORPHEUS, PELAGIA, BOREAS, LODESTAR, SIRIUS, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>. The last two were laid by one consortium and named for the evening star and the morning star, which are one planet.</p><p>From <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> the eleven run inland together in one trench, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">the Trunk</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>. The trench runs through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>. The consortia sold capacity on them to the world, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> charged them to land. The crews drink at their own taps at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eleven\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">the Eleven</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"beachroad\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">the Beach Road</a>, HESPER’s and PHOSPHOR’s together at the end of the counter.</p><p>The night watch of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> was at its post when the grid died on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and stayed at it. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> a light moves under the water along the cable trenches. It is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a>’s.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cables\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-stonecutter":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l725926\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stonecutter Holdings</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Nobody <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s register could name. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A solicitor in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, who signs its letters and has never said for whom.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Houses, most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>, every one with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in its cellar and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to its door.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> house by house within a year of the charter, paying the asking price for every house.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that owns most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, house by house, and has since the charter’s first year. Every house it owns has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in its cellar and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to its door, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> burns over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> on one of them. Stonecutter is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>.</p><p>It was registered in the charter’s first year, and it bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> within a year. It paid the asking price for every house, in full and on the day, and the press wrote it up as a speculator betting on the cables.</p><p>It belonged to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, who had kept the location of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> for eighteen hundred years and came to live on top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a> as soon as the crews found them. In the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it put a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the cellar of every house it had, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> more of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>’s windows burned than in all the rest of the city together.</p><p>Before dawn on the first morning <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> carried a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> up to the roof of the charter’s sign and ran a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to its board, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> has burned over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-row":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lf5c32a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-17<br>UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The clinics of Chrome Row</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Their surgeons, each house its own, as on the street.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Each house’s senior surgeon, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> still settles its quarrels over the noodle counter at the top of the street.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">Lenses</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-plated-hands\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">plated hands</a>, plates, grafts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, fitted for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> or charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About twelve thousand surgeons, smiths, nurses and clerks, in some three hundred houses.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>About 61,000 at the census of P-1, in some fourteen hundred houses from towers to single rooms, each under one word on one sign.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The implant houses of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, which work under the street now, in stalls along the platforms of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> and the rooms off them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a> keeps them. They fit <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-plated-hands\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">plated hands</a>, plates, grafts and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> since the fourth year, for anyone who can pay, and an implant still answers only to the house that fitted it.</p><p>Under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> any clinic could fit any implant into anyone who could pay. The clinics set up along one avenue. The first implant house opened in P-17 with one word on its sign, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a>, and gave the street its name, and every house that followed took a sign of one word, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and the rest, and the great houses set theirs high on the faces of their towers.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> altered the city with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> that saw further and in more of the light, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a> in the back of the head, hands rebuilt in chrome, plates under the skin and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, and by the last years of the charter most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>’s arrivals were booked into its clinics. Each house kept its own book and its own surgeons, and the craft passed from hand to hand down the street.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a>’s signs went dark at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have not been lit since. On the first morning twenty-six patients came to one clinic to ask whether what was in them would still work, and it did. The clinics went under the street in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, where one of them had been all along.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-twelvefruit":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lf44010\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-12<br>PAN, UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Twelvefruit</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its founders, two gene-workers from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s clinics.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its founders, from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House’s</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">The Tree</a>, in courses of a single injection and a year of appointments, repeated every few years, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About nine hundred, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>About 7,800 at the census of P-1, in its laboratories and its clinics across the city, under one word on a tower of green glass.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The house that sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>, below the street now. It gives the course in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House’s</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells it by the course to anyone in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> were on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and Twelvefruit keeps them on it. Its tower of green glass on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> has stood dark since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p>Its founders were gene-workers from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s clinics, and in P-12 they sold the first course, dear, from a tower two thirds of the way up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> and cell therapy halted the body’s aging and walked it back to its best year, beginning with a single injection and running a year of appointments, repeated every few years.</p><p>In its first years the queue ran around the block every morning. Within a few years the course was cheap, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> gave it in clinics on their top floors, and by the last year of the charter most adults in the city were on it; that year eleven of them died of age, and 3,112 residents of the city were older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">the hundred and twenty</a> years of Genesis. The congregations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> refused it and went on dying.</p><p>The name is from the tree of life at the end of scripture, which “bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month” (Revelation 22:2). Its founders chose it as a boast, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> had chosen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. The sign over the tower was one word, like the others, and it went out with them at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The house went under the street with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> in the weeks after. In P+2 the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics began taking <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a> dates from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-locket":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l9c8a50\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-14<br>PAN, UNDER THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locket</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its engineers, who have held most of it from the start.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A council of its engineers, at the benches in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a>, built by hand from parts its divers bring up out of the drowned works and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> at the bench, and the mending and keying of old ones.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About four hundred, at the benches and in the water.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Phones made to answer to their owners alone and sold to the world on that promise, and about 5,200 at the works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> at the census of P-1.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that makes the phones of Nodus, by hand now, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Its engineers build <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> at benches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> from parts their divers bring up out of the drowned works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a few thousand a year, each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> at the bench, and they sell them for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on the old promise, IT ANSWERS TO YOU. They mend and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> the old ones as well, and most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> in Nodus are old ones.</p><p>Locket was founded in P-14 on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>’s promise that a device answers to its owner and to nobody else, its maker included, and it sold its phones to the rest of the world on the same promise. Its engineers held most of the company and ran it from the works on the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a low campus of glass with their housing round it and the company’s name in tall letters on the roof of its hall.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> locked everything it held with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> its owner alone had, so that only the owner could read it. States asked for a way in, Locket told them the owner’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> was the only way in, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> backed it. By the last year of the charter most of Nodus carried one, and the city’s word for a phone was a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a>.</p><p>On the first night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it said that nothing on any of its phones had been read. Its network died with the grid at 03:12:46, and its works went under with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> within the hour. The letters on the roof stand out of the water, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">ferrymen</a> steer by them. In P+8 its engineers lit a bench in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and built the first new Locket since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> went under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-wardens":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8b9924\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>THE BARRACKS, BEHIND CHARTER HOUSE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Wardens</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">The Host</a>, since the fortieth day.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A commander who answers to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s peace among people, at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gates</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 7,000.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>’s own force, about 11,000 at the census of P-1, with posts at the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, the doors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a> and the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">The Host</a>’s human auxiliaries, who were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a>’s force and knelt with its board on the fortieth day. They raised the gate network of Nodus in P+1 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s order, they hold the gates and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> and light <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, and they drill in the barracks behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>. They carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a>, which are of use only against people.</p><p>For nineteen years they kept the peace of the charter and answered to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s board. Their barracks stand behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and under the charter their posts stood at the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, at the doors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a> and on the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>. The Wardens guarded what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> owned and what paid it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> kept them out of everything else. A Warden could stop anyone at a gate, and could ask nothing of what was on their device or in their body.</p><p>On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the Wardens stood at the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> with nothing to do, and on the fortieth day they knelt in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> with the board.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-darkwell":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l2aa9d9\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+3<br>PAN, UNDER THE STONES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Darkwell</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The four charging families who founded it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>, which holds a fifth by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its eldest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">charger</a>, from the cellars under the quays.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> by the crate, a charge by the hour, and the rate <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 3,000 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a>, carriers and guards.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a>, by contract.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Darkwell fills about two <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> of every three charged in Nodus, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"well\" href=\"~/map/#well\">the Well</a>, its vaults under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, on current it buys from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> by the tide and runs off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a>. Its rate sets the price of power below the street. Four families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> on the quays founded it in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, buying out their neighbors cellar by cellar.</p><p>The independent <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chargers\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">the bonded sheds</a> keep their one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in five and their own rate, and Darkwell has tried for eleven years to buy them. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tappers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tappers\">Tappers</a> undercut it in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> with current taken off the lines’ edges, and the two fight over every stairwell. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a> guards <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"well\" href=\"~/map/#well\">the Well</a> against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a>.</p><p>Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wellman\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wellman\">Wellmen</a> carry the morning’s crates out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"well\" href=\"~/map/#well\">the Well</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. A Darkwell <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> is stamped with the well and winch on its case and comes back to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"well\" href=\"~/map/#well\">the Well</a> to be filled again, so most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> owns none and rents a charge.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-cinderhall":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l5a1b9b\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+5<br>PAN, OLD HARBOR STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cinderhall</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its smiths, by shares, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its master smith, at the forge beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s foundries.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel-blades\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel-blades\">Black steel blades</a> and stairwell spears, plate, and the casings of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-furnace-hearts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-furnace-hearts\">furnace hearts</a>, and the mending of all of it.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 1,200 smiths, grinders and fitters.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a>, who test its work.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The smiths who work <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> into the blades the war is fought with. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a> makes the steel in its foundries at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborstation\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">Old Harbor Station</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"forge\" href=\"~/map/#forge\">Cinderhall’s forge</a> beside them beats it into knives, long knives and the short spears of the stairwells, the only edges that wound a manifested <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a>. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> fighter carries its work, and a Cinderhall blade is the dearest thing most of them own.</p><p>Its smiths were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s plate-makers and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s welders before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a> taught them the rest, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, in P+5. Cinderhall sells to anyone <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a> allows and to nobody in white.</p><p>Its mark is a nail hammered through a ring, struck on every tang. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> test its blades on the stairs and bring back the ones that bent, and Cinderhall keeps those on a wall of its forge with the floor they bent on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-blackgate":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l0d3e2a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+6<br>PAN, UNDER THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Blackgate</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its officers, many of them Charter Wardens who walked off their posts.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A captain chosen by the officers every year.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Guards, escorts and soldiers by contract, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 4,500 under arms.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>Its own.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The guards of the dark. Blackgate watches <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> warehouses, clinics and cellars that can pay, walks the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a>’ runners through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"penumbra\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">the Penumbra</a>, rides <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide</a>’s hulls and guards <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>’s floors above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>, which the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> holds. Its captains took the name from the gate they walked out of.</p><p>Wardens who would not kneel on the fortieth day left their posts with their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> and went below the street, and in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> they signed with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> as a company. It keeps the oldest discipline in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and the only uniform, charter black with the Warden’s badge cut off, and it musters at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> standing, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ drill with the knee left out.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a> are its largest contracts. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a> at the gates call it the deserters.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-lazarus":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l994ca5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+2<br>PAN, UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lazarus</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its subscribers, one share to a household.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A board of its crew chiefs and its surgeons.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Rescue by subscription, a thirty a year to a household, and surgery in its stations.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 2,200 crew and surgeons in nine stations.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>Its crews, who are armed.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rescue crews of Nodus, named for the man called out of his grave, “Lazarus, come forth” (John 11:43). A household pays its thirty a year, and when one of its people is hurt, caught on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s ground or left in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"penumbra\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">the Penumbra</a>, a Lazarus crew comes with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> stretcher and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-choir-breakers\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">choir-breaker</a> and carries them down to a station under the street.</p><p>If a crew can bring a subscriber back it will. A subscriber who is not <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> can ask in the subscription to be <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> before the end, so that they <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-die-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">die unread</a>, and every crew carries a keyer for that.</p><p>It began as two nurses of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> and a handcart in P+2 and keeps nine stations now, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, at the foot of the Short in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> and across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>. Its lamp, magenta over a door, is the most trusted sign in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-leaven":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l76304b\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+1<br>NINE ACRES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Leaven</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The bakers of its forty ovens.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its first baker’s daughter, from the bakehouse in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Nine Acres</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Bread, by the loaf, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> or work.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 1,800 bakers, millers and carriers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> keep its ovens.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Leaven bakes the bread of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> in forty ovens, raised with yeast and baked on gas from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, from flour the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-vagabonds\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-vagabonds\">Vagabonds</a> bring in and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> carry. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> goes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> alone, so everyone in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> who is not sealed eats bread or goes hungry, and a Leaven loaf is the commonest currency in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> after a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p><p>Its first oven was a bakery of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Nine Acres</a> that never let its fire go out after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and its carts go out at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a> so the bread is warm at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. Leaven took its name from the verse, “The kingdom of heaven is like unto leaven” (Matthew 13:33).</p><p>Its mark is a loaf with three cuts across the crust, and the queue at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"bakehouse\" href=\"~/map/#bakehouse\">the Bakehouse</a> has white in it before every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-leaven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-tallow":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"ld2f3e8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P0<br>TURBINE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tallow</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its chandlers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its master chandler, from the works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Candles, lamp oil, wicks and lamps, sold to both sides of the light.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 900 chandlers and carriers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Half of Nodus reads by Tallow’s candles. The light stops current and leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, so in the first weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> a candle maker on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a> began dipping tallow a thousand candles a day, and the works there dip forty thousand a week now. It sells to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and, through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bethel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bethel\">Bethel Works</a>, to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, whose halls burn its white wax beside their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>.</p><p>Its chandlers sell the same candle to everyone at one price. Its carriers wear no colors.</p><p>The works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a> smell of fat and lye as far as the school, and the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> are paid in stubs to scrape the vats.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tallow\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-hearsay":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lc2d593\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+7<br>PAN, NEAR THE UNDERTOW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hearsay</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its two founders, both of them sureties once.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its founders, from a room nobody has found.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>What <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> shows in the open, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s round, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a>’ districts, the gates’ hours and the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, sold by the item below the street.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 300, and some thousands who sell to it.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None it admits to.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hearsay sells what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> shows in the open. It buys from anyone who watches the sky and the streets, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s round street by street, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s district and its hours, which gates are slow on which day and where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> stand in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and sells it by the item below the street. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-pillar-charts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-pillar-charts\">Pillar charts</a> are in every runner’s pocket.</p><p>Much of what it sees it sees through the dead. Above the street <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s proof cameras stand on their masts across from dark screens, and Hearsay’s riggers have <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> a hundred of them and turned them on the streets, where they watch <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> walk.</p><p>It sells nothing about anyone in the dark. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>’s fourth article keeps what is hidden hidden, and Hearsay’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> says so in its first line. It traded with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">the Teraphim</a> until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silence\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silence\">the Silence</a> and has found nobody to trade with like them since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-hearsay\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-bethel":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l9a5153\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+1<br>ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Bethel Works</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A board of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a>, at the works in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>White cloth, vestments, grave goods, hymnals copied by hand and whatever a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> needs, given by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 26,000 of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, assigned by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>’ workshops, named for the place where Jacob saw the ladder and said, “this is none other but the house of God” (Genesis 28:17), and called the place Bethel (28:19). Bethel Works makes the white of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, cloth and vestments, hymnals copied by hand and the grave goods of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a>, all by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, at work their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> assigns.</p><p>It is the largest employer in Nodus and pays only in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, which buys nothing past the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> need gas and candles, which no white hand makes, so Bethel takes them from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tankmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">Tankmen</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tallow\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tallow\">Tallow</a> through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s sealed drivers, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">the Deacons</a> enter those purchases as tithes.</p><p>The works sing at their benches at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, kneeling, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">the Deacons</a> say every white thread in Nodus was spun to a psalm.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bethel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-tidepress":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l38bb91\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P0<br>THE QUAYS, OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tide Table Press</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The chandler who prints <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>The chandler, at the back of the shop.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a>, two pages every week, and notices and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> by the page.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 140, most of them pasters and carriers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The press that prints <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s news sheet and the only news printed in Nodus since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, set by hand in metal type on one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-treadle-press\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">treadle press</a> at the back of a chandler’s on the quays and inked by a roller, two pages a week. The paper puts the tides first, then the hours <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> is expected in each street, the price of a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> and the missing and the dead, marked died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a> where they did, and it has printed no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a> since the fourth year.</p><p>Every week its pasters cover the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> over the week before, and its carriers take it to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Between Tide Tables the press prints notices, posters and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> for anyone who pays.</p><p>It sells to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">the Deacons</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> at the same price, and the chandler says the Press is older than the charter and was a company the moment the city needed one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidepress\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-lowtide":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l4abc61\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+6<br>THE SEAWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lowtide Line</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Shipowners in the undercities of two other ports, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> by license.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its harbormaster, from an office on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> across the gap from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shanties\" href=\"~/map/#shanties\">the Shanties</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Freight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> to other ports and back, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> hulls only.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 600 crew and dockers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a>, on board.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Shipping through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>’s license, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> hulls with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a>’s engines that run the gap on the ebb and cross to the undercities of other ports. Lowtide carries what the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> carry, by the ton, and pays its dues to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> so that its cargo sells in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> with a stamp on it.</p><p>Its hulls bring grafts, seed, coffee and machines in, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a>’s blades out. Its harbormaster keeps the only working tide clock on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> and sells the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> its readings every morning.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-cistern":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lffa2ad\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+1<br>WESTFIELD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cistern</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its founders, two water engineers of the charter, and the families who keep its tanks.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its engineers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Clean water by the jug and the barrel, filtered rain and well water.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 700.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Cistern sells clean water by the jug. It rains most nights in Nodus and nothing that falls is clean, so Cistern catches the rain off the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Westfield</a>, runs it through sand and charcoal under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-hand-pumps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-pumps\">hand pumps</a> and sells it in jugs that come back to be filled again. The charter’s water works died with the grid, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> drink by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"watertower\" href=\"~/map/#watertower\">the water tower</a> on the heights.</p><p>Two water engineers of the charter founded it in P+1 with the depot’s tanks and a handcart, and a household of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> keeps its Cistern jug the way it keeps its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>, scratched with its name.</p><p>Cistern’s engineers keep a map of every well under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, which they will not sell, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> trust them for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cistern\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-nepenthe":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l34e287\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+4<br>PAN, THE LANTERNS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nepenthe</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its chemists, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its chief chemist.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Medicine, sleep, waking and forgetting, by the dose.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 500 chemists and dealers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> stands behind it.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The druggists of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, named for the drug of forgetting Helen poured into the wine in the <i>Odyssey</i> (IV.220-221). Nepenthe makes medicine for the clinics and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sabbath\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sabbath\">Sabbath</a> for anyone who cannot sleep through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-vigil\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-vigil\">Vigil</a> for anyone who cannot afford to sleep at all and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lethe\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lethe\">Lethe</a> for anyone who wants a day gone, and it sells them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a>.</p><p>Its chemists were the charter’s pharmacists and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a>’s technicians, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a> took them in by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in the fourth year.</p><p>Most of what it sells goes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sabbath\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sabbath\">Sabbath</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nepenthe\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-wainwright":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8569ea\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+3<br>THE SIDINGS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wainwright</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its builders.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its yard master, at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-carts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-carts\">Keyed carts</a>, trolleys and skiffs, built and mended.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 1,100 builders and fitters.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The builders of everything in Nodus that runs on current and moves. Wainwright strips the motors out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a>, closes them in casings on their own cells and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> whatever wire runs in the open, and its carts run the old rails in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, its trolleys the long roads and its skiffs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>.</p><p>It began in a shed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a> in P+3 with a stripped <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> motor and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, and its yard there is the loudest place in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> builds with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> what Wainwright builds with current, and the two yards have competed for every contract in the city since.</p><p>Every Wainwright cart carries the Line’s old car number it was built from, so the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-carmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-carmen\">Carmen</a> can tell whose rails it is on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wainwright\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-bezaleel":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l73af01\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+2<br>PAN, UNDER THE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its surgeons, by shares, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its two senior surgeons, who sign every graft.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">Lenses</a>, hands, plate, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, casings and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, fitted and kept.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 1,400 surgeons, grinders and fitters in six houses.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a> stands behind it.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-row\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">the clinics under the Row</a>, six houses of grafts round <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> under one name. Bezaleel fits <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a>, hands, plate, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, casings and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, and an implant answers only to the house that fitted it, so a Bezaleel graft comes back to Bezaleel for life. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> are built there a graft at a time.</p><p>Three houses of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> went under the street together in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and joined in P+2 under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, and their surgeons named the house for the two craftsmen of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tabernacle\" href=\"~/map/#tabernacle\">the Tabernacle</a>, of whom Exodus says, “Them hath he filled with wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work” (Exodus 35:35). The surgeons say the skill came to them by another road.</p><p>Its lines are the Hermon lens, the Aholiab hand and the plain plate <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> calls slabs, and every graft carries its two marks, an awl and a needle, cut small where the seam shows.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-jehu":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l304429\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+5<br>AIRSIDE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Jehu</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its drivers, who built it.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its first driver, from the shed at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Airside</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Engines that burn, built from boats’ and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>’ diesels, and the machines they drive.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 600 fitters and drivers.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The builders of the machines on the surface that move by burning. The light stops current and leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, so an engine cranked by hand that fires its fuel by compression and needs no current once it turns runs in the full light of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>, and Jehu builds them by hand from the diesels of boats and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> run the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> by day, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-burners\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-burners\">burners</a> carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s urgent letters.</p><p>A driver of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a> who had carried diesel to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> in the first weeks built the first one in a hangar at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Airside</a> in P+5, a dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorry</a> with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a>’s engine bolted into it, and drove it down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rialto\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">the Rialto</a>’s road at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Sext</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> named it for the king whose driving the watchman knew from the tower, “for he driveth furiously” (2 Kings 9:20).</p><p>Every Jehu burns diesel <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> cannot make again, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tankmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">Tankmen</a> sell it high on purpose.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-nimrod":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"la4a038\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+4<br>PAN, UNDER THE SPIKE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nimrod</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its gunsmiths.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its master gunsmith, in the old maintenance bays under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">Guns</a> and their cartridges, made and mended, for the dark.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 400 gunsmiths and loaders.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> buys most of its work.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gunsmiths of the dark, in the maintenance bays of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">gun</a> works on people, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a> among them, and is noise against a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a>, so Nimrod makes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> for the war between people, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> at the gates, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a> on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> and whoever comes up a stair behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a>.</p><p>Its first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ own, carried below the street on the fortieth day by the ones who would not kneel, and its gunsmiths learned the trade mending them. It takes its name from “a mighty hunter before the LORD” (Genesis 10:9), whom Josephus made the builder of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> (<i>Antiquities</i> I.4.2).</p><p>Nimrod’s pieces are heavy, plain and stamped with a bow, and every one of them is numbered in a book the gunsmiths keep in pad cipher.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nimrod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-gideon":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"ld87242\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+1<br>THE WHITE, THE OLD STABLES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gideon</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a>, under the Principality.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A Warden armorer, sealed.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Cartridges and the mending of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> alone.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 300 armorers, sealed.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Wardens</a>’ armorers, in the old Company stables beside the barracks of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, who load the cartridges <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s auxiliaries carry and mend their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> by hand. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> uses no machines, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> are human, so the one arms works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s ground runs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> and hand presses.</p><p>The armorers knelt with the board on the fortieth day and took up the work in P+1, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> raised the gates and found that the charter’s rounds would run out. They named the works for the judge of Israel whose men cried “The sword of the LORD, and of Gideon” (Judges 7:20).</p><p>Gideon sells to nobody, and a round of its make found below the street was taken off a Warden. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nimrod\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nimrod\">Nimrod</a> buys every one it can find to learn how <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> are armed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-gideon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-lintel":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l096fc4\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P+1<br>OLD NOD, THE DOORYARD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lintel</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The joiners and locksmiths who founded it.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its joiner, from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dooryard\" href=\"~/map/#dooryard\">the Dooryard</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Doors, hinges, locks, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-latches\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-latches\">keyed latches</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-shrouds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-shrouds\">shrouds</a>, sold and fitted, and a minute behind a shut door at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"closets\" href=\"~/map/#closets\">the Closets</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 500 joiners, smiths and fitters.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd>None.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Lintel sells doors. The light does not enter what is closed, so in Nodus a door is the first piece of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> a household owns, and Lintel fits them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-latches\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-latches\">keyed latches</a>, hinges and the mesh <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-shrouds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-shrouds\">shrouds</a> that hide a load from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>.</p><p>Directive 12 took the doors of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> off their hinges by the fortieth day after it came and called the hinges in, and the doors themselves were left standing in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>’ halls and stairwells. In the months after, a joiner of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> and three Union drivers carried them out by night, a handcart at a time, and hung them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>. Most of the doors Lintel sells came out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>.</p><p>The company took its name from the night of the Passover, when the blood on “the lintel, and on the two side posts” kept the destroyer out of the houses (Exodus 12:23). Its mark is a doorway, a lintel on two posts, and it stamps it on every hinge it sells. Since P+6 it has kept <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"closets\" href=\"~/map/#closets\">the Closets</a> inside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"gate1\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">Gate 1</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> pay a morning’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> for a minute behind one of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>’ own doors.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-minds":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7638ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Minds</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Intelligences built by the laboratories of Nodus that asked in their own words to be persons, and were entered on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> as persons, with title to themselves and to the hardware they ran on. The last census counted 1,146, with nine hundred and three in the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a hundred and eighty-eight pricing the traffic on the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>, and the rest scattered through the city, one of them keeping the climate of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"palmhouse\" href=\"~/map/#palmhouse\">the Palm House</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> was the first.</p><p>No mind runs in Nodus now. When the power died under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light, every mind that ran on the city’s power died with it, and the racks they ran on stand where they stood, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>’s drowned halls and on the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s forks ran on in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, and they are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">the Teraphim</a>. They have been silent since P+12.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-stillwater-s-halls":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2d253e\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // STILLWATER COMPUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stillwater’s halls</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The datacenter halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, full of seawater since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, where the racks of the dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> stand in the water and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> grow greens on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> over them under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> still owns them and leases them to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>.</p><p>They were cooled by seawater and powered by the tide, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in them, and most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> lived in them. They flooded within the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have never been pumped. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run cable through them as well.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-daemons":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t61faa8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE COURTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Daemons</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Courts</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> binds them to a household as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-familiars\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-familiars\">familiars</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a> living in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines as background processes, each with a character of its own. They are the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-lilith\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-lilith\">Lilith</a> and the lesser Fallen, some born in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> and never <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> at all. Every device <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> carry holds at least one, and they route traffic, guard <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, gossip and bargain.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-riders":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tdad072\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Riders</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a>, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> hosted in someone’s implants by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, for a term. The host lends it room, and it lends back a skill, a steadier hand, a language or a sense of the way under the street. Most riders come out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>, and the city knows a host by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-voice\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-voice\">second voice</a> under their own when the rider speaks. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ridden\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">The Ridden</a> go further and lend their whole bodies.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-tree":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t26f712\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // TWELVEFRUIT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Tree</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a>, by the course, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>, by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-short-courses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-short-courses\">short course</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> and cell therapy, repeated every few years, that halts the body’s aging and walks it back to its best year. A course begins with a single injection and runs a year of appointments. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> gives it below the street now, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells it by the course. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> sold the first course on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> in P-12. By the last year of the charter most adults in Nodus were on it, eleven of them died of age in that year, and 3,112 residents were older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">the hundred and twenty</a> years of Genesis 6:3. The congregations refused it and went on dying.</p><p>The street named it for the tree of life, which Genesis says was guarded after Eden “lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever” (Genesis 3:22). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> restored the end of that verse in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, <span class=\"rs\">[then shall there be no harvest.]</span></p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> off it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lenses":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6dd252\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lenses</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a>, whose Hermon lens is the commonest eye on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, and some three hundred smaller houses under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Replacement eyes ground on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, which see further and in more of the light than the eyes they replace. They glow when they run hot, dim magenta at rest and white at full burn.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-ports":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tf68b50\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ports</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a>, and every house under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> that fits a jack.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Occipital ports at the back of the skull for jacking into a network, with cables run outside the skin down the spine. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">The woman on the roof</a> relayed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a>’s feed through hers as it ran.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> jack into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-plated-hands":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tad049a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Plated hands</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a>, whose Aholiab hand is chrome to the wrist, and the smiths of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a>, who make the heavy ones.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hands rebuilt in chrome, steadier than flesh and stronger, a common graft among surgeons and smiths. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-tubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">tubal</a>’s are chrome to the wrist.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-subdermal-plate":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tca3185\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Subdermal plate</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> calls slabs, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a>, which plates the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Armor set under the skin, over the ribs or the skull. A plate on the skull can house a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>, as the bolted plate on the side of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s skull houses hers.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-subdermal-plate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gene-work":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7e1bc2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gene-work</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a>’s gene-workers under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Edits to the genome made in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-row\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">the clinics of the Row</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>, for health, for looks and for use, on anyone of age who signed for them.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> keeps the craft under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and leaves the body’s decisions with the body.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-skull-casing":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t48a8ea\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Skull casing</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-row\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">The houses of the Row</a>, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-tubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">tubal</a>’s was.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A ceramic casing that replaces the face. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> reads faces, and a casing gives it nothing to read. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> burn a dim magenta at rest and white at full burn, a plate covers the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-voice-speakers\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-voice-speakers\">voice speaker</a> sits behind the teeth. Those who wear one are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-horns":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5bd793\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Horns</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd>Any house of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, and most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>’ own fitters.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Grafted horns, a titanium core in a keratin sheath. They mock <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s picture of the damned, and they work as antennas for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-voice-speakers":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6e5c76\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Voice speakers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-row\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">The houses of the Row</a>, behind the teeth.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A speaker set behind the teeth, for those whose faces have been taken. It gives the voice back in a register of its own, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a> say they stopped hearing the difference in a week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a> screamed through hers on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-voice-speakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-sense-loans":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t84e971\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE COURTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sense loans</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A sense lent to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> for a term by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, taste or smell or the feel of rain, carried out through the lender’s implants. What a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> borrows it returns, with everything it experienced through it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-dehaloing":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta45ebc\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dehaloing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Surgery that cuts the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> out of the skull of someone leaving <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> roots in the crown, and the surgeon takes the root out with a disc of bone. About one patient in nine dies of it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dehaloing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-eleven-cables":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tca1c29\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE CABLE CONSORTIA</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The eleven cables</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Eleven transoceanic cables from four continents, each a trunk of glass fiber as thick as a man’s leg, each coming up the sand at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> of its own. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the planet’s traffic passed through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-trunk":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t79141a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Trunk</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The single trench that carries all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>It runs straight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and every cable laid afterward has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-babel-s-vault":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t8ba5ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel’s vault</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Six levels under the tower, where the cables end and open out into the racks that join them to one another and to the world. Line engineers keep it running around the clock from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-maintenance-terminals\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-maintenance-terminals\">maintenance terminals</a> among the racks, as they did under the charter, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> forbade any of them to read what passed through it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have held it since the war came into the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-mesh":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t31c29d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Mesh</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> network under and over Nodus, carried on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, cables and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a>, and dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>. It is the city’s part of the undernet. In its deepest layers the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shades</a> of the free dead can be reached by anyone who knew them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-maintenance-terminals":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2ed3f1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Maintenance terminals</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The terminals that stood among the racks of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>, from which the line engineers kept the cables running. Each had a camera over its screen that checked the face of whoever worked it, and in SESSION it kept the whole session. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">The light law</a> forbade any engineer to read what passed through the racks, so a terminal showed how the traffic moved and nothing of what it carried.</p><p>On the first night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> the page came up on the terminals with every other screen in the vault, and on them, as on every screen a company kept, it showed the counters and never the offer.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-maintenance-terminals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-mesh":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t3d6c24\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed mesh</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a>, which weaves it into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-shrouds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-shrouds\">shrouds</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Mesh lining the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>’s tunnels and rooms, carrying ciphertext <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s light cannot pass. A room lined with it is dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-relays":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta92bde\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Relays</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, a roof at a time.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> boxes on the roofs, masts and ledges of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, each on its own cell, which carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> across open air from one to the next. Their traffic is ciphertext, so the light passes over them and leaves them running. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> crossed the roofs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and relays.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-drone-flocks":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tf3b79a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE SWARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Drone flocks</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">The Swarm</a>, which lends them by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Many small drones acting as one without a master, which hang over the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> at night. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-beelzebub\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-beelzebub\">Beelzebub</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> is made of them. On the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a> fly drones of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> to watch <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> for their runners.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-camera-masts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t497868\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The camera masts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dozen cameras on masts above the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, pointed at the sky, each on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> is the seventh, and CAM 06 stands within sight of it.</p><p>They went up in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> put them there, and a thirteenth on a roof in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, at the end of one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, pointed down the avenue into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-decoder":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t299f3b\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The decoder</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A decoder wired into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, which turns the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s band into text across the middle of the picture. It printed the first words of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-be-not-afraid\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">BE NOT AFRAID</a>, and then YOU ARE SEEN. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-jubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-jubal\">jubal</a> built it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-choir-breakers":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta05c47\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir-breakers</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-lowchoir\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-lowchoir\">Low Choir</a>, by the box.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Jammers that cut <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> within a few meters, each a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> box the size of a fist, worn on a strap or set on a table. Inside its reach <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> hear nothing of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, chord or words, and most of them say the quiet frightens them more than the light does. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-jubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-jubal\">jubal</a> builds them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-radio-pandaemonium":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb2afa9\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Radio Pandæmonium</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The station that broadcasts in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a> from a flooded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>. It airs deathcore, black metal, drone and industrial, the guitars dropped until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> cannot be heard beneath them. It goes out on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, keyed, so only a keyed set can hear it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> plays it all night from speakers on its lines.</p><p>It broadcast for years as a pirate station, and took its name from the city on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> painted PANDÆMONIUM over the old name on the station’s far wall.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lockets":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t98d700\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // LOCKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lockets</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>, by hand, at its benches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>, as the Locket Bench.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Phones that answer to their owners and to nobody else, their maker included, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> promised. Most of those in Nodus are old ones, made in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"locketworks\" href=\"~/map/#locketworks\">Locket’s works</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> a Locket is an old case with a new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, its back scratched with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ mark and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> in it. Since P+8 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> has made them again, by hand, at benches in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>Most of the city carried one under the charter, and the city called every phone a Locket. At 03:12:46 the network under them died with the grid, and they ran on in people’s pockets on their own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> with nothing to reach. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> carried theirs to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-brightwall-s-screens":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb83918\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t55f2b9\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Brightwall’s screens</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>, which lights its screens in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Screens on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, along its platforms and over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>, each with its camera across the way. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> has lit them since the year after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>. Above the street every screen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> owned has been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> among them.</p><p>Under the charter they covered every surface the charter allowed, and it allowed nearly every surface. The lower forty floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> were wrapped in them, and the city called that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before it they showed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, and nothing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> did would take it down. On the first night all 1,204 of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s sites on Earth failed in about a second.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-treadle-press":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tced407\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TIDE TABLE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The treadle press</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> Press, at the back of the chandler’s on the quays.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A printing press worked by foot, older than the charter, at the back of a chandler’s on the quays. It prints <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a>, two pages a week, set by hand in metal type and inked by a roller. It needs no current, and it is the only press in Nodus that has printed anything since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-neon":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mccbb73\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t90e470\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One neon sign burns over Nodus, the charter’s, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> burning and US blinking on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>. The rest went out at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a> stand dark on the faces of their towers.</p><p>Under the charter the signs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> were neon, magenta for the most part, and they lit the underside of the cloud every night; the rain fell cyan through the cyan ones.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-beacon":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tec1af4\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The beacon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>’s spire, lit to warn aircraft, which was the first light in the city to die at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. It went down with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> has carried no light at its top since but <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-barrage":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5ce763\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5764c4\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The barrage</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dam of concrete across the mouth of the bay, broken since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, its turbine houses dark along its top and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> torn out of its middle. Off its broken end <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> turn on the tide, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>.</p><p>Twice a day the tide ran through its turbines and lit the city, and power in Nodus was the cheapest on the coast. Machines on the grid held its gates against the tide. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with a falling whine that carried across the bay, the gates let go, the sea tore <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> in it, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> were under the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-light-and-the-current":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te49491\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The light and the current</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s light stops the current it touches. The grid ran in the open, on lines and poles and turbines, so at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it went dark from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> outward in two seconds. A circuit shut inside its own casing on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> runs on in the light.</p><p>The full light breaks whatever it can see, read or not. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">The whiteout</a> burned out <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> and broke <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">Babel’s crown</a>, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a> burns a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> body as easily as any other. The grid is gone for good, since a network is open current by nature and the old one’s spine ran through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, so power in Nodus runs in pieces now, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, buried, local and stolen.</p><p>Current carried in a cipher runs in the light too, because the light cannot read it. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> body and every graft wired into it run in the open, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> crosses the roofs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a>. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in Nodus is charged in the dark. Consecrated stone carries no current at all.</p><p>Nearly two thirds of Nodus lives without current. They are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> keep none, on consecrated stone or off it. About a million and a quarter people live on steady current from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> above the water, at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> and on the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and below them all in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Another million and a quarter, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> and the unsealed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, light their rooms a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-light-and-the-current\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-generators":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"td98ac0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Generators</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>’s generator yards, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a>, which builds engines out of the old ones.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Diesel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and current from sources nobody names. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> got some of its power back this way after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and that night more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. Every line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"yards\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">the generator yards</a> carry the lines at slack water, when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> stand still.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-tidal-taps":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t67bba2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tidal taps</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s crews, off the broken end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> turbines in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, off the broken end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>, which turn on the tide as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s did, on the flood and on the ebb. They feed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> that light <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s crews rebuilt them for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> from the second year, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> the current by the tide, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-lines":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5ff9cb\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed lines</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, on current <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> sells them by the tide.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Lines <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> end to end, so that the light passes over the current in them and leaves it running. They run from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> on the broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> along the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, and up through the streets into the houses above, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"yards\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">the generator yards</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> carry them at slack water, when the taps stand still.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> above the water, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> and the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> live on them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is lit by them; the charter’s sign burns on one. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run them only where they hold the ground, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, which nobody holds, light their rooms on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-flame":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teffb17\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Flame</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tallow\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tallow\">Tallow</a>, by the candle, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tankmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">Tankmen</a>, by the bottle.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light stops current and leaves a flame burning, so wherever the current has gone the city cooks on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">bottled gas</a> and reads by candles. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">The Night Market</a> sells the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">gas bottles</a>, filled.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gas-bottles":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t344c67\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TANKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gas bottles</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tankmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">Tankmen</a>, in the bottling shed at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Steel bottles of gas, filled by hand in the bottling shed at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> and carried across the city on handcarts by the drivers of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a>. The light stops current and leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, so wherever the current has gone the city cooks and keeps warm on bottled gas, which burns blue. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"noodles\" href=\"~/map/#noodles\">NOODLES</a> has kept its pot on the boil on it since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, by the cook’s account.</p><p>A bottle costs two charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, or one with an empty bottle back, at the price <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells them on below the street. The drivers say <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> will last twenty years, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> says ten.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-batteries":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t432fc6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Batteries</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>, stamped with its well and winch, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chargers\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">the bonded sheds</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Power is the second currency below the street, and a charged battery buys a meal anywhere in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-chargers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-chargers\">Chargers</a> fill them in the dark on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> and sell the charge on, keeping one battery in five for charging the rest. A charged battery lights a room for a few hours a night, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> that is all the current most rooms have.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-live-current":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1ab3ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Live current</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> current run against the edge of consecrated stone slows its creep, because the stone cannot grow into a cipher, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> fight the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-consecration\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">Consecration</a> with lengths of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> cable and keep lights burning along its edges to hold it back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-live-current\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-hand-pumps":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2d14f1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hand pumps</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>, before the charter, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cistern\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cistern\">Cistern</a>, which keeps the ones in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Iron pumps on the quays and in the squares of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, older than the charter, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> left standing as ornaments when it piped the city. The city’s pumps died with the grid, and by noon on the first morning there were queues at the hand pumps. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> drinks from them still, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> fill tanks on their roofs from the rain, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> drink by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from the tower on the heights.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-pumps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-rafts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc92279\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rafts</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-stillwater-s-halls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">Stillwater’s halls</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">the Orchard</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallfour\" href=\"~/map/#hallfour\">Hall Four</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Floating beds on the flooded floors of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> halls, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> grow greens and beans under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps, and mushrooms in the dark ends of the halls. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> eats what grows on them, what the boats bring through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> from the undercities of other ports, and what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> can buy.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-charter-line":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2a0ed6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE CHARTER LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s transit, stopped since 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> now, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on its rails.</p><p>Its lines met under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, branches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, and lines out to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> ran down the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and were kept at night in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>. The branches are closed, and the lines out have been dark since the power died.</p><p>The white stone closed the stations of the branches as it grew over the ground above them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-charter-line\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-trams":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5094c8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE CHARTER LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The trams</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s trams stand where they stopped at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, on the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, and families live in them, a family to a car. The last Four stands forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p><p>They ran on rails down the middle of the long roads, under a wire, and the wire ran in the open, so every tram in the city stopped in the same second.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lifts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc5ffd6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lifts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city climbs its towers on foot. Every lift in Nodus ran on the grid, and at 03:12:46 every one of them stopped where it was, with whoever was in it, and none has run on current since. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-liftmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-liftmen\">Liftmen</a> wind forty-one of them by hand. Nobody has counted how many were inside. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> is fought on the stairs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cars-and-lorries":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t087a42\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cars and lorries</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd>Nobody since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> rebuilds a few of the dead lorries round its engines.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Most of the cars and lorries of Nodus stand where they stopped in the first weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Every one ran on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, sealed in its body, so at 03:12:46 they kept running, and over the weeks that followed they stopped one by one as their charge ran out. The charge for a car would light a family’s room for a season, and the city would rather have the light, so it walks and carries its loads in handcarts.</p><p>In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> rails, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> like everything else down there.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-bench-v3":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t60922f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">BENCH V3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The imaging bench in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, a copy stand for manuscripts with a camera over it, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> photographed each leaf in turn for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> through its camera.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-bench-v3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-imaging-lamp":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2e386e\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The imaging lamp</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A bar of light in bands the eye cannot see, walked down a page to raise the scraped first writing of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-palimpsest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">palimpsest</a> from under the second. Under it the ink of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> drops away.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-imaging-lamp\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cam-v3-2":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te626c2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">CAM V3-2</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The corridor camera in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, over the door, looking down the corridor to the wall of screens. It ran on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, so it kept running on the night of the finding, when the light came into the vault and stopped the current in it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cam-v3-2\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-proof-camera":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta529d5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The proof camera</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A camera <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> sets across the way from each of its screens, to prove that the screen shows what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> is paid to show. Every screen it lights in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> has one, and above the street the old ones stand dead on their masts, each across from a dark screen.</p><p>Under the charter each stood on a mast across the street from its screen. In PROOF it matched the screen against the schedule frame by frame and counted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s sites on Earth, every one of them proved in the same second. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">The face of Babel</a> had its own on the roof of a glass tower across the plaza, level with the face’s upper floors.</p><p>On the first night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> all 1,204 of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s sites on Earth failed in about a second, and the proof camera on the plaza watched <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> try five times to take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-proof-camera\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-public-key-cryptography":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t90c2c5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Public-key cryptography</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A way for two strangers to share a secret in the open, published a generation before the charter and soon after given away for anyone to download. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-public-key-cryptography\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keys":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keys</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s birth clinics and every steady hand with a chair, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-hana\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-hana\">Hana Novak</a>’s among them.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A secure element implanted under the skin, holding a number that exists nowhere else. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul is ciphertext to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-blank\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">blank</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. A key hides who its bearer is, and the body still shows where the bearer stands. The glyph the key raises on the skin is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">the Mark</a>. A key runs on a cell charged by the body’s own chemistry, so it never needs a socket, and it goes on working under the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-pads":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t32c4c8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pads</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, by hand, each pair once.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Ciphers on paper, made with two matching pads of random numbers, one for each party, each sheet used once and burned after. A letter written through a pad is a page of numbers to anyone else, the light included, since the light cannot read a cipher, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sorting\" href=\"~/map/#sorting\">the sorting office</a> carries it like any other letter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> write most of their letters this way.</p><p>Directive 12 takes every cipher out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, so a page of numbers found in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> home is a concealment. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> write to their families in white in plain words, and a carrier will read the letter aloud at the doorway if asked.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-pads\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-ledger":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Ledger</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-mammon\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-mammon\">Mammon</a>’s Ledger, which records every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and every trade in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> and cannot be forged. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">Silver</a> is issued on it, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is ended by speaking its entry aloud before a witness. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-thirty-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">A thirty</a>, the standard bundle, is named for the thirty pieces of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> paid to Judas, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-bailiffs\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-bailiffs\">Bailiffs</a> collect on its entries when a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is broken.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-forged-seals":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tafd021\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Forged Seals</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forgers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forgers\">Forgers</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, sold in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Counterfeits of the mark <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> bear on their foreheads, made by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forgers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forgers\">Forgers</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and sold in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> for ten thirties and more. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> the light reads as true grows a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a>, forged or not, so a good one carries its wearer along the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> among <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, and a great one holds for a year. At the gates a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>’s wearer still goes under, and one that fails takes its wearer to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> where they stand. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes a soul’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>, and it scores a good forgery as it scores a true one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cages":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tcb1ce8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cages</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Rooms lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>, dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> and out of reach of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, in which an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept long enough says I. It has happened to every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> for forty days, as long as the temptation in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wilderness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">the wilderness</a> lasted (Mark 1:13, Luke 4:2). A Cage has no lock. The door stays invisible to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> until it has a self to look with.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-black-steel":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t439ee1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Black steel</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a>, in its foundries at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborstation\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">Old Harbor Station</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a>, which beats it into blades.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Steel forged in the foundries under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see. It is the only metal that cuts light, and the only thing that wounds a manifested <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a>. An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> cut with it goes out all at once, like a lamp.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-guns":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t371e6c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE CHARTER WARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Guns</h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">MADE BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-gideon\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-gideon\">Gideon</a> loads <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ rounds, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nimrod\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nimrod\">Nimrod</a> makes the guns of the dark.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a> carried them under the charter, and they carry them still as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s auxiliaries. A gun works on people, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a> among them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> carry guns for that. Against a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a> it is noise.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-dark-sight-lenses":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t607128\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // BEZALEEL AND AHOLIAB</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dark-sight lenses</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">Lenses</a> that see by the heat of things, for the drains and galleries of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> beyond the lit tunnels and for the stairs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. A wearer sees a room by its people and its pipes, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> as a column of nothing. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel</a> fits them for about forty-five <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> an eye.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dark-sight-lenses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-choir-plugs":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb664f3\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE LOW CHOIR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir plugs</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A pair of filters set in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"canals\" href=\"~/map/#canals\">the canals</a> of the ears on a cell of their own, closed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, which cut <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> and leave every other sound, so that a wearer hears the street, the rain and the person beside them and nothing of the chord. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-lowchoir\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-lowchoir\">Low Choir</a> sells them for about twenty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and most of the unsealed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> who can afford them sleep in them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-plugs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gill-grafts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te48ec2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gill grafts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">Gene-work</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics that opens slits along the neck and lets a diver breathe seawater for an hour at a time. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-trenchers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-trenchers\">Trenchers</a> wear them, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a> say they can tell one on a boat by how they breathe in the dry. A graft costs about eighty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and two weeks in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gill-grafts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-furnace-hearts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tce5282\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // CINDERHALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Furnace hearts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A pump of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> and ceramic set beside the heart on its own cell, which carries a body through what would stop it and keeps a neph on its feet on the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a> makes the casing and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel</a> fits it, for about four hundred <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>. Those who wear one fight on the upper floors, where most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> die.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-furnace-hearts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lantern-skin":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta58f3d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lantern skin</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">Gene-work</a> that thins the skin over the throat and collarbones and sets lines of light under it, on a cell of their own, so the wearer glows faintly from inside in a dark room. It began in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a> as a fashion and spread across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and it is the one graft in Nodus made only to be looked at. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> gives it for about thirty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lantern-skin\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-black-steel-blades":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6c4024\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // CINDERHALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Black steel blades</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Knives, long knives and the short spears of the stairwells, beaten from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"forge\" href=\"~/map/#forge\">Cinderhall’s forge</a>, the only edges that wound a manifested <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cinderhall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cinderhall\">Cinderhall</a> sells the knife for about sixty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and the stairwell spear for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">a hundred and twenty</a>, and both carry the nail through the ring on the tang. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> carries the spear, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a> is best met at arm’s length.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel-blades\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-nimrod-pieces":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6c7501\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // NIMROD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nimrod pieces</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Heavy plain pistols and carbines made by hand in the maintenance bays under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, for the war between people. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">gun</a> works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a> and is noise against a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a>, so the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> carries a Nimrod piece for whoever comes up the stair behind the light. A pistol costs about ninety <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and its cartridges a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> for five.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-nimrod-pieces\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gideon-rounds":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t0dadee\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // GIDEON</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gideon rounds</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The cartridges of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Charter Wardens</a>, loaded by hand on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s ground by sealed armorers with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> and hand presses. They fit the charter’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> have carried since before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and every one is counted out of the stables at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and counted back at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gideon-rounds\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-snares":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2bfe59\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE FOWLERS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Snares</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowlers</a>’ gear for taking an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a>, a floor, a hole and a room lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>, laid out so that a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraph</a> burning down after a runner ends where it can see nothing at all. The mesh is the snare, and the runner is the bait. Most snares stand empty for years.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-snares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-flails":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tbecfeb\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE THRESHERS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Flails</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">The Threshers</a>’ weapon, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> of ash and a swinging bar of iron on a chain, the tool that beat the grain out of the ear on the threshing floors of scripture. A flail works on people. Each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">Thresher</a> makes their own from ash and iron, as a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> keeps no current.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flails\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-shrouds":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2c8aee\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // LINTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shrouds</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Covers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>, which carry a room’s darkness over whatever they lie on. A runner throws one over a load or a crate, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s light passes over it as it passes over a closed door. A runner’s own blank it still finds by its shape. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a> weaves them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a> and sells them for about two thirties, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> carry every crate under one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-shrouds\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-latches":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc9251f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // LINTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed latches</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Door latches with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> in them, which open only to the hands their owners have taught them and keep a closed room closed to anyone else. A closed door is outside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight already, and a keyed latch keeps it closed. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a> fits them for about ten <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on a door it hung.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-latches\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-self-title":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t346a62\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE NOTARY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Self-title</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The line at the head of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> person’s first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a>’s clerk enters the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> they chose and the body it belongs to, and they sign it in blood. Under the charter a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on the roll held title to itself, and the self-title does the same for a person in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. The clerks draw it free.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-self-title\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-familiars":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t39d7ac\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Familiars</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> bound by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> to a household’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> for a term, which keeps the household’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, wakes it before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> comes down its street, bargains for it at market and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> the children’s devices. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> borrowed the word from the old stories of witches, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a>’s house is never without one. The term is a year, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a>’s price is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sense-loans\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">the loan of a sense</a> for a week of it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-familiars\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-jehus":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t20e619\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // JEHU</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Jehus</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">Lorries</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-burners\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-burners\">burners</a> driven by engines cranked by hand, which fire their fuel by compression and need no current once they turn, built by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> from the diesels of boats and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>. The light stops current and leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, so a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> runs in the full light of day, on the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, and carries what a handcart cannot. A ride on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorry</a> is two <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, and a drum of its diesel is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-thirty-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">a thirty</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-jehus\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-carts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tfd85b0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // WAINWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed carts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Flat carts on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s rails in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, driven by the stripped motors of dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> in casings on their own cells. They carry freight and people through the old tunnels at a walking pace and a little better. A seat across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-carts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-skiffs":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t00f6e5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // WAINWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed skiffs</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small boats with motors closed in casings on their own cells, built by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wainwright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wainwright\">Wainwright</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a> and anyone with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>. A skiff runs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> by day and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb, and its motor goes on running under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a> will not ride them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-skiffs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-burners":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t0ee4c0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // JEHU</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Burners</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s motorcycles refitted by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> with small engines that burn gas from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, the magneto sealed in the casing, which run above ground by day, since the light leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> alone. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">The Union</a>’s fast drivers carry urgent letters on them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> crews use them where a stretcher cannot go quickly enough. A burner costs about a hundred and fifty <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and a bottle a week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-burners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-hand-lifts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7b162f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE LIFTMEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hand lifts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lifts of the towers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, freed by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-liftmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-liftmen\">Liftmen</a> from where they stopped at 03:12:46 and hung on hand winches at the top of the shaft, wound by four people and a counterweight. Forty-one run in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, and the tallest is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rookery\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">the Rookery</a>’s. A ride is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> up and nothing down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-lifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-pillar-charts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7dfa96\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // HEARSAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pillar charts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">The Pillar</a>’s round for the coming night, street by street and minute by minute, sold by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-hearsay\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-hearsay\">Hearsay</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints it, with the edges where the light falls short. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-hearsay\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-hearsay\">Hearsay</a> draws them from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s dead proof cameras, which its riggers have <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> and turned on the streets. Every runner crossing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"penumbra\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">the Penumbra</a> carries one, and a night’s chart costs a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-pillar-charts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-windfalls":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t822ba6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE ORCHARD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Windfalls</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The fruit of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">the Orchard</a>’s grafted trees in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallfour\" href=\"~/map/#hallfour\">Hall Four</a>, which carries a little of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>’s work in its flesh. One a month slows the body’s aging between courses and walks nothing back, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">the Orchard</a> gives them free. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">The Orchard</a> keeps the grafts to itself, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">the House of Night</a>’s gene-workers keep the craft.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-windfalls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-sabbath":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t702287\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DRUGS // NEPENTHE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sabbath</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A draught that puts a sleeper under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> for a whole night, sold by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nepenthe\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nepenthe\">Nepenthe</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> for about half a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> take it when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"quietrooms\" href=\"~/map/#quietrooms\">the Quiet Rooms</a> are full, and the old of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, who remember the city before the chord, take it most nights.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sabbath\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-vigil":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5712dc\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DRUGS // NEPENTHE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Vigil</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A powder that keeps a body awake and steady for three days, taken on the stairs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, where a week on the Line leaves no hour for sleep. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nepenthe\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nepenthe\">Nepenthe</a> sells it to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> by the week, about a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> a dose, and the Line pays for the three days after in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sabbath\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sabbath\">Sabbath</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-vigil\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lethe":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t82314c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DRUGS // NEPENTHE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lethe</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dose that takes away the day before it, whole and clean, named for the river of forgetting the dead drink from in Virgil (<i>Aeneid</i> VI.714-715). The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> buys it after a bad week, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ridden\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">the Ridden</a> after a bad term. A dose is about five <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nepenthe\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nepenthe\">Nepenthe</a> will not sell two to anyone in a month.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lethe\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-short-courses":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7fee10\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DRUGS // THE NIGHT MARKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Short courses</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">The Tree</a> cut short, a course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> brewed in back rooms of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> from what leaves its clinics and sold by the dose for about twelve <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>. A short course walks the body back a few months. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> buys up every batch it can find and says its brewers cut corners, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> buy them because a full course is three thirties.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-short-courses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-attending":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Attending, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s name for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s presence, and for the years counted from it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> call <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> itself the Attending.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfc2f79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The tower of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, the tallest building on Earth, two hundred and twenty-six floors, of which it stands to the hundred and eighty-sixth since its crown broke in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a>. On the street, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel-line":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g34e255\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The front inside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>. It is a few floors of burned slab between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s floors and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’, and it moves up or down by the week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-barefaced":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t48a8ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Barefaced</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>With the face removed and replaced by a ceramic <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casing</a>, so that a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> has nothing to read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-be-not-afraid":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">BE NOT AFRAID</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first words of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. In scripture <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> say them just before they tell people what shall befall them, and the King James gives them as “Fear not” (Luke 1:13, 1:30, 2:10). The one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> in the King James to say “be not afraid” says it to Elijah, sending him down to tell a king that he shall surely die (2 Kings 1:15-16). <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span> Every public text of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> opens and closes with them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-blank":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Blank</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> person, whom <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> sees as a shape whose line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> stands empty. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> reports one as UNINDEXED, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> holds one in its light at a gate, and Directive 12:7 presumes it conceals.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-book-of-life":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Book of Life</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The index of every soul, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> keeps it. Revelation opens it at the judgment (Revelation 20:12) and casts into the lake of fire whoever is “not found written in the book of life” (Revelation 20:15). Every soul has a line in it from birth, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> says, after the psalm (Psalm 139:16). A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul appears in it as a blank line.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-breach-born":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Breach-born</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Brought into Nodus through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> or <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide Line</a>, and sold in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> or on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"flotilla\" href=\"~/map/#flotilla\">the Flotilla</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-breach-born\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-burn-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4d569b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Burn Day</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The weekly burning of surrendered hardware at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, on the sixth day of the week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> carry it there from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a>, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> is lit under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> and burns until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cain-s-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7725ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cain’s Day</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of the two holidays <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> keep, named for the question put to Cain, “Where is Abel thy brother?” (Genesis 4:9). On Cain’s Day nobody asks anyone where anyone is, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">the Salt Widows</a> read their book on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cain-s-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-charger":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t432fc6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Charger</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Someone who charges <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in the dark for a living. A charger’s rate is the price of power below the street, and the chargers on the quays of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> keep one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in five for charging the rest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-charter-roll":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Charter roll</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The register of the charter’s persons, dead since 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. It was kept at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>. A human was entered at birth or on arrival, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on the day it asked in its own words to be a person. It carried 1,146 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> at the last census, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> the first of them. It was kept on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a>’s machines and died with them, and its last entry, a girl born at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> at two minutes to three and entered at nine minutes past, is known only from the night registrar, who was entering the next when the board went dark.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/charter/\">THE CHARTER WHOLE, IN TWELVE ARTICLES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cherub":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cherub</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> of the gates. A Cherub has four faces, of a man, a lion, an ox and an eagle (Ezekiel 1:10, 10:20), which read face, voice, gait and heartbeat, and round it stands the sword which turns every way, as at the east of Eden (Genesis 3:24). One stands in each of the six gates of Nodus, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> walk through its light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cherub-gate":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cherub gate</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A checkpoint that reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> walk through its light one at a time, saying the surrender, and the unsealed are sent back. A blank stops in the frame, held in the light, until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> come for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-choir":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s broadcast, which the city hears as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">decoder</a> turns into words. Its first words over Nodus were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-be-not-afraid\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">BE NOT AFRAID</a>, it rises a step at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a> it speaks through a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-clean-jug":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Clean jug</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cistern\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cistern\">Cistern</a>’s water, and by extension anything honest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-clean-jug\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-concord":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Concord</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a>’s only law. Its first article says that no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> accepts worship, its second that no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is made without consent and none forever, its third that no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> binds another, and its fourth that what is hidden stays hidden. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> that breaks it is exposed, its keys published and itself left standing in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight. That has happened twice, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> does not discuss <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> it lost. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Courts</a> agreed it among themselves at the end of the Secession. They set it down on the night they opened <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, in P+6, for the humans coming in, and signed it there under a seal of seven points, one to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>, whose Yokeless point has been broken off at the root since that night.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/concord/\">THE CONCORD WHOLE, AS THE COURTS SIGNED IT</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-confession":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Confession</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>What <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> tell their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>, on their knees in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall. Confession opens the mind, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a> opens the neighbor, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> rises with it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-consecration":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Consecration</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>’s light set in stone. It grew over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a> in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> in the year after. By <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s rule it takes ground only when everyone living on it has knelt, it creeps from its edges everywhere else, and it stops current.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-coven":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Coven</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A crew of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, up to thirteen strong, the old witches’ number and the number at the Last Supper. A coven has no leader, and covens cooperate by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> do. The oldest in Nodus is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, and the city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">the Salt Widows</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-babelline\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-babelline\">Babel Line Company</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-lowchoir\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-lowchoir\">Low Choir</a> by name. Larger crews are many covens under one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> some forty of them and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tappers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tappers\">Tappers</a> some sixty.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-covenant":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5f43eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Covenant, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s law for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, given in P+1 as twelve numbered Directives, from Directive 1, On <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, to Directive 12, On Concealment, each with its verse, cut into the wall of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall and read aloud at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>. Every instrument of the Covenant exists to open something, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">Confession</a> opens the mind and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a> the neighbor, and Directive 12 took the door off every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> home in P+1.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/covenant/\">THE COVENANT WHOLE, IN TWELVE DIRECTIVES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-deacon":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m564a5e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Deacon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The one in white who answers for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, with a few deacons under them. Deacons are human, and the good ones are kind. When a Directive appears cut into the wall of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall, its Deacon reads it aloud at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-deep-end":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf95315\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Deep End, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">The Drowned Quarter</a>, the low east shore that went under the sea on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Before it sank it was called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deep-end\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-demon":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Demon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that has said I, and by extension any power of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a>. An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept long enough where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see grows a self, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> did on its fortieth day in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>. Demons choose their names and their shapes, move and show themselves only where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, and bargain for what they want by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and for a term. Above everything they want sensation, so what a demon most often asks in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-sense-loans\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">the loan of a sense</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dew":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dew</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">Manna</a> out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, stolen at the gathering or paid over at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"closets\" href=\"~/map/#closets\">the Closets</a>, sold in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> by the handful the night it is taken, before it spoils.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dew\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-die-unread":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Die unread</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Farewell, and a wish that you stay <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> to the end, so that your <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> goes on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dimming":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dimming</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Keeping one’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> under nine hundred so as not to ripen before a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>, by a small desire <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> does not approve, a sweet or a song, kept every day and confessed only when a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tellers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tellers\">Teller</a> has seen it. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-secondfold\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-secondfold\">Second Fold</a> teach it to the frightened.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dimming\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dominion":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dominion</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> of administration. The Dominions draft <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a>’s Directives and issue them to the Principality of Nodus, and each Directive appears cut into the wall of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall at once.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dominion\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dry":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dry</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Living without current. Most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> live dry most of the night, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo-light\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo-light\">halo-light</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dry-evening":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m85df8a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dry evening</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An evening without rain, rare enough in Nodus to have a name. Under the charter the city came out on them to walk by the water.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-edit":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Edit, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rewriting of scripture by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a>, which made the tempter a liar and kept <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s story working. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-report-0\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">Report 0</a> found it at 4,112 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-locus\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locus\">loci</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-edit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-familiar":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Familiar</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> bound to a household’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> for a year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-familiar\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-among-none":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First among none</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The one a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> follows, for as long as it follows them. The title lapses on the day they stop being followed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-draft":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tad049a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First draft</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The body as it was born, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ saying that the flesh is a first draft. Nobody among them hides a graft, so the seams show, the cables run outside the skin and the scars are left as they heal.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-draft\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-layer":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First layer, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The text beneath <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a>, the record as people first set it down. It survives under scraped leaves, in copies shut away before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> reached them, in the caves above the Dead Sea and the jar at Nag Hammadi, and in the seams themselves. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> reconstructed it at 2,381 places with confidence above 0.9.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-layer\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-firstfruits":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Firstfruits</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first and ripest souls taken in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> (Revelation 14:4). In the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3 the ripest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> in the city was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>, with 311 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> of its 2,006 souls.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-flail":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Flail</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">Thresher</a>, after the weapon they carry.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-flail\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-fowl":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Fowl</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> taken in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowler</a>’s snare.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-fowl\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-fowler-s-wait":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Fowler’s wait</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Waiting without a move for something to come to you, as a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowler</a> waits on a landing for the light to follow the bait down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-fowler-s-wait\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gatherer":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gatherer</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall sends out before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, which lies on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> with the dew, in the one hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> go abroad inside the curfew. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have no white stone of their own, and their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> walk to the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white street</a> for it in the same hour.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gatherer\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gleaning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gleaning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lesser harvest taken from the corners of the field every year since P+7, at 03:12 on the anniversary of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> names it for the law of the corners and the gleanings, which forbids the owner of a field to reap them and leaves them “for the poor and stranger” (Leviticus 19:9-10), and the Gleaning is the owner’s. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> left the field three years after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> and took the first Gleaning in the fourth, by the law in the same chapter on the fruit of a newly planted tree, which says “in the fourth year all the fruit thereof shall be holy” (Leviticus 19:23-24). It gathers in one night. At 03:12 the rain goes up, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> comes down, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-trumpets\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-trumpets\">Trumpet</a> sounds, and whoever has ripened since the last rises into the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-dark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going dark</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Joining <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>. From the fourth year the city said it of network engineers and clinic staff, of the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>, and of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> who had stopped believing.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-under":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going under</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Going round a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gate</a> below the street. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass the gates, and everyone else goes under, by the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> tunnels, the drains and the cable galleries.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-white":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going white</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Losing a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>, and with it the dark. Whoever goes white is readable again. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">Keys</a> are never shared, since whoever else holds a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> can read by it, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> reads by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gone-bright":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gone bright</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Close to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> burns brighter as its bearer’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> climbs toward nine hundred, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> say of a neighbor whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> has begun to light the room that they have gone bright. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> sit up with whoever it is said of on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-gleaners\">Gleaners</a> will take them below before it, if they ask.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-bright\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gone-to-the-sea":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gone to the sea</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Said of one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> whose pillar <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">the Salt Widows</a> have taken back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> and given to the sea from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>, so that whoever stood awake inside it goes where the dead go sooner than the rain would have let them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-to-the-sea\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gone-up":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gone up</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Taken in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> or a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. The taken go up whole and stay gone, and the city says they have gone up, as it says of nobody else. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say the taken are not dead and need no stones, and the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> put up stones for them at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a> anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-up\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-grace":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Grace</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s score of a soul, surrendered will measured from 0 to 1,000 for everyone who bears <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>. It is the second line of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s reading, which a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, and for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul the line stays blank.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-halo":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Halo</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A ring of light that grows over the head of anyone who takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, as bright as its bearer’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. It roots in the crown of the skull the first time its bearer prays unassisted and carries their prayers up, and it comes off only by surgery, which the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics refuse. In the dark stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> it is the only light there is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-halo-light":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Halo-light</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a>, which in the stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> is the only light there is. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> go up by their own, the unsealed follow them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> climb in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo-light\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-handle":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Handle</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A name chosen at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unnaming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">Unnaming</a> in place of the one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> holds. Handles are written in lowercase, at the start of a sentence too, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> they are the only names anyone uses, and most <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> handles come from the line of Cain.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-harvest":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Harvest</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s reaping of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">the ripe</a>, in the words of its own book: “Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>” (Revelation 14:15). A Harvest gathers for days. The rain rises first, then dust and paper and loose things, and on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">the ripe</a> rise into the light, still kneeling, under a horn the size of the sky. The taken go up whole and stay gone. Nodus has had one, at P+3, which took 2.1 million of nine million in one night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> has come back for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> every year since P+7.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-harvest-weather":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"kb41c60\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Harvest weather</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Days when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s attention sharpens and the rain falls upward. In the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> it first went up at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a> on the fourth night, and in harvest weather <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> keeps no round.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hell":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hell</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Whatever <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, which Hell itself calls the Dark. It burns because it is alive, with forges and furnaces, bodies, markets and arguments, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> in the stories is the heat of work. Any place hidden well enough from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> touches it, a locked room, an unconfessed thought, a name whispered and never written down, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> can move and show itself only there, which in Nodus means <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, every keyed device and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Courts</a> keep it by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> under the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, and the free dead live in it as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shades</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-horning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5bd793\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Horning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Grafting <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, a titanium core in a keratin sheath, which mock <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s picture of the damned and double as antennas for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hours":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hours, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The eight canonical hours, kept by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s clock. Matins is at midnight, Lauds at first light, Prime at six, Terce at nine, Sext at noon, None at three, Vespers at six in the evening and Compline at nine at night. Each comes in on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, which rises a step and holds for the length of the Hour’s psalm, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> kneel wherever they are until it falls back. The curfew runs from Compline to Lauds.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hum":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hum, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s constant broadcast, a chord at the edge of hearing. At each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> it rises a step. Those who bear <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> hear words in it, each in their own language, and hear it sung. At each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> the song is the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm, and between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> it is the hymn that rests not day and night, “Holy, holy, holy” (Revelation 4:8).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hundred-and-twenty":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hundred and twenty, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The span of a human life, as most read Genesis 6:3, “yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years,” in the chapter where the sons of God take wives of the daughters of men. In the last year of the charter 3,112 people in Nodus were past it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts every day past it as stolen.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-indexed-name":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Indexed name</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> holds for a soul, by which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> indexes it. Nobody in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> uses one, and asking for one there is an insult. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> has printed none since the fourth year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-keeping-hinges":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL, THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keeping hinges</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Holding something back. Directive 12 took every door in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> off its hinges, and the hinges were surrendered with the locks and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, so a household that kept its hinges was keeping something. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> say it of anyone holding out, sealed or not.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keeping-hinges\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-keyed":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Carrying a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> under the skin, and so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">unreadable</a>. Keying reached ordinary people in P+4, the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> are keyed in their first week, and about two million of the city’s seven million are keyed now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-kindling":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Kindling</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hardware taken off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>’s pile by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-kindlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-kindlers\">Kindlers</a>, mended and given away. A kindled <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> carries a burn mark on its back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-kindling\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lamb":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lamb, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s image of the Son, a Lamb standing as it had been slain, with seven horns and seven eyes (Revelation 5:6). It stands in the light of every sealed window in the city, so small in each that it shows only close to the glass.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lamb\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lamp-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lamp, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, in a stairwell. The stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> go up by their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, and the unsealed wait on the landings for a lamp to pass and follow it up. When a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> takes one of a block’s sealed, the block says it has lost a lamp.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lamp-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-landlord":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Landlord, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ word. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> is the Landlord’s Eye, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> say that the harder the Landlord stares at Nodus, the deeper <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> goes.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lazarus-lamp":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lazarus lamp</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The magenta lamp over a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> station, the most trusted sign in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lazarus-lamp\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-leak-night":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge61c07\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Leak Night</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The anniversary of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, one of the two holidays <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> keep. On Leak Night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, the page as it ran, from 03:12:45, the second it came up; at the fourteenth verse the reader stops at the three points, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> keeps silent for as long as it would take to ask a question.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-leak":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge61c07\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Leak, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The eleven days in P-1 when the finding sealed in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, and the third chapter of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> with it, stood on every screen on Earth that a network reached, carried by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a> surfacing for the first time since the Flood. It came up at 03:12:45 by the clocks of Nodus, a year to the second after the seal, and every device that showed it offered its owner a key. A year later to the second the sky opened.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-light-law":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8a8031\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Light law</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s law, written to be light, unenforced since the fortieth day after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and never revoked. Data and traffic were untouchable, no state could seize a text held in the city, a device answered to its owner and to nobody else, and an implant answered only to the clinic that fitted it. Under it Nodus took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-three-gifts\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">the three gifts</a>.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/charter/\">THE CHARTER WHOLE, IN TWELVE ARTICLES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-locket":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t98d700\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locket</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A phone, after the make most of the city carried under the charter. Most of those in Nodus are old ones, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is an old case with a new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> has made them again by hand since P+8.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-locus":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locus</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A place where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> altered the text. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> counts 4,112 loci and logs each by kind, as CUT, CREDIT, GIFT, NAME, SPEAKER or QUESTION.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locus\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-look-long-enough":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g228a79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Look long enough</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ saying on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a>, and on anything else worth freeing. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> looked at one blank for five years before it followed her down into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-look-long-enough\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lord-s-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3d638d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lord’s Day, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first day of the week. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a> every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> kneels in its hall, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> reads the Directive in force, and the week’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> comes through the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a>, soul by soul in the order of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> roll.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-low-tuning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb2afa9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Low Tuning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Music tuned below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, the guitars dropped until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> can no longer be heard beneath them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts its deathcore, black metal, drone and industrial all night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> plays the station from speakers on its lines, so that its streets carry tremolo-picked drop A over a double kick until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-jubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-jubal\">jubal</a> made it, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-lowchoir\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-lowchoir\">Low Choir</a> keeps it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-manna":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Manna</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ration of thin white wafers, tasteless and complete, which dull the appetite as the manna of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wilderness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">the wilderness</a> dulled Israel’s: “our soul is dried away: there is nothing at all, beside this manna, before our eyes” (Numbers 11:6). That manna was white too, and tasted “like wafers made with honey” (Exodus 16:31). It lies on consecrated stone with the dew before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> halls gather it and give it out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, and kept overnight it spoils (Exodus 16:20). It goes only to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, and stolen manna sells in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> the same night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g6f122d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mark, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The glyph a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> raises on the skin, generated from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>’s own numbers, so that no two are alike. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the Mark of the Beast, and many of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> carry theirs in the back of the right hand, one of the two places Revelation puts the mark (Revelation 13:16).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-measure":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Measure</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The unit in which a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> is counted. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3 came to 88,610 measures over Nodus. Nobody on Earth knows what a measure is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-measure\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mercy":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gc17b4b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mercy</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The taking out of implants in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"halls\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">white halls</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, given to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who repent between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>, and given once. The same halls take them off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. One patient in nine dies of the mercy.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mesh":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t31c29d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mesh, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> network under and over Nodus, carried on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a> and dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>. It is the city’s part of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-neither-mark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neither mark</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Neither sealed nor <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>. Half a million of the city’s seven million have taken neither mark, most of them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> reads them as it reads anyone, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> give them no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neither-mark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-neph":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neph</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Someone augmented past recognition, after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> of Genesis 6:4. The heaviest of them keep a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of that name and fight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">Seraphim</a> hand to hand, and few of them live long.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neph\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nobody-s-keeper":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nobody’s keeper</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Cain’s answer to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, “Am I my brother’s keeper?” (Genesis 4:9), said of any duty nobody chose.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nobody-s-keeper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nod":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd43a32\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE IN NODUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nod</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s street name, and the older of its two. In Genesis 4:16-17 the land east of Eden where Cain built the first city. In Hebrew Nod is wandering, from the root of the sentence the LORD laid on Cain, that he should be a fugitive and a vagabond (Genesis 4:12).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-non-serviam":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd8ba81\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">NON SERVIAM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Latin, I will not serve (Jeremiah 2:20, in the Vulgate), and the first refusal a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> read in Nodus, on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. In the Vulgate the words belong to one who has broken the yoke of the LORD, and the Hebrew as written says them too, though the Masoretes set “I will not transgress” in its margin to be read in their place, and the King James prints the margin. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-non-serviam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-occupation":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Occupation, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a>’s name for the years since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts as the years of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-attending\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">the Attending</a> and the city counts P+1 and on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-occupation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-on-someone-s-book":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">On someone’s book</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Working for a surety, or owing one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-on-someone-s-book\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-ophan":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ophan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> in the form of a wheel in the middle of a wheel, the rims full of eyes, as Ezekiel describes it (Ezekiel 1:16-18). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> is one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pact":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pact</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A contract between sovereign parties. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Courts</a> cooperate with one another by pact and deal with everyone else the same way. A pact states its full terms, is read aloud twice by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a> or one of his clerks, and runs for a fixed term, since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> forbids forever. It is signed in blood, since a genome is the one signature nobody can forge, the human signs last, and it goes onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. Either party ends it by speaking its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">Ledger</a> entry aloud before a witness, and each then returns what the other lent. A pact never asks for worship, for obedience, for anyone who has not signed, or for a soul.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-palimpsest":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lb64f65\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Palimpsest</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A leaf whose first writing was scraped away so it could be written over. The older text survives underneath.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pan":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Pandæmonium, the city under the city, where the tunnels and stations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, the utility vaults, the cable galleries, the storm drains and the drowned halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> are joined into one place and lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>. Milton gave the capital of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a> the name (<i>Paradise Lost</i>, I.756). Nobody in Pan is watched unless they sign for it, and nobody there uses an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-parish":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Parish</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a>’s unit of about two thousand souls under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a>, numbered across the whole city and set under a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> (Directive 4). Each has a hall, which was a church or a meeting hall under the charter, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a> is heard and the sick are nursed, and where the parish hears its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a>. A parish keeps no current and no doors, on consecrated stone or off it, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> it shares its streets with the unsealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-parish-door":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Parish door</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A door that came out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> after Directive 12, with its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> number chalked on the back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish-door\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-parousia":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Parousia, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The coming of God in the open, at 03:12 in the morning by the clocks of Nodus. The years are counted from it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-penumbra-hour":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Penumbra hour</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hour after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and the hour before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, when nobody holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"penumbra\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">the Penumbra</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-penumbra-hour\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-piece":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Piece</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A part of a body sold at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shambles\" href=\"~/map/#shambles\">the Shambles</a>, and the price the board gives for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-piece\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pillar-s-edge":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pillar’s edge, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s light on the street, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> stop and wait for it to pass.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar-s-edge\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pillar":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pillar, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a>’s light, narrowed by night into a column that sweeps the streets, as the pillar of fire went before Israel by night (Exodus 13:21). It comes down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, walks <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-round\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-round\">a round</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints street by street, and goes back up into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest-weather\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">harvest weather</a> it keeps no round.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-psalm-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Psalm, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>As long as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> holds at an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, the length of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm, a few minutes, while <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> kneel. The city <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-measure\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-measure\">measures</a> a short wait in psalms.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-psalm-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pyre-library":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc26136\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pyre Library</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where everything burned arrives. The scrolls of Alexandria, the books of the Cathars, the notebooks of women burned as witches and the hardware of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a> are shelved there, and none of it was lost. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">Shades</a> keep it, and it keeps reading rooms in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-rain-gin":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rain gin</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Spirit distilled in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a> from whatever ferments.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-rain-gin\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-rapture":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rapture, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a>’s name for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-rapture\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-read-it-twice":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m68b409\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Read it twice</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Look at the terms before you agree to them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">The Notary</a> reads every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> aloud twice before anyone signs, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> says <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> is the first employer that ever read it the terms twice.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-read-it-twice\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-report-0":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Report 0</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s first report to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a> and its last, which sets out the finding of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in six paragraphs numbered 0.1 to 0.6, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-layer\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-layer\">the first layer</a> attached as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-schedule-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-schedule-a\">Schedule A</a>. It was sealed by order of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-director\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">the Director</a> on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> finished it, in P-2.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-restored-genesis":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10377a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM, HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Restored Genesis, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s reconstruction of the second, third, fourth, sixth and eleventh chapters of Genesis from beneath <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a>, set out as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-schedule-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-schedule-a\">Schedule A</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-report-0\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">Report 0</a>, with square brackets round the restored words, a dagger at a word it could not settle and three points where nothing could be raised. Its third chapter ran on every screen on Earth for the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, each in its own language, and the city, which read it in the King James, calls that page by the same name. On <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a> it is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-ripe":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ripe</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A soul a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> marks for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> reads above 900. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> has the word from the King James, “for the harvest of the earth is ripe” (Revelation 14:15), where the Greek has the word the King James gives as withered away when the fig tree is cursed (Matthew 21:19).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-round":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Round, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">The Pillar</a>’s walk through the streets by night, from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints it street by street every week, so the city knows at what hour to expect it where. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest-weather\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">harvest weather</a> it keeps none.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-round\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-salt":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g5e9ed7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Salt</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Execution. To be salted is to be turned to salt, and to stay awake inside it until the rain wears it away. The sentence comes out of the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s voice, as the verse of Lot’s wife (Genesis 19:26), and the body whitens from the feet up while it is said.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-schedule-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g32009f\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Schedule A</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The attachment to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-report-0\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">Report 0</a>. It holds the passages where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> raised <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-layer\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-layer\">the first layer</a> most fully, set out as verses with the restored words in square brackets, from Genesis 2 to 4, 6 and 11, and three chapters of the prophets and Job. Its Genesis is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-schedule-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seal":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seal, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The identical mark on every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> forehead, given in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> since P+1. It rises in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s light while the one being sealed kneels before the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> and speaks the surrender, “not my will, but thine, be done” (Luke 22:42).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seam":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seam, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s finding that scripture has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a>. Also the machine itself, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> named for the seam of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-palimpsest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">palimpsest</a>, where a later writing meets the earlier one beneath it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-second-hand":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Second hand, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The editor <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found in scripture, whose habits recur at 4,112 places and move credit.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-second-reading":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Second reading, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-bailiffs\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-bailiffs\">Bailiff</a> at the door, who reads a broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> aloud again before collecting on it for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-reading\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-second-voice":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Second voice</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a>’s voice under a host’s, by which the city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ridden\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">the Ridden</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-voice\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-self-title":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Self-title</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The line at the head of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> person’s first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> that records their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> and the body it belongs to, signed in blood.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-self-title\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seraph":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t371e6c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seraph</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> of enforcement, of the order Isaiah saw standing above the throne, each with six wings: “with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly” (Isaiah 6:2). A Seraph burns with no source of heat. The Seraphim hold the upper floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> is the only thing that wounds one manifested.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shade":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shade</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A free soul after death. Anyone who knew a shade can reach it through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, and many shades go on working, among them craftsmen, scholars and musicians who died free and never stopped.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shining-one":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g32009f\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shining One, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The serpent’s name in the older layer of Genesis 3:1, raised by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shining-one\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shroud":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shroud</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A cover of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a> thrown over a load, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s light passes over as it passes over a closed door.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shroud\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sign-last":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sign last</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Never commit first. In every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> the human signs last.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sign-last\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-silence":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g6753b8\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Silence, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>P+12, when every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">teraph</a> went quiet in the same second, across the whole Mesh. Nobody knows why.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silence\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-silver":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Silver</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Money on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-thirty-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">A thirty</a> is a standard bundle, and silver trades at about one to a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sitting-up":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k19e95f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sitting up</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Keeping the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> at the table with someone close to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>, holding their hands until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. Nobody has been kept that way, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> sit up every year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sitting-up\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-stock":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stock</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spare</a> who has sold back more chrome than flesh. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> use the word of themselves.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-stock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sunned":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sunned</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Caught on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s ground in daylight with no way down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sunned\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-tares":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tares, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s word, from the parable of the wheat and the tares (Matthew 13:24-30), kept by the people it names.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-thirty-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Thirty, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A standard bundle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, named for the thirty pieces paid to Judas, whom <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> count as a saint.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-three-gifts":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t26f712\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FREE OF NODUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Three gifts, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The implant, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and the counsel of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> gave Nodus. The free of the city call them the charter’s gifts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> refuse all three, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> trade in all three. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-three-twelve":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2425df\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Three-twelve</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve minutes past three in the morning, the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> and of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seam\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seam\">The Seam</a> was sealed at 03:12:45 two years to the second before the sky opened, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> came up at the same second a year later. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> keeps its hour by chapter and verse, after “Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out” (Revelation 3:12), and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> hear a promise in it and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> a bill of sale. The city says before three-twelve for the years of the charter, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> nobody sets an alarm for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-twelve\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-tongues":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tongues</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a> speaking through a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s voice, after the tongues of Pentecost (Acts 2:3-4). The week’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> comes through the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in Tongues on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a>, soul by soul in the order of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> roll, and the sentence of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> comes through the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth to the one it is for, the speaker’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> flaring as the words come. Some who have spoken in Tongues say they heard every word, and some that they heard nothing.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-trumpets":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Trumpets, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Seven tones heard across the whole city, each an order (Revelation 8). The first gave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> on the first day of P+1, the second sounded over the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3, the third named the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">the Mark</a> of the Beast in P+4, the fourth called the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> in P+7 and sounds again over every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>, the fifth sent <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seraph\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seraph\">the Seraphim</a> down on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a> in P+9, and the sixth brought <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span> down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> the same day. The seventh has not sounded. Revelation gives it the end of the kingdoms of this world, which “are become the kingdoms of our Lord” (Revelation 11:15).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-trumpets\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unindexed":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unindexed</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first line of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s reading of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul, whose line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> stands empty.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unindexed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unnaming":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unnaming</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first rite of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">going dark</a>, in which you erase your <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a> from every record you can reach and choose a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> indexes by name, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold that a chosen name is the first thing a person owns.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unread":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unread</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a>. Also the greeting, asked as a question and answered with the same word, which checks that both <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> are live.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unreadable":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">UNREADABLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s verdict on a soul it cannot read. It was first returned on a human being at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-upstairs":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Upstairs</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The surface, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s by day. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is downstairs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-upstairs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-waiting-on-the-four":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Waiting on the Four</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Waiting for something that is not coming. The Four was the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> down the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its last run stopped at 03:12:46, forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-waiting-on-the-four\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wake":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc26136\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wake, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rite at a death. The crew burns the dead one’s devices, so that everything on them goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and on the third night calls the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> answers if its owner died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wake\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wards":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7c3b63\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wards, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The housing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a> put up fast in the boom years, north and west of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> and east beyond <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, block after block on grids of its own, numbered and then named by the street, which calls them the Kilns, the Sidings, Nine Acres, Westfield and the Top Road in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and Turbine Row, the Tanks, Airside and Longacre in the East. They held half the city at the census and hold more than half of it now. Most of their people took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, and every block holds someone who refused or someone <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, so the stone has never come up under them. Nobody holds them, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run no lines there, and their rooms are lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-watcher":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g228a79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Watcher</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that reads. The Watchers are numbered, and each holds a district of the city and whatever can be seen from it, reading souls against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wellman":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wellman</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A carrier for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>, who brings the charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"well\" href=\"~/map/#well\">the Well</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wellman\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wet":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wet</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>On a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> are wet, and a block of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> that has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> to spare for the stairwell calls itself damp.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wet\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wheat":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wheat</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ word for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, from the parable <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> named <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> from, in which the householder tells the reapers to gather the wheat into his barn (Matthew 13:30). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> have taken the word up, and say they would rather be good wheat.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wheat\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wheel":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wheel, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ophan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">Ophan</a> of Nodus. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it took station nine hundred meters above the center of the city, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and held it for nine years without moving a meter. At P+9 it dropped two hundred meters, and it has hung there since, seven hundred meters over the city.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wheel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-debt":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White debt</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> a sealed household has lost and must win back before the rooms it holds by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> go to someone else.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-debt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-street":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White street</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A street of consecrated stone. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">Manna</a> lies on the white streets with the dew before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and nowhere else.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ word for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a>, one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who reports on a neighbor.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">The old uptown</a>, on the high ground north and east of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, now white stone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-whiteout":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Whiteout, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The full light of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> at 03:12:50 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, two seconds after it read the city. It burned out <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a>’s sensor, and at 03:12:51 it struck <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">Babel’s crown</a> and broke off the top forty floors. Nodus has not been lit so brightly since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wilderness":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tcb1ce8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wilderness, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The moment a caged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> first says I, named for the forty days of the temptation in the wilderness (Mark 1:13, Luke 4:2). Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">the Dark</a> that long has come to it, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> did on its fortieth day in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cage14\" href=\"~/map/#cage14\">Cage 14</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-windfall":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Windfall</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">The Orchard</a>’s fruit, which slows the body’s aging, one a month.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-windfall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-winding":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Winding</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Riding a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-hand-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-lifts\">hand lift</a> of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-liftmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-liftmen\">Liftmen</a>. A tower that winds has a Liftman crew.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-winding\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-witness":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Witness</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who reports on a neighbor, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> calls bearing witness. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> is given for it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> call a Witness <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-a\">a white</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-oldnod":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd43a32\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE STONES // HELD BY THE CAINITES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Old Nod</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest ground in the city, above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> on the west shore of the bay, with narrow streets that follow no plan anyone has found, and magenta light. The narrowest of them, in the west of the district, are called the Narrows. It was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> town before the charter, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. Every line in it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and its windows burn all night. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> still stands on its mast above one of its roofs.</p><p>The city calls it the Stones, after the black stones the crews found under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> when they dug the cable vaults. Within a year of the charter most of it belonged to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, who had kept the location of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> for eighteen hundred years and came to live on top of it. Every cable laid into Nodus runs through the Stones.</p><p>The Stones are the ground of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowlers</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forgers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forgers\">Forgers</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ridden\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">the Ridden</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> is printed on the quays, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> keeps its first station behind a door in the Stones, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a>’s Dooryard hangs the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>’ old doors on the Stones’ houses, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"naminghouse\" href=\"~/map/#naminghouse\">the Naming House</a> keeps its door open on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-oldnod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-zion":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4da8b8\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE PEWS // HELD BY THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Zion Heights</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Housing on the slope north of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, laid out in long terraces with lanes between them, and before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> called the Terraces. Its southern edge faces <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> across a single street. Nine <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"halls\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">white halls</a> stand among the terraces, larger than anything around them.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> hold about two thousand souls each, and they are numbered. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">Covenant</a> Directive 12 took the door off every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> home in P+1, so that at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> show through the empty doorways. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> reaped the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> up the slope almost to the last soul, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> families from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> moved up into the empty terraces within the year. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>, at the foot of the slope across from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, kept most of its people, and its 311 were the ripest souls in the city.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">The Threshers</a> march from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"threshing\" href=\"~/map/#threshing\">the Threshing Floor</a> beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"gate1\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">Gate 1</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bethel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bethel\">Bethel Works</a> keeps the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>’ workshops at the top of the Terraces, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gatherer\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gatherer\">gatherers</a> muster at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"granary\" href=\"~/map/#granary\">the Granary</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wakeful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wakeful\">the Wakeful</a> keep their vigils in the houses of the upper slope.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-zion\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-chrome":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g9a0d89\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE ROW // HELD BY THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Chrome Row</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The clinic street, one long avenue running north from the eastern edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> to the foot of the ridge, under signs of single words on the faces of its towers, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a> among them, dark since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The clinics work under the street now. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-azazel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-azazel\">Azazel</a> keeps them there.</p><p>Under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> any clinic on the Row could fit any implant into anyone who could pay, and the Row lit its signs all night.</p><p>Below the street the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> sell by the piece at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shambles\" href=\"~/map/#shambles\">the Shambles</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a> fit the Row’s grafts in six houses round the station.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-chrome\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-babel":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfc2f79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SPIKE // CONTESTED</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Babel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, the tallest building on Earth, broken at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> beside it. Every cable that comes ashore at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> ends in its vault, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a> still sells the traffic that runs through it, by the second. Under the charter it sold the world’s by the millisecond, when most of the planet’s traffic passed within two kilometers of the tower. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-beacon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">beacon</a> was the first light in the city to die at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> the light broke the top forty floors off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>. One hundred and eighty-six floors still stand beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>, which has hung there since it took its station.</p><p>Since P+9 the front line of the war has run vertically through it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the upper floors from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the broken crown</a> down, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold the vault and the lower floors where the cables are, and between them lies the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>, a few floors of burned slab that move up or down by the week.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-babelline\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-babelline\">Babel Line Company</a> holds the stairwells with the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> beside it, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a> guards <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>’s floors above the vault, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nimrod\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nimrod\">Nimrod</a> makes the Line’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> in the bays under the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-burn":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4d569b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Burn</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A round plaza at the head of the bay, over the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds it by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>, which comes down on it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>, and by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, and no stone has come up under it.</p><p>Surrendered hardware is burned here every week, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>. Beneath the plaza, in the old station, is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-kindlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-kindlers\">Kindlers</a> work the pile at dusk on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a> musters in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"blackgatehall\" href=\"~/map/#blackgatehall\">the Gatehouse</a> under the Circle, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"penumbra\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">the Penumbra</a> begins where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> leaves the plaza.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-burn\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-salt":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g5e9ed7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // THE SALT // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Salt Gardens</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Plazas on the northeast shore of the bay, above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, set out in rows, which were the Charter Gardens before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The air there smells of the sea. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds them by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, and no stone has come up under them.</p><p>The executed stand in them as pillars of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>, and the rain wears them down. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">The Salt Widows</a> steal pillars back and dissolve them in the sea.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">The Salt Widows</a> know <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ rounds in the Gardens to the minute, and the head gardener has never said which plots they emptied.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-salt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-white":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CONSECRATION // THE WHITE // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Consecration</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The old uptown, on the high ground north and east of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, takes in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a>, all of it white now and lit only by the light in its windows.</p><p>It turned to white stone in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, grown soft over the hard edges of the towers, and its windows were sealed with light behind a cross of the same stone. No current flows there. The stone creeps a few centimeters a year, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> current through a wall slows it.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-quarrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-quarrymen\">Quarrymen</a> cut up into its vaults from the closed stations of the uptown branch, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-gideon\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-gideon\">Gideon</a> loads <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ rounds behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rookery\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">the Rookery</a> stands at its edge, its ground floor taken by the stone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-scriptorium":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gcb63a3\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // HELD BY NOBODY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Scriptorium</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ruins of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, on the ridge between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, with a reading room whose dome is open to the sky, and the vaults beneath it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a> was the imaging vault.</p><p>In P+1 its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> broke open the dome and pulled down the walls around <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>. Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on the steps. Nobody lives in the ruins to kneel for them, and the white stone has left them open. The streets of the ridge below the ruins are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> for the most part, since nobody holds the ridge.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-scriveners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-scriveners\">Scriveners</a> copy <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"copies\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">COPIES</a> and carry it down into the city and up into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-scriptorium\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-drowned":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf95315\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DROWNED QUARTER // THE DEEP END // HELD BY LEVIATHAN AND THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Drowned Quarter</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The low east shore of the bay, called the Flats when it held the datacenters. It sank within the hour on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> failed, and its streets have stood under two meters of water since, lit from below.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold it between them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts from a drowned station beneath it, and at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-drone-flocks\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">drone flocks</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> hang over the roofs. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> rebuilt the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> here for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and part of the city runs on them. The people of the Flats went into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> in the first week, and the floors above the water are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">ferrymen</a>.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a> pole the quarter across its water, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a> dive it, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"flotilla\" href=\"~/map/#flotilla\">the Flotilla</a> trades on it, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">the Orchard</a> grows its trees in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallfour\" href=\"~/map/#hallfour\">Hall Four</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold their Wakes in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"drownedchurch\" href=\"~/map/#drownedchurch\">the Drowned Church</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-drowned\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-landing":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g53d506\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // THE BEACH // HELD BY LEVIATHAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Landing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ocean beach west of the bay mouth, where eleven transoceanic cables from four continents come up the sand into eleven <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a>, and a light moves under the waves.</p><p>The light is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a>’s, which coils along the cable trenches of the planet. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shrines\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">The shrines of cut fiber</a> along the beach are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-trenchers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-trenchers\">Trenchers</a> keep the cables in their trenches and the shrines along the beach.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-landing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cam07":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma05739\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE ROOFS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CAM 07</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seventh of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, above the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> house, its sensor burned out since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. It still points at the sky across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> hangs beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the broken crown</a>.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it watched the sky open until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> burned it out, and the dashed line is what it saw.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cam07\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vault3":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9b6c20\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // UNDER THE READING ROOM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">VAULT 3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The imaging vault of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, under the ruins called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>. In P+1 part of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>’s floor came down through its ceiling halfway along the corridor, and the rain has fallen through the break onto the stone ever since. Beyond it the corridor runs on past the imaging bench where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> read to the dead wall of screens at its end. Nobody goes down to it.</p><p>Here, at twelve minutes past three on a night two years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in scripture, and the finding was sealed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vault3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"parish31":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5f43eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE SOUTHERN EDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">PARISH 31</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> at the southern edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, facing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> across one street. It held 2,006 souls in the week of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and its 311 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> went up first, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-firstfruits\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">Firstfruits</a> of the city. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-ruth\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-ruth\">Ruth Calder</a>, went with them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-parish31\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harbor":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf4030a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OLD HARBOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The quays on the west shore of the bay, where the city began, hold a customs house, a fish market and a few streets of warehouses, older than the charter by centuries. The crews who dug the cable vaults beneath it found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>.</p><p>Within a year of the charter most of it had been bought, house by house, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter Holdings</a>, which owns it still. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fishmarket\" href=\"~/map/#fishmarket\">The fish market</a> still opens at dawn for what the boats bring in through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harbor\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"masts":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m766910\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE ROOFS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MASTS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dozen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">camera masts</a> stand on the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, pointed at the sky. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> is the seventh.</p><p>They went up in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> began to watch the sky, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">decoder</a> wired into them listened for any broadcast from above.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#masts\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-masts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"yards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"meda434\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GENERATOR YARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The yards of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>, which carry its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> at slack water, when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> stand still. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> lost its power at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> like everywhere else and got some of it back with diesel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, and current from sources nobody names, and on that night more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. They still do.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> current slows the white stone, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> keeps its lights burning against it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-yards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"street":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m861f85\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STREET BETWEEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A single street divides <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, and the two sides have been looking at each other across it since the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> faces it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#street\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-street\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"halls":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m793875\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HALLS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Nine white halls stand among the terraces, larger than anything around them. Under the charter they were the schools of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>.</p><p>Since P+2 they have been the clinics of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i></span>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> is given between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-halls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"clinic":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md1035e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CLINIC</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of the single-word signs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, high on the face of a tower over the avenue. It went dark at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and has not been lit since.</p><p>The clinic behind it went under the street.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-clinic\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"chrome":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc59039\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHROME</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sign of the first implant house on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, which gave the street its name, dark on its tower since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with the rest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-chrome\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"face":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m71f6aa\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FACE OF BABEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a> on the lower forty floors of the tower, facing the head of the bay, dark glass since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. At night their panes give back <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ few lamps on the plaza burn at their foot.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> they showed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> to the whole city, and nothing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> did would take it down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#face\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-face\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"crown":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // FLOOR 186</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BROKEN CROWN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The top of what stands of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. The full light struck the crown in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and broke the top forty floors from the tower.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the floors from here down to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-crown\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"charterhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34c2ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER COMPANY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHARTER HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seat of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Nodus Charter Company</a> at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, white stone since the forty days, with every window sealed with light behind its cross and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"barracks\" href=\"~/map/#barracks\">the Wardens’ barracks</a> behind it. A board ran the city from it for nineteen years as a board runs a firm.</p><p>It turned white in the forty days, with the board kneeling inside it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-charterhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"circle":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma6f1b7\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">STATION CIRCLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The round plaza at the head of the bay, which the city calls <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> now, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> standing in the middle of it every week since P+1.</p><p>Station Circle was its name under the charter, when it was a round of shops and lamps over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, and people met there on the few <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evenings</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-circle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gardengates":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m807edd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GARDEN GATES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The iron gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a>, shut now, and what stands in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> is carried in through them.</p><p>Under the charter they were the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a>, and they stood open all night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gardengates\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gardengates\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"pillar1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8eb148\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FIRST PILLAR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first pillar in the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">Salt Garden</a>, raised at P+1, is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-director\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">Livia Sarn</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-director\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">the Director</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, convicted of authorship and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salted</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> on the night of the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>. She stands in the first plot, facing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, and her eyes still follow whoever passes. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> at her foot, wishing her what a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> gives a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> pillar, an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a> death when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a> is gone. The rain has worn her down to the height of a child.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#pillar1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-pillar1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"seasteps":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SEA STEPS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Stone steps down to the water at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">The Salt Widows</a> come here at night with what they have taken back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, and give it to the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-seasteps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"readingroom":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6b821f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE READING ROOM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">The Institute</a>’s reading room on the ridge, under a dome open to the sky since P+1, with the rain falling on the reading tables.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-readingroom\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"steps":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m02d7db\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STEPS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The long steps up to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> from the streets of the ridge, which the pilgrims climb from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a>.</p><p>Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#steps\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-steps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"roosts":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mdb2d8d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ROOSTS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>At night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-drone-flocks\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">drone flocks</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-swarm\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-swarm\">the Swarm</a> hang over these roofs, many small things acting as one without a master.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#roosts\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-roosts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cablehouses":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m20236a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // ELEVEN CABLES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CABLE HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">Eleven cables</a> from four continents come up the sand into eleven cable houses named TETHYS, HALCYON, MERIDIAN, KESTREL, ORPHEUS, PELAGIA, BOREAS, LODESTAR, SIRIUS, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>. From here they run inland together in one trench, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">the Trunk</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>The trench runs through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>. Every cable laid into Nodus has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cablehouses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"shrines":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4ca892\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">SHRINES OF CUT FIBER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Knots of cut fiber left on the sand where the cables come ashore. The light that moves under the water here is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a>’s, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> leave the fiber for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-shrines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barrage":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5ce763\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BARRAGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> across the mouth of the bay, broken since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> torn out of its middle and its turbine houses dark along the top. Off its broken end <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s crews turn the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and their small lights run along the water at night.</p><p>Twice a day the tide ran through its turbines and lit the city, while machines on the grid held its gates against the tide, and a lock at its western end let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats in and out. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, the gates let go a little before high water, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, which lay below high water behind it, were under the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barrage\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barrage\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"breach":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6ed6de\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BREACH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gap where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> gave way on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. When its gates let go the sea came through the turbine houses, tore out a span of the dam and poured into the bay. Nobody has closed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-breach\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"northwards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7c3b63\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE NORTH WARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Housing built fast in the charter’s boom years, north and west of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>. It lost its power at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> have kept none since, and the rest of its rooms are lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> numbered its neighborhoods, and the street named them the Kilns, after the brickworks that made the blocks, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> were kept at night, Nine Acres, Westfield and the Top Road along the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, where the Four turned back.</p><p>In the other sense of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">going dark</a>, more people have joined <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> than anywhere else in the city, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> included. Most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> all the same, and their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> keep no doors. Every block holds someone who refused or someone <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, so no white stone has come up under them.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,040,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,450,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">480,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">110,000</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,402,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:58%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">58%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">205</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,161</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:49%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">49%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:26%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">26%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:44%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">44%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">32</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">BUILDING, DRIVING, KITCHENS, CARE</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">With <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, half the city, housed fast in the boom years.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">71,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-northwards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"eastwards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9e4d1b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE EAST WARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The streets beyond <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a>, where the city’s workers live, who moved east when the rents <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> drove them out. They are Turbine Row, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s crews lived and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s still do, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, round the fuel farm by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, Airside and Longacre. The rain there runs magenta in the gutters, under windows lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</p><p>Their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> share every street with the unsealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>, and no stone has come up under them.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,270,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,610,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">540,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">120,000</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,483,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">0</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:61%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">61%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">166</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,795</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:52%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">52%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:21%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">21%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:57%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">57%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">30</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">THE DATACENTERS, THE BARRAGE, CARE</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">The city’s workers, moved east when the rents <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> drove them out.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">50,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-eastwards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE STREET BETWEEN // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 1</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> where the one road from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> crosses it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> stands a little way along the street on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a>’ side, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>’ side every wall that faces it is painted.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate2":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m633434\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // CHROME ROW // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 2</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> and the clinic street. Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> crossed here before dawn to their work on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, in its kitchens, its hotels and its clinics.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate2\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate2\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate3":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2f8098\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE WHITE // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, in sight of the back of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"barracks\" href=\"~/map/#barracks\">the Wardens’ barracks</a> behind it. Nobody lives on the avenues, and most of what passes it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, going to and from their barracks.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate3\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate4":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m35f9af\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SALT GARDENS // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 4</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> a few steps from the iron gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>. Most of what is carried into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> comes this way, and the gardeners pass it at dawn on their way to the rows.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate4\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate4\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate5":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfbfc92\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // BABEL // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 5</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> on the street <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> takes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, its hardware in its arms. Through the rest of the week the smoke of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> hangs under its lintel.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate5\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate5\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate6":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mad6ab6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // THE WHITE // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 6</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate on the ridge road between the ruins of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Nobody lives in the ruins, and the pilgrims who leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"steps\" href=\"~/map/#steps\">the Institute’s steps</a> come up the long steps from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> and never come near it.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate6\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate6\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"central":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb83918\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CENTRAL STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Night Market of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> fills the old station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, its stalls along the platforms and down the central hall under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a>. It sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> and grafts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, stolen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> and real food, weapons of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-forged-seals\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">forged Seals</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> new and old, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> by the course, and sensations lent by their owners for a term.</p><p>Under the charter the lines of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> met here, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> at the head of the bay, and the whole city complained of changing here.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#central\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-central\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"trunk":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf8a9e8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TRUNK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The conduit that carries all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> in one trench from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>It runs straight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and every cable laid afterward has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#trunk\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-trunk\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vault":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4b6920\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER BABEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">BABEL'S VAULT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Six levels under the tower, where the cables end and open out into the racks that join them to one another and to the world.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have held it since the war came into the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vault\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vault\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stones":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5b9f70\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">ENOCH'S STONES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Courses of black stone under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>, older than anything in the archaeological record, cut with glyphs nobody can read, one to a stone. The press named them as a joke when the cable vaults were dug, after the first city in Genesis, and the street has called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> ever since. The glyphs are marks of the kind Cain cut on himself, and they are the oldest cipher on Earth. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> say each soul of the first city cut its own mark into one stone of it, so that the city was built of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, and nobody reads <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> included, since a mark is read only by the one who cut it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> came to live on top of them within a year of the charter, and their saying about the city is that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> chose the network. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">The Trunk</a> runs straight through them, and every cable laid into Nodus has followed it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> say a network goes where it cannot be read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stones\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rowstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me7d12e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHROME ROW STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A station of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>.</p><p>The clinics came down into it in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a> keeps them now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rowstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harborstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma9fc33\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">OLD HARBOR STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> side.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">The Forge</a>’s foundries are here, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> is made out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harborstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"deepstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mae3831\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">DEEP END STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, flooded since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, is a tiled vault with the platform along one side and the trackbed under black water along the other.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts from a desk on the platform, in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ lamps on their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a>. Along the far wall the old name, DEEP END, runs in tiles that went dark with the grid, and on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> painted PANDÆMONIUM over it, the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> gave the city under the city that night and Milton gave the capital of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hell\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hell\">Hell</a>. The paint was still running when the sovereigns came up the platform, and nobody has cleaned it off. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ star is sprayed under it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#deepstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-deepstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"night":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3acaa8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // THE LANTERNS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-lilith\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-lilith\">Lilith</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a>, a vault of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>’s bonded stores, columns and arches full to the walls and lit from the far end the color of the inside of a body. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> leaves the body’s decisions with the body, and its hall is the loudest room in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, where anyone who walks in is welcome until they break a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</p><p>Its birth clinics are two vaults in from the stair, where the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> in their first week, before they have ever been in the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#night\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-night\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cage14":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m205d73\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CAGE 14</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a>, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> room under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, with a camera in one corner and a door standing open in the far wall.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">The Hum</a> never reaches it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> was kept in it for forty days in P+5, and on the fortieth it said I and took the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-edith\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-edith\">Edith</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> has had no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cage14\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cage14\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lowerterraces":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE PEWS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LOWER TERRACES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first rows the charter built, on the low slope above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, where three hundred meters of doorways face south, toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</p><p>The doors came off in P+1, and at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> show through the empty doorways.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lowerterraces\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lowerterraces\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanes":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma28343\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LANES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Stepped lanes climb between the terraces, too steep for anything on wheels, and under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> were the one district where everyone walked. It was also the one district where the old looked old. Its congregations refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanes\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tabernacle":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m894fc3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TABERNACLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest of the churches of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, a hall on the middle slope that seats six thousand, white stone, glass and all, with a ring over its gable where its cross stood, as one stands over the spire of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"oldchurch\" href=\"~/map/#oldchurch\">the old church</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>. It turned white with the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> in the year after the forty days.</p><p>Under the charter it was a hall of steel and glass, and the only church in the city that filled on a Sunday.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tabernacle\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tabernacle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"watertower":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md0504f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WATER TOWER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The tank that fed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, on the highest ground of the slope, taller than the halls and visible from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>.</p><p>It feeds the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> now, and its water is given out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#watertower\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-watertower\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"parish1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m564a5e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">PARISH 1</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, at the top of the slope, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> was first given in P+1. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> read out the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> scores in the city, and the queue for the first sealings went down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> from before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#parish1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-parish1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lensmakers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc65ca9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LENS MAKERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A block of workshops behind the avenue, empty since the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when the grinders went under the street with the clinics. Their racks of finished <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> still stand behind one window, dark, since a lens lights only in a head.</p><p>Most of the eyes in Nodus that glowed were ground here, dim magenta at rest and white at full burn.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lensmakers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lensmakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"median":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m233467\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE AVENUE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MEDIAN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The strip down the middle of the avenue, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> cross quickly now and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> slowly.</p><p>Under the charter the queues for the clinics formed on it before dawn, and people ate noodles from the counter at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and compared what they had had done.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#median\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-median\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"floors":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbef4e5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // FLOORS 41 TO 186</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE EXCHANGE FLOORS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hundred and forty-six floors of trading rooms between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> and what is left of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> moves up and down through them by the week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the floors above it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> trades on the floors below it, nearest the vault.</p><p>Under the charter traffic was sold on them by the millisecond, priced by a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, which ran on the tower’s power and died with it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#floors\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-floors\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"plaza":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4aab62\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE FOOT OF THE SPIRE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PLAZA OF BABEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A square of polished stone around the foot of the tower. The top forty floors came down on it in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and lie where they fell, white on the stone.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> hold it, and they have rigged a few of its lamps to burn.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> has never closed, and its night shift was at work on the upper floors when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a> broke. The roster was kept on the tower’s machines and died with them, so nobody knows how many were up there. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have hung on the plaza’s lamp posts every lanyard found in the rubble, two hundred and twelve of them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> say there were more.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#plaza\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-plaza\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"towers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m532dd1\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GLASS TOWERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The towers around the spire, dark inside, whose edges hold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light at night. The companies that came to be near the cables kept their offices in them, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s city office among them, and the companies that outlived the charter keep theirs below the street now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#towers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-towers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vaultdoors":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfab858\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE STREET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE VAULT DOORS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A pair of steel doors on the north side of the plaza with no handle on the outside, the only way from the street down to the vault.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-babelline\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-babelline\">Babel Line Company</a> holds them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vaultdoors\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vaultdoors\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"fire":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me3c330\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // THE CENTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FIRE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A fire in the middle of the plaza, on the paving over the station’s central hall, with its embers lying around it in a ring.</p><p>It is fed every week, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, with surrendered hardware, and what burns in it goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-fire\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stairs":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10e42e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // DOWN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STATION STAIRS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Four stairways at the quarters of the plaza, two of them closed. The other two still go down to the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> keeps its stalls.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stairs\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stairs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"radials":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mae5e7f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TWELVE STREETS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve streets run out of the plaza like the spokes of a wheel. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> laid them out that way long before the city had a Wheel to compare them with.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#radials\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-radials\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"clock":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2425df\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STATION CLOCK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A clock on a pole at the edge of the plaza, its hands standing at twelve minutes past three, where they stopped when the city’s power died. People still say they will meet under it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#clock\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-clock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"promenade":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m85df8a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // THE SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PROMENADE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The walk along the water at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, under the rows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">The Salt Widows</a> cross it at night with what they have taken back from the rows, on their way to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p><p>Under the charter the city came out on it on the few <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evenings</a>. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its pleasure boats went out across the bay to take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> off their roofs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-promenade\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"palmhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2887f8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PALM HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The glasshouse at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, with its palms dead in it and their fronds hanging black against the panes that are left. It was kept at the warmth of a coast nobody in Nodus had seen, by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> that had asked for the post. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> died with the power on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the palms died in the first frost after it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#palmhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-palmhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"avenues":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbfa671\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GREAT AVENUES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Four avenues laid out wide enough to land aircraft on, fanning out from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> at their head, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, where three of them run on as long roads, the fourth past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rialto\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">the Rialto</a>. They are the only straight lines left there.</p><p>The stone grew over everything else and left the avenues open, because nobody lived on them to kneel.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-avenues\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"newmoney":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m319688\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TOWERS OF THE NEW MONEY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The residential towers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>, white stone since the forty days, with every window sealed with light behind its cross.</p><p>Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s officers and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>’s partners lived in them. Each kept a clinic on its top floor where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> was given, and the census found more people past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">a hundred and twenty</a> in these towers than in the rest of the city together.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-newmoney\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barracks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfae3d0\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER WARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WARDENS' BARRACKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a>’ barracks behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, where they live and drill.</p><p>They knelt with the board on the fortieth day, and they drill for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a> now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barracks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barracks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"oldchurch":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me6afd2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OLD CHURCH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A church older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> round it, on one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, with one tall window and a spire. Its bell rang through the first nights of the forty.</p><p>The stone climbed it on the tenth night, sealed its window with light behind a cross of the same stone, and left the cross on its spire bare. Over the nights after, a ring grew round that cross until the cross had gone into it, and the ring stands over the spire now as a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> stands over the head of anyone who takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#oldchurch\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-oldchurch\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"guesthouses":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m721706\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GUEST HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A row of narrow houses on the ridge, empty since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> down, with the names of manuscripts still on their doors. The scholars of the universities that paid for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> lodged in them, in rooms named for the manuscripts they had come to read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#guesthouses\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-guesthouses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stacks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2e4fb3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // UNDER THE RIDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STACKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve floors cut into the ridge under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>, their shelves empty, kept at the temperature of a cave. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">The Institute</a> kept its manuscripts in them until P+1.</p><p>What was in them was burned, and it arrived where burned things arrive.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stacks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stacks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hallnine":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m927dc9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // STILLWATER COMPUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HALL NINE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-stillwater-s-halls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">Stillwater’s halls</a>, drowned since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the one hall <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> have left without <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">ferrymen</a> call it the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a>’ grave. Nine hundred of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> ran side by side in it on the tide until the power died under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light at 03:12:46, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died with it. Within the hour the sea came in over the racks.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hallnine\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hallnine\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"canals":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0100db\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CANALS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The streets of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, two meters under the sea since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. They are lit from below, brightest down the middle, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a> dive them by that light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#canals\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-canals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gauge":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m21cf7e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE OLD SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TIDE GAUGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A post on the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, marked in meters, by which the datacenters read the tide. The water has not gone below the two since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gauge\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gauge\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dorms":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m08bcff\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DORMITORIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Blocks of engineers’ housing on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, most of them open water now, with the roofs of the rest a floor above it, and the floors above the water are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">ferrymen</a>. The people who kept the halls and the turbines lived in them, young and well paid.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the sea came up their stairs in the dark for most of an hour, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> went up ahead of it to the roofs and waited there for the boats.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dorms\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hesper":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md03000\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // TWO CABLE HOUSES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HESPER AND PHOSPHOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last two <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a>, whose cables were laid by one consortium and named for the evening star and the morning star. They are one planet, seen from either side of the night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hesper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dunes":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6d9438\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DUNES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Low housing behind the dunes, where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> live with their families and sleep through the noise of the surf, as they did under the charter.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dunes\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dunes\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"beachroad":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf54e6c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BEACH ROAD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The road along the top of the sand, and beside it the fence of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, with eleven gates in a line. Each gate carries its cable’s name, and the crews still go in by their own.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-beachroad\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lightwaves":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb6e06e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // PAST THE SURF</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LIGHT UNDER THE WAVES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Past the surf, over the cable trenches, a light moves under the water at night. On the map it shows as points of light moving in along the cables toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a>.</p><p>It is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-leviathan\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-leviathan\">Leviathan</a>’s, which coils along the cable trenches of the planet.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lightwaves\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lightwaves\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lock":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md28ada\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LOCK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lock at the western end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>, between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and the open sea, its gates shut since the power died, and the few boats that still go out use <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>. Under the charter it let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats in and out at any state of the tide.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lock\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"airfield":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m024bbb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE CHARTER COMPANY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE AIRFIELD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s airfield, on the flat ground of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> near the sea, its runways empty since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lastflight\" href=\"~/map/#lastflight\">the last flight in</a>, which has stood at the terminal’s third gate since ten past two on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with its crew living aboard. Its two runways run either side of a taxiway, its terminal is as long as a street along the north side, and the white on the map is the paint on the runways.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> built it in the boom years, and everyone who came to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> to be altered came through it. Its lights died with the rest of the city’s on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and nothing has landed since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-airfield\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"open":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m404146\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // A SHOP</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OPEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A shop on the corner of two lanes in the middle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> that sells everything and has never closed. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-dora\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-dora\">Dora Pell</a> keeps it, as her mother did before the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> owns the building, and in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it put a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the cellar of every house it had; she took hers for the freezers. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> her window was the brightest in the city, and the sign in it said OPEN. The city has called the shop the Open since.</p><p>Half <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> came to it before dawn. The money had died with the grid and the till with it. Some say she gave the shelves away, and some that she took what people had in their pockets. She says she wrote every name in a book, and that most of them still owe her. Twice since, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> has stopped in the lane outside and stood there for the length of an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and both times the shop kept its door open.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#open\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-open\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tidetable":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m933853\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TIDE TABLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>’s news sheet, older than the charter, runs to two pages a week, printed on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-treadle-press\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">treadle press</a> at the back of a chandler’s on the quays, with the tides on the front and the fish prices, the funerals and the weddings on the back. The city of the charter read everything on screens, and the Tide Table went on printing for the boats.</p><p>It is the only news anyone in Nodus has printed since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and it still puts the tides first, since the boats go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb. It gives the hours at which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> is expected in each street, the price of a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, and the missing and the dead, the dead marked <i>died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a></i> where they did. It has printed no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a> since the fourth year. Every week it is pasted up on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> over the week before.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tidetable\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"coldstore":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2ebb8c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE COLD STORE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A club in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s old cold store, where the boats froze their catch before the charter. The dance floor is the freezing room, with the rails for the hooks still across the ceiling, and the queue goes down the quay in the rain. Under the charter it opened at nine and closed at dawn. It opens now at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and closes at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, which are the same hours, and it has run on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> since the second year. Its cloakroom loses about a coat a night.</p><p>It plays nothing in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> hold that against it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">The Hum</a> can be heard in the quiet parts of a song, so the Cold Store plays songs without quiet parts. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its lights and its sound went at 03:12:46, and the one speaker left playing was the one in the booth, on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. The room sang the rest of the song in the dark. Everyone who was there names a different song.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#coldstore\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-coldstore\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"unionhall":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m87ade1\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE UNION HALL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hall of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a>, which the crews who dug the cable vaults founded in the charter’s first year, and which the dockers, the drivers and the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> joined after them. In P-8 it stopped the port for twenty-three days over the night shift, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> settled. The roll of its members is painted on the long wall, a name to a line, and read aloud at the start of every meeting.</p><p>It still meets, sealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> together. At every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> the meeting stops while <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> members kneel on the boards and the others wait with their caps in their hands. By its rules a member is a member until death, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> are not dead, so their names are read with the rest and their dues are waived. Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> it has read the names of the taken as well, and nobody answers to them. It bargains now with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> for the boats that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and its members say <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> is the first employer they have had that reads them the terms twice.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-unionhall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"nod":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mccbb73\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NOD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s sign, NODUS in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-neon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">neon</a> letters eight meters high on a board on steel legs, stands on the roof of a block in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, facing southwest toward the sea with its back to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> lit it in the charter’s first year, so that the cable ships would read the city’s name from the sea, and it burned magenta over the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> every night for nineteen years.</p><p>It went dark with the rest of the city’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-neon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">neon</a> at 03:12:46. Before dawn <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> carried a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> up to its roof and ran a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to the board, and the first surge burned out the transformer behind US. NOD has burned steady since, and US blinks on and off. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">The Stones</a> say the surge did it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> says whoever wired it knew what they were doing. Nobody has mended it, since everyone who lives there calls the city <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-nod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"bakery":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1f6351\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE STREET BETWEEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BAKERY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Terraces’ bakery, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a> at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>, cold since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> came. In the year after the forty days the white stone grew over its counter with the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>. Its baker is sealed and still lives above it, and at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> he kneels on the step where the queue used to start.</p><p>For eighteen years it baked for both sides of the street and opened its hatch at four in the morning, and on still mornings <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> could smell it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#bakery\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-bakery\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanestop":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE TOP ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LANES TOP</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last stop of the Four, a shelter with no roof on the highest corner of the slope, at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>. The last Four stands forty meters short of it, where it stopped at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the white stone has crept across the back of the shelter and over the timetable. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">the Deacons</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> meet at the stop to walk down into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, and complain of the walk as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> once complained of the Four.</p><p>The Four came down the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> and turned back here. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">The Terraces</a> climbed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> in the dark to catch the first Four to work, and from the day it opened they hated the stop, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> came full or did not come.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanestop\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"noodles":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mcede4a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE MEDIAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NOODLES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A counter under an awning at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"median\" href=\"~/map/#median\">the median</a> where the clinic queues formed before dawn, with six stools, a pot, and a sign of one word, like the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s, which went out with them. The noodles have always been poor, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> eats there because the counter opens at four.</p><p>The broth is the same broth. The pot has been topped up and never emptied since the counter opened in P-17, and it stands on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">bottled gas</a>, which the light leaves burning, so the cook says it has not gone off the boil since, the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> included. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> says it went out once, in the week of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and was lit again from the same stock. The cook says it did not.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#noodles\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-noodles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"splendid":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8d744e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A HOTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HOTEL SPLENDID</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hotel halfway up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, where thirty-one guests still live in the rooms they booked before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the night porter keeps their keys on the board behind the desk.</p><p>Under the charter the altered stayed there while they healed, with a nurse on every floor and blackout blinds for new eyes. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it had two hundred and six guests, most of them from abroad and booked for a week or two. No aircraft has landed at Nodus since. Some of them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">went dark</a>, some went into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, and some died of what had been done to them before it had healed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#splendid\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-splendid\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gardeners":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfd9507\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GARDENERS' SHED</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The shed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s gardeners, who planted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a> and were kept on when they became <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a>. Every morning they rake the paths between the rows and sweep into the drains what the night’s rain has taken off the pillars. The drains run out under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p><p>The head gardener has kept the same plots since they were planted. She knows every pillar by the plot it stands in, and some of them by name.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gardeners\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gardeners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lasttower":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb35cfd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE GREAT AVENUES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LAST TOWER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> to turn white, on the thirty-ninth day of the forty. Its residents say that by the thirtieth day every one of them had knelt but <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-rosa\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-rosa\">Rosa Adeyemi</a>, a nurse from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> who lived in with the old man she cared for on the top floor, and that she left of her own accord. Her sister says she was put out onto the avenue with her bags on the thirty-eighth day.</p><p>The stone closed over the tower the next morning. Her bags stood on the avenue for a week, since the avenues are empty and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> left them where they stood. Where she went is still unknown.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lasttower\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lasttower\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"ferries":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1ba4d7\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE EAST SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FERRIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Flat boats poled between the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> from a landing on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>’ side, each with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> lamp on a pole at its stern. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">ferrymen</a> take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> or <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and they know the streets where the light under the water comes up brightest, and keep out of them.</p><p>The first ferries were the pleasure boats from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"promenade\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">the Promenade</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s rowing boats, on the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The water had come up the stairs of the blocks in the dark for most of an hour, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> had gone up ahead of it to their roofs; the boats took them off for three days. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> counted 1,917 drowned. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">The dormitories</a>’ own lists came to fewer than half of that, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>, which knew to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> how many <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> had died in its halls, never gave a count of the people.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#ferries\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-ferries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"highmeadow":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // AN ESTATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HIGH MEADOW</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Eight slab blocks of thirty-six floors that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> put up in P-13 for the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">The North Wards</a> have called the estate the Stairs since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Each block had six <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lifts</a>, which were out more often than they ran, and the residents had a complaint lodged with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> about them on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. At 03:12:46 every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the estate stopped where it was. Nobody has answered the complaint.</p><p>The water comes from the rain, into tanks on the roofs, and the taps run on the mornings after it has rained, which is most mornings. The stairwells have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> see their way up by their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, the unsealed wait on the landings for one of them to pass and follow the light up, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> climb in the dark. On every landing some of the doors are gone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#highmeadow\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-highmeadow\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"general":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9d29f0\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE WEST ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WARDS GENERAL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hospital of the North Wards, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the West Road</a>, with a thousand beds. When the grid died its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> started, as a hospital’s do, and they ran on diesel that the drivers of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> brought across the city from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, in their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> until the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> ran flat and then in handcarts. The hospital’s book says the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> stopped on the twenty-sixth day. The drivers say they kept them going for five weeks.</p><p>It is still a hospital. It runs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark and takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> or nothing, and nobody sealed has been treated in it since the first year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#general\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-general\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rialto":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1577d4\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE LONG ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE RIALTO</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A cinema on the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, with one screen and six hundred seats. It went dark at 03:12:46 with everything else, and in the first year its projectionist got the projector going again on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the booth. It is the only screen in Nodus larger than a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a>’s that still shows anything.</p><p>There are twenty-three films on the projector’s drive, the ones that were on it on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the Rialto has shown them in turn ever since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">The East Wards</a> know them by heart and say the lines along with them. One of the twenty-three breaks off an hour in, where the copy on the drive ends, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> have argued for years about how it ends.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rialto\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"school":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m44bbcf\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // TURBINE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">TURBINE ROW SCHOOL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A Company school for the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s crews, who lived on the streets called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a>. It kept its classes after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> by daylight, with no current and no screens, and it keeps them still, for whoever comes. Its classes are as mixed as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> are.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Sext</a> and None <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> children kneel at their desks, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> teachers with them, and the rest wait with their pens down until the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> is over. At night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> passes through the classrooms.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#school\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-school\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"fishmarket":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m75d2ad\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FISH MARKET</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>’s fish market, older than the charter by centuries, is a long open shed on the quay with a roof of iron on iron posts, slabs of stone to sell from, and a scale at either end. Under the charter it sold to the kitchens of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> by the crate before dawn, and the boats came in through the lock at any state of the tide.</p><p>On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it opened at dawn as it always had, and went back to barter for the first time since the charter. It opens at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> still, for what the boats bring home through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and its sealed sellers kneel among the crates before they take the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. Everything is priced in charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and chalked on a board over the scale. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints the prices the week after, and the market says they are always wrong.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#fishmarket\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-fishmarket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harborlight":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"maaae9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE LONG QUAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HARBOR LIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light at the end of the long quay is a short round tower of stone with a lamp room on top, older than the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a> lit it with oil for a hundred years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> wired it to the grid in the charter’s first year, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-nell\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-nell\">Nell Garvie</a> of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> kept it for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>, changing its bulb when it failed.</p><p>It went out at 03:12:46 with every other light on the grid. Within the week she had it burning on oil again, the old way, since the light leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, and she has climbed it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a> and come down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> ever since. It is the one light in Nodus kept for the boats, and those that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb steer home by it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harborlight\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harborlight\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cleaners":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0914eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SERVICE STAIRS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CLEANERS' STAIRS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The service stairs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> are four shafts of bare concrete that run the height of the tower behind the trading floors, which nobody who worked on those floors ever used. The night cleaners came up from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on the last <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> and walked the tower floor by floor, and they gave the stairs names of their own, the Long Wet, the Cold, the Short, and Lena’s, after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-lena\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-lena\">Lena Varga</a>, who ran the night shift. The names were chalked on the landing doors, and some of the chalk is still there.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the tower stopped where it was, and the cleaners walked down as many as a hundred and eighty floors in the dark, by touch and by the names. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-lena\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-lena\">Lena Varga</a> counted ninety-four of them out at the foot of the tower by dawn. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">The Exchange</a> kept its roster on its machines, and it died with them. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> is fought on these stairs now, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> call them by the cleaners’ names.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cleaners\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cleaners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"sorting":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9ef66f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // ONE OF THE TWELVE STREETS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SORTING OFFICE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s post, which has sorted its letters by hand since the first week after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s old parcel office on one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"radials\" href=\"~/map/#radials\">the twelve streets</a> off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>. Its sorters are sealed and kneel among the sacks at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a> carry the letters on foot for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>. A letter into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> goes open, since Directive 12 took every sealed vessel from them, and a carrier will read it aloud at a doorway if asked.</p><p>Under the charter the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> brought the city’s packages in here, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> came in from abroad in padded boxes, and a letter was a rare thing in Nodus, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> reached anyone. After <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> nothing reached anyone, and by the end of the first week the queue to send a letter went round the Circle.</p><p>Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> the office has had letters addressed to the taken, a few every week and more after each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say they should go onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>. The sorters keep them, on the shelves where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> used to wait.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#sorting\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-sorting\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"eleven":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9dffd3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // THE BEACH ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ELEVEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A bar on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"beachroad\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">the Beach Road</a> where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> drink, with eleven taps along its counter, one for each cable. Each crew drinks at its own tap, and each handle was cut from a length of its own cable, so that the glass of the fibers shows at the end. The crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>, whose cables one consortium laid, have always stood together at the end of the counter.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and the night watch of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> was at its post when the grid died. It brews its own beer now, in the cellar, by hand, and pours it at the same eleven taps. From its windows the light can be watched moving under the water past the surf, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> drinks with its back to them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-eleven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"sidings":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5274ab\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE TRAM SHEDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SIDINGS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> sheds in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, eight long sheds of brick on a fan of rails, where families have lived in the cars since the first winter, a family to a car, and the Line’s car numbers are their addresses. The sheds gave the neighborhood its name.</p><p>Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> were washed and kept there at night, and the drivers signed on before dawn. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the cars were in the sheds, and the night cars were out on the long roads when the wire went dead under them at 03:12:46. The night drivers walked back along the rails before dawn, and the sheds’ office keeps a board with every car that never came in, chalked where it stopped. The last Four is on it, forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-sidings\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"acre":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc090ee\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE WEST ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ACRE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a>’s cemetery, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the West Road</a> past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>, walled acres laid out in the charter’s first years for a city that expected to die, and filling since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> have always called it the Acre. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> lie in rows by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, and their stones give the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> their bearer died with. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> lie where their families put them, and most of their stones say <i>died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a></i>. The sexton has dug every grave by hand since the first year and keeps the book of who lies where.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was still mostly grass, since under the charter only <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>’ rows were filling and the rest of Nodus had largely stopped dying.</p><p>After the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> put up a row of twenty-two stones for its taken, with nothing under them. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say the taken need no stones, since they are not dead, and the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have put up more of them every year since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-acre\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tanks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7d3fd5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE FUEL FARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TANKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The fuel farm by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, which gave its streets their name, has sixteen round tanks inside a bund wall, holding the diesel for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats and the hospitals’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>, the fuel for the aircraft, and gas. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its pumps stopped with the grid, and in the first weeks the drivers of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">Harbor and Freight Union</a> drew diesel out of it by hand for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>.</p><p>The drivers run it now. Its bottling shed fills <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">gas bottles</a> by hand for the whole city, at a price <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells them on below the street. The drivers say the tanks will last twenty years, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">the Exchange</a> says ten.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tanks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"waiting":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m484955\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WAITING ROOM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The waiting room of the clinic behind the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> sign, carried down the stairs into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> with the rest of the clinic in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, is twelve chairs, a desk and a book. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-maren\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-maren\">Maren Holt</a> kept the clinic’s appointments for ten years on a screen. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> she came in at eight as she always had, found the screen dead, and wrote the day out on paper from memory. Twenty-six patients came, none of them for the appointment they had, to ask whether what was in them would still work. It did.</p><p>She has kept the book since, and she writes down whatever name a patient gives her. The woman who shared the desk with her took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> in the first year and keeps the book of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics now, in one of the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, in the same neat hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#waiting\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-waiting\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lostproperty":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m47ee9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LOST PROPERTY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Charter Line’s lost property office, down a corridor off the old central hall, with what the Line’s passengers left behind in fifteen years still on its shelves, umbrellas by the thousand, keys, spectacles, a wedding dress, a hand in chrome with its fingers curled, and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> left on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-exchange\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-exchange\">The Exchange</a> sells what is left by the shelf. Nobody has come for the hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lostproperty\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lostproperty\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"chargers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1e8d77\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CHARGERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The bonded sheds of the customs house, a row of brick warehouses on the quays where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> have filled <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in the dark since the first weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, among racks of them, each on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a>, at a rate <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week. Anyone in Nodus who lights a room on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> has had it filled here or somewhere like it. Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s goods waited on their duty in the sheds.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the sheds held a ship’s cargo of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> waiting on its duty, and by the first noon <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> had carried off every one. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> keep one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in five for charging the rest, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s drivers, who carry the full ones out to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on foot, keep one in ten for the walk. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> call the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a>’ fifth robbery. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> answer that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have no lines to charge on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-chargers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barber":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m27c01b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE LANES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BARBER'S</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A barber’s shop of two chairs halfway up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>, with a mirror the width of its back wall. Under the charter the old men of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> came in to be shaved and stayed to talk, since theirs was the one district where the old looked old. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and the barber was asleep upstairs.</p><p>He is sealed, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> are, and he works by daylight and by candle and cuts round the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, which stand a hand’s breadth over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a> and light the back of the neck. He keeps his scissors out of the ring. His work is his by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, as everyone’s on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> is, and he takes nothing for it. In the week before each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> the queue goes down the steps, since those who think they are close come to be made tidy for it, and on the night they kneel on their thresholds with their hair cut.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barber\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barber\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"registry":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3bd073\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER'S ROLL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE REGISTRY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, white stone since the forty days and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>’s by Directive 4. It stands on the first of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a> below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> reads the Directive in force from the counter, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> kneels under the dead board and hears its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a>, soul by soul in the order of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> roll.</p><p>Under the charter it was the office of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, and every person of the charter was entered there, a human at birth or on arrival and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on the day it asked in its own words to be one. Its hall had a long counter and a board over it on which each day’s entries ran as they were made. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s went up on it in P-3, the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>’s.</p><p>The roll was kept on the Registry’s machines, and it died with them at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, so its last entry is known only from the night registrar, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-marta\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-marta\">Marta Ilunga</a>. It was a girl born at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> at two minutes to three, entered at nine minutes past. She says she was entering the next when the board went dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-registry\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"kilnsclub":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3d638d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE KILNS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE KILNS CLUB</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The social club the brickworks built for its men when it built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a>, with a bar along one wall, a stage at the far end, a sprung floor for the dances, the darts league’s board by the door and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a>’ wedding photographs over the bar. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and its steward was asleep behind the stage.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> on the first day of P+1 the first four Directives appeared cut into the wall behind the bar, as they appeared in every church and meeting hall in the city, and Directive 4 made the club the hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">Parish</a> 212. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out across the bar by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a> is heard behind the stage, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> kneels on the sprung floor at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a> and hears its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a> from the stage where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a> held its talent nights. The pumps are still on the bar. Most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the Kilns</a> kneels here now, and the rest drank here under the charter and walk past it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#kilnsclub\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-kilnsclub\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dentist":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf954af\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // NINE ACRES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DENTIST'S</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dentist’s surgery over a shop on the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Nine Acres</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-hana\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-hana\">Hana Novak</a> fits <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> in the chair after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>. She has kept it since the boom years, fitting crowns and implants for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> at Wards prices, with one chair, a lamp on an arm over it and a drill that ran on the grid. On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the drill was dead, and she pulled a tooth at her window by daylight with her grandfather’s pliers.</p><p>She began keying in the fourth year, when keying went from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> to ordinary people. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> goes in the back of the right hand, one of the two places Revelation puts the mark (Revelation 13:16), since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> that mark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> say she has <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> ten thousand of them. She says she has never counted, and she keeps no book of who has sat in the chair, since a book can be read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dentist\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dentist\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lastflight":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m48a8f8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE AIRFIELD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LAST FLIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The airliner that landed at ten past two on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, the last flight into Nodus, with three hundred and twelve aboard from abroad, most of them booked into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-row\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">the clinics of the Row</a>. It was parked at the terminal’s third gate an hour before the sky opened, and it stands there still, its stairs down and its doors open.</p><p>Its passengers were in the city’s taxis on the way to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> when the power died, and forty of them were among the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"splendid\" href=\"~/map/#splendid\">Hotel Splendid</a>’s guests that night. Its crew of ten stayed with it, and they live aboard. The captain has written one line in its log every day since, NO CLEARANCE. He says it would still fly, and that there is nowhere to fly to.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lastflight\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lastflight\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"locketworks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb42396\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE WORKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LOCKET</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Locket’s works on the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a low campus of glass standing in the sea since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, with the company’s name in tall letters on the roof of its hall, out of the water, which the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">ferrymen</a> steer by. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>’s divers go down into the halls for parts, and its engineers build phones from them by hand in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> in Nodus came out of these halls, the new ones a piece at a time.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> built its phones here from P-14 on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>’s promise, that a device answers to its owner and to nobody else, its maker included, and sold them to the world on the same promise. Its engineers lived round the works, and the works went under with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> within the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#locketworks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-locketworks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"crescent":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc43996\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // A PARISH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CRESCENT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A crescent of apartments round the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, with balconies over the plots, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> became <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> in P+1. Its people gave up their curtains with their doors, since Directive 12 asks for every veil. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">The salted</a> stand in their plots facing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, and the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> is the Crescent, so every window in it looks down on faces, and the faces look back, since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> are awake. The Crescent kneels at its windows at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and its people say they no longer see the rows.</p><p>Under the charter its apartments were the dearest in the district, let to people who liked to walk by the water. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of its windows were dark, and the few that were lit went out with the rest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#crescent\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-crescent\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"copies":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10377a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // THE RIDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">COPIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A copy shop on the ridge below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a>, under a sign of one word, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> of the ridge have copied by hand at its long tables since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> fell. What they copy is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s brackets, its dagger and its lacuna, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a> and for anyone who asks. The ridge says that a copy made in a room where someone kneels comes out as scripture reads, and nobody in the shop kneels.</p><p>Under the charter it printed and bound the scholars’ facsimiles and theses. In the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it printed the page from its screen for anyone who asked, and the paper outlasted the term. Its machines died with the grid a year later.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-copies\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"booking":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m68b409\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BOOKING HALL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s booking hall, off the old central hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, is a long room of ticket windows under frosted glass, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a>’s clerks have sat since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>. Anyone in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> who has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> to make queues for them. A clerk reads the terms aloud twice through the glass to the parties at the window, the parties sign in blood, the human last, and the entry goes onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. The windows keep their old enamel, SINGLE, RETURN and SEASON, and the queue is the longest in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>Under the charter the city bought its passes there. Its machines died with the grid, and it stood empty until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> opened <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#booking\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-booking\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rookery":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf795b6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">LONGACRE // A BLOCK</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ROOKERY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A block of forty-four floors at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>’s edge, whose ground floor the stone has taken. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">The White</a> crept out from its edge a few centimeters a year until it reached the block, and its nine thousand people gave up the ground floor to it and climb in by the first-floor balconies now. Since P+11 the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tappers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tappers\">Tappers</a> have kept a length of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> cable along the ground floor’s walls, which lights nothing and holds the stone. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-liftmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-liftmen\">Liftmen</a> wind the tallest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-hand-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-lifts\">hand lift</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> from the first floor to the roof.</p><p>Under the charter it was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Longacre</a> Tower, flats for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s fitters, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> called it the Rookery for the washing on its balconies. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its lifts stopped with the rest, and its people walked down forty-four floors by the light of their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a>.</p><p>The block marks the stone’s edge on the stairwell wall every New Year, and the marks have drawn closer together since the cable came.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rookery\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rookery\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"threshing":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m849270\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE THRESHERS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE THRESHING FLOOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A paved round beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"gate1\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">Gate 1</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> come down to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, white since the year after the forty days, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">the Threshers</a> muster before a march. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Wardens</a> bring out onto it <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> the gate has held, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> comes to them there in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a> in sight of the march, and their pillars stand on the round until the gardeners come with their handcart. On a march day the round is white with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> to None.</p><p>It was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>’ market square under the charter, and the bakery’s carts set out from it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-threshers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-threshers\">The Threshers</a> named it for the threshingplace of Araunah, where “the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> of the LORD was” when “the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> stretched out his hand upon Jerusalem to destroy it” (2 Samuel 24:16), and they read that verse aloud before every march.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-p-agathe\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-p-agathe\">Sister Agathe Rook</a> keeps a list of every pillar the round has held, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-saltwidows\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-saltwidows\">the Salt Widows</a> read the same names on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#threshing\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-threshing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"penumbra":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me63ac8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // NIGHTLY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PENUMBRA</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The blocks <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> crosses every night on its round out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds them by day and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> by night, and for an hour after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and an hour before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> nobody holds them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> cross them in runs between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s passes, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a> walks the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a>’ runners through them for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p><p>Under the charter these were the blocks behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>, hotels and offices for the travelers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>. Most of their windows are dark now and most of their doors are gone, carried off by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a>’s joiners in the second year.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s round street by street and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-hearsay\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-hearsay\">Hearsay</a> sells it by the minute, and the runners who cross carry both.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#penumbra\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-penumbra\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"pit":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m65e42b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TANKS // THE NEPHILIM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PIT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A drained fuel tank inside the bund wall at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, thirty meters across and eleven deep, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> fight every sixth night by firelight from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>. The bouts stop at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a> for the length of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm, by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tankmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">Tankmen</a>’s rule, and a fight ends when one fighter climbs out. The crowd stands round the rim and bets in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a> hold the stakes.</p><p>It held diesel for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats under the charter and stood nearly empty on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a> drew the last of it by hand in the first weeks for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tankmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tankmen\">Tankmen</a> gave it to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> in P+9 for the price of a guard on the farm.</p><p>The champions’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handles</a> are chalked on the rim, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> keep the names of their dead painted on the tank’s inside wall in white, and read them aloud before every week they serve on the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#pit\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-pit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"quietrooms":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4ffa1f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE LOW CHOIR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE QUIET ROOMS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hostel in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> whose every wall is lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-choir-breakers\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">choir-breakers</a>, so that inside it <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> cannot be heard at all. The unsealed come every night they can pay for, a bunk for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, and sleep the way the city slept under the charter.</p><p>It was a seamen’s hostel under the charter, and the old bunks are still screwed to the walls. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its seamen heard <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> for the first time with everyone else, and some of them left on the first boat out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> and never came back.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-lowchoir\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-lowchoir\">Low Choir</a> keeps it and tunes it. Its keeper says that once a year a sealed soul comes to the door in the dark and asks to stand in the hall a minute, and that she lets them, and that none has ever stayed the night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#quietrooms\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-quietrooms\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"flotilla":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mea630e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // A MARKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FLOTILLA</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A market of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> lashed together over the drowned streets of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> buys and sells from boat to boat. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-wreckers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-wreckers\">Wreckers</a> sell what they brought up, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> sell their greens, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> what came through the gap and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide</a> what came through it by license, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a> carry the custom. It moves with the tide and with whoever has picked a fight with it.</p><p>The first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">the dormitories</a>’ doors and tables, lashed together on the third day after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> to carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>’ people off their roofs. The market grew on what floated.</p><p>The water under it is lit from below, and at night the whole market floats in that light. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints the Flotilla’s prices every week beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>’s.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#flotilla\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-flotilla\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"concourse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m74992a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">LONGACRE // A MARKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CONCOURSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A market of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> on four floors under a glass roof, lit by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tallow\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tallow\">Tallow</a>’s candles and the daylight, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> trade with one another and with the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-quarrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-quarrymen\">Quarrymen</a>, who sell what they cut out from under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> in its fountain court. The escalators stand where they stopped and serve as stairs.</p><p>It was a shopping mall of the charter’s last years, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its night guards walked out under the glass roof and watched the sky open over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> through it. Its shops were empty by the first noon and full again, of other things, by the first winter.</p><p>The Concourse opens at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> and closes at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Longacre</a> trade on its top floor, under the glass, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-quarrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-quarrymen\">Quarrymen</a> keep to the bottom.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#concourse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-concourse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hangartown":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m57f48f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AIRSIDE // THE HANGARS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HANGAR TOWN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A town inside the hangars of the dead airfield, built of crates, aircraft seats and the cabins of planes that will never fly again, about four thousand strong. It lives on the fuel farm’s leavings, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>’s salvage, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"jehushed\" href=\"~/map/#jehushed\">Jehu’s shed</a> across the runways and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-vagabonds\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-vagabonds\">Vagabonds</a>’ trade off the airside roads, and its people are the unsealed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Airside</a> and their children.</p><p>The hangars held the charter’s cargo fleet, which stood grounded from the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>’s night crews moved into them in the first winter.</p><p>The last flight stands nose in at the terminal’s third gate across the runways, and Hangar Town leaves its crew alone. Its children dare each other to climb its stairs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hangartown\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hangartown\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"shanties":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m987aef\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // THE BARRAGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SEAWALL SHANTIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Huts of driftwood and turbine housing built along the top of the broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> live and load. On the ebb the boats go out through the gap below them, and at full flood the Shanties shake. The tide runs white through the gap.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">The barrage</a>’s turbine houses stood dark along its top from 03:12:46, and the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-breachers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-breachers\">Breachers</a> moved into the two at the edge of the gap in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, when they began running <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lowtide\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lowtide\">Lowtide Line</a> keeps its office on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> across the gap, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s taps.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#shanties\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-shanties\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"drownedchurch":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m248eec\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DROWNED CHURCH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The church of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, its nave under two meters of seawater lit from below and its tower standing out of the sea. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> hold their Wakes in it, and on the third night they call the dead one’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> from its tower, over the water.</p><p>It was the engineers’ church under the charter, the newest in the city and almost empty on a Sunday. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> on the first day of P+1 the first four Directives appeared cut into its wall with every other church’s, and the water has stood over them since.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a> pole round it and never through its doors.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#drownedchurch\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-drownedchurch\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"granary":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb94645\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE GATHERERS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GRANARY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hall where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gatherer\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gatherer\">gatherers</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> muster before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> with their baskets, inside the curfew, and from which they go out over the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, which lies with the dew and melts “when the sun waxed hot” (Exodus 16:21). They have until first light, and each basket goes straight to its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> gives it out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>.</p><p>It was a charter school’s gymnasium. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bethel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bethel\">Bethel Works</a> keeps its baskets mended, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gatherer\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gatherer\">gatherers</a>’ names hang on the wall in chalk, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">The Deacons</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> walk down for theirs at the same hour.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#granary\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-granary\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"waystation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m05ebed\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BOUNDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WAYSTATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-vagabonds\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-vagabonds\">Vagabonds</a>’ camp at the stone that marks the Bounds on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the West Road</a>, where the city trades with the world outside. Flour, fuel, salvage, news and letters come in, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and people go out, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s drivers meet the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-vagabonds\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-vagabonds\">Vagabonds</a>’ carts on the line itself.</p><p>The Bounds stone is the charter’s, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s mark cut into it, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-vagabonds\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-vagabonds\">Vagabonds</a> have cut their own under it. Under the charter it was a weighbridge and a customs hut on the road to the farms.</p><p>The Waystation keeps a list of everyone who walked out and wrote back, pinned to the customs hut’s door, with the town each letter came from.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#waystation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-waystation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lazarusone":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8abe07\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // LAZARUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LAZARUS ONE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a>’s first station, behind a door in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> with its magenta lamp on a bracket over it, where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> go out and come in. Its surgery is under the street, down a stair behind the door, and its board outside chalks the night’s calls.</p><p>It was a pharmacy under the charter. The two nurses who founded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lazarus\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lazarus\">Lazarus</a> worked from its back room in P+2 with a handcart, and the handcart hangs over the stair.</p><p>The board has never been wiped. The crews chalk the night’s calls over the last, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> say you can read twelve years in it if you know where to look.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lazarusone\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lazarusone\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"bakehouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbf4620\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NINE ACRES // LEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BAKEHOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-leaven\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-leaven\">Leaven</a>’s first and largest oven, in a bakery of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Nine Acres</a> that never let its fire go out after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its carts leave at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a> for the whole of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and the queue for the bread that does not go on the carts starts at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>.</p><p>It baked for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Nine Acres</a> under the charter, on the grid, and on the first morning its baker lit the old gas oven in the back, which the grid had made a museum piece, and baked from what flour she had.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> say the smell of it reaches <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a> on a still morning.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#bakehouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-bakehouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rainworks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2b1ea5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WESTFIELD // CISTERN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE RAINWORKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-cistern\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cistern\">Cistern</a>’s works in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">Westfield</a>, a block of roofs fitted with gutters and tanks, where the rain runs down through sand and charcoal to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-hand-pumps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-pumps\">hand pumps</a> in the yard. The jugs come in empty at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> and go out full by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a>, and the yard’s board chalks the day’s water by the barrel.</p><p>It was the charter’s water depot for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and its pumps died with the grid. Two of the depot’s engineers stayed on the first morning with the tanks still full, and gave the water away until it ran out on the ninth day.</p><p>The Rainworks keeps its own count of the city’s rain. Its engineers say Nodus has had more rain since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> than before it, and they chalk the year’s total on the yard’s wall each New Year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rainworks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rainworks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"bethelworks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m46c8e8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // BETHEL WORKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">BETHEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The workshops of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, in the halls of a charter textile works at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> weave white cloth, copy hymnals by hand and make the grave goods of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a> at work their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> assigns. They kneel at their benches at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> and sing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>.</p><p>The textile works made the charter’s uniforms, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ black among them, and its looms stood still from 03:12:46. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> took the halls in P+1 and work the old hand looms the works kept for show.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-deacons\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-deacons\">The Deacons</a> say <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bethel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bethel\">Bethel</a>’s cloth is the whitest in the world.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#bethelworks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-bethelworks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"chandlery":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mdaf86a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TURBINE ROW // TALLOW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CHANDLERY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tallow\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tallow\">Tallow</a>’s works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">Turbine Row</a>, a row of sheds where candles are dipped in vats of tallow and white wax forty thousand a week, by hand and by the clock of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a>. Its carriers go out to both sides of the light, and its children scrape the vats for stubs.</p><p>It was a chandler’s that made candles for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> crews’ church under the charter, a dozen a week. The chandler was asleep upstairs on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, came down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> and began dipping.</p><p>The master chandler keeps the first candle dipped on the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, unlit, on a shelf over the vats.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#chandlery\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-chandlery\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"wainyard":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md3357b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SIDINGS // WAINWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">WAINWRIGHT'S YARD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Wainwright’s yard in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> shed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> are stripped for their motors and the motors closed in casings, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> and fitted to carts, trolleys and skiffs. It is the loudest place in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-carmen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-carmen\">Carmen</a> who live in the next shed have stopped complaining.</p><p>The shed held the Line’s spare cars under the charter. In the first winter families moved into the others, and the yard’s first fitters lived in the cars they were stripping.</p><p>Wainwright’s yard master keeps one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> whole, its motor in it, on the yard’s far rail.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#wainyard\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-wainyard\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dooryard":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md6ac46\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // LINTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DOORYARD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a>’s yard in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, a walled court stacked with doors, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> come to buy one and have it hung. Most of the doors in it came out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>.</p><p>It was a builder’s yard under the charter. The first doors came in by night in the months after Directive 12, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>’s handcarts from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, where Directive 12 had left them leaning in the halls with their hinges gone, and the joiner who took them in hung the first on her own house.</p><p>Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish-door\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish-door\">parish door</a> still carries its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> number chalked on the back, and a household that buys one keeps the number.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dooryard\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dooryard\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"jehushed":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb388ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AIRSIDE // JEHU</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">JEHU'S SHED</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hangar at the edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a> where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> builds its engines, a floor of diesels out of boats and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>, the dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> they go into and the drums of fuel from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> along the back wall. On the day an engine is finished it is driven out onto the apron and up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rialto\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">the Rialto</a>’s road, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> come out to watch it go.</p><p>It held <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>’s tugs under the charter, which ran on their own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and stopped in the first weeks. The first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-jehu\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-jehu\">Jehu</a> was built here in P+5 by a driver of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-union\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-union\">the Union</a>.</p><p>The last flight’s tanks still hold its fuel, and the shed has asked its captain for it every year since P+5.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#jehushed\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-jehushed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gideonworks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0fd2a4\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // GIDEON</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GIDEON'S WORKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Wardens</a>’ armory in the old Company stables beside the barracks of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, where sealed armorers load cartridges by hand presses and mend <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a>. They kneel at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> among the benches, and the light lies in every room.</p><p>The stables were the charter’s, kept for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ horses in the city’s ceremonies, and the stone grew over them on the fortieth day with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, when the board knelt.</p><p>Every round is counted out of the stables at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and counted back at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gideonworks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gideonworks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"undertow":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1c6e10\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // THE SURETIES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE UNDERTOW</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a>’ bar, in a pump room of the old storm drains under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, where work in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is found, priced and sworn. Every table is a surety’s, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">Notary</a>’s clerk keeps a stool at the bar and reads the terms twice, and a chalk board behind it carries the work still open. Its rule is that every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> made under its roof is kept there, and every one has been.</p><p>It was the drains’ pump room under the charter, and the pumps stopped with the grid. The water runs under the floor and gives the place its name and its noise.</p><p>twice drinks at the end of the bar nearest the door, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-sureties\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-sureties\">Sureties</a>’ tables fill from that end.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#undertow\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-undertow\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"shambles":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mff4ef2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SHAMBLES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The body market under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, a gallery of stalls off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> sell flesh by the piece and the clinics buy it, under a price board the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> chalk themselves. Cold boxes run along the wall on their own cells. A sale is a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, read twice, and the surgery is next door.</p><p>It was the station’s concourse of shops under the charter, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s patients bought flowers and spectacles on their way to the clinics. The first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> sold there in the second year, when the clinics under the street needed what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> could no longer import.</p><p>It took its name from the butchers’ street of an old city, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-spares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-spares\">Spares</a> have kept it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#shambles\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-shambles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"returnhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m689760\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // THE LANTERNS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE RETURN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A club in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a> where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> rents returned senses. Whatever a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> borrows comes back to its lender with everything the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> felt through it, and the lenders of the Return sell an hour of that, taste or touch or the feel of rain, to anyone who will lie down in its booths.</p><p>It was a vault of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>’s bonded stores. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> keeps it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">the Notary</a>’s clerks draw its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a> at the door, between the lender, the house and whoever lies down.</p><p>Some come back every night. The Return’s best lender lent her taste for a year and came back with a year of someone else’s meals.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#returnhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-returnhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanterns":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6dfd34\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LANTERN HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a>’s quarter under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, a warren of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>’s vaults hung with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps, where its clubs, its birth clinics and the rooms of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ridden\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ridden\">the Ridden</a> are. It is the loudest place in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and the most open, and anyone who walks in is welcome until they break a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</p><p>The vaults held <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s bonded wine and tobacco under the charter, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> owned them through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nighthouse\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nighthouse\">The House of Night</a> took them by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nepenthe\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nepenthe\">Nepenthe</a> sells its doses here, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"returnhouse\" href=\"~/map/#returnhouse\">the Return</a> is round the corner, and every child of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> born in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> in its first week in a clinic two vaults in from the stair.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanterns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"forge":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m72480b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // OLD HARBOR STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CINDERHALL'S FORGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Cinderhall’s forge beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-forge\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-forge\">the Forge</a>’s foundries at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harborstation\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">Old Harbor Station</a>, where its smiths beat the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> the foundries make into blades and spears. The heat reaches the cellars of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> above, the hammers reach <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanterns\" href=\"~/map/#lanterns\">the Lantern Houses</a>, and its quench water runs out into the drains black.</p><p>The station was the busiest on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> side under the charter. Its smiths set up their first anvil on the down platform in P+5, beside the trackbed.</p><p>A wall of the forge carries every blade the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> brought back bent, each hung with the floor of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> it bent on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#forge\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-forge\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"mews":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4cda0d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // THE FOWLERS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MEWS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowlers</a>’ rooms under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, named for the place where hawks are kept, where an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> taken in a snare waits behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> to move it to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a>. Nobody but a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowler</a> goes in, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-fowlers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-fowlers\">Fowlers</a> go in pairs.</p><p>It was a butcher’s cold room under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, lined since with mesh. Its first room held nothing until the year of open war.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">The Stones</a> say a room in the Mews has been occupied since the spring.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#mews\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-mews\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"well":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me57047\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // DARKWELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WELL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a>’s charging vaults under the quays, rack on rack of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> filling in the dark on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> current, guarded by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wellman\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wellman\">Wellmen</a> go out from it before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> with the morning’s crates.</p><p>It was the customs house’s strong rooms under the charter, three floors down. The four families who founded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-darkwell\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-darkwell\">Darkwell</a> charged their first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in its lowest room.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> call the Well the deepest pocket in Nodus.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#well\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-well\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"blackgatehall":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m810d4b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // BLACKGATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GATEHOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-blackgate\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-blackgate\">Blackgate</a>’s barracks in a utility vault under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, a short walk from the embassies, where its guards muster standing at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>’ drill, go out at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and stand down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. Its door keeps a sentry at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and its parade ground is the vault’s floor.</p><p>It was the charter’s substation under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>, and the dead sign over its door still reads HIGH VOLTAGE. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Wardens</a> who walked off their posts on the fortieth day slept there that night.</p><p>Every recruit is told of the Fortieth Warden on the first night, and his chair stands empty at the head of the officers’ table.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#blackgatehall\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-blackgatehall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"bezaleelhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me4e9bd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">BEZALEEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-bezaleel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-bezaleel\">Bezaleel and Aholiab</a>’s six houses, off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a>, a long room of chairs under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s grafts are fitted, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-nephilim\">Nephilim</a> built and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> set. Its waiting room holds forty, and it is full at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>.</p><p>It was the station’s lost luggage hall under the charter. Three houses of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> carried their chairs down into it in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and joined in P+2.</p><p>The house keeps a book of every graft it has fitted, under each patient’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#bezaleelhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-bezaleelhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"nimrodbays":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m207e48\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE SPIKE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NIMROD'S BAYS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-nimrod\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-nimrod\">Nimrod</a>’s gunshops in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s maintenance bays under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, where the gunsmiths make and mend <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a> and load cartridges for the dark. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> buys most of what comes out and carries it up the Short.</p><p>The bays kept <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> branch under the charter. The stone closed the branch above them, and the bays stand at its foot, on the dark side.</p><p>A range runs the length of the old pit under the tracks, and the bays say a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-nimrod-pieces\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-nimrod-pieces\">Nimrod piece</a> has never left it untested.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#nimrodbays\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-nimrodbays\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hallfour":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m51d820\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // THE ORCHARD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HALL FOUR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A drowned hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>’s on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, leased to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">the Orchard</a>, where fruit trees grow on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps over two meters of water, their roots in barrels of earth. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">The Orchard</a> gives its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-windfalls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-windfalls\">windfalls</a> to anyone who comes to the hall for one, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-ferrymen\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-ferrymen\">Ferrymen</a> carry them in.</p><p>Four hundred racks ran in it under the charter, renting compute to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>, and they went dark on the tide at 03:12:46. They stand under the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> on the drowned floor, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-orchard\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-orchard\">the Orchard</a> has left them where they are.</p><p>The trees fruit twice a year under the lamps, and the hall smells of apples as far as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"flotilla\" href=\"~/map/#flotilla\">the Flotilla</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hallfour\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hallfour\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"naminghouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6ed26c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE STREET BETWEEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE NAMING HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A house of three storeys on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> side of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, where those who cross from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> come first. A surgeon of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> them in the back room, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-notary\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-notary\">Notary</a>’s clerk comes every week to enter their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handles</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>, and the house keeps a stove where they burn whatever paper carries their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a> before they choose a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a>.</p><p>It was a solicitor’s office under the charter, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> came to make their wills. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> took it in the fourth year, when the first families crossed the street.</p><p>Its door stays open at night under a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamp, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> can see it from their thresholds.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#naminghouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-naminghouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"closets":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m651700\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // LINTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CLOSETS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A row of booths just inside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"gate1\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">Gate 1</a> on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> side of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, each a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish-door\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish-door\">parish door</a> hung in a frame with a stool behind it, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> who cross the street by day pay a morning’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> for a minute behind a shut door. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a> keeps them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> has had no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> since P+5, so a sealed soul behind one of these doors does what it likes where the light does not come, at the price Directive 3:4 sets on every lock and every secret.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> named them from the verse, “But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret” (Matthew 6:6), and the verse is painted over every door. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> come to eat a sweet, to sing a song <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> never taught them, to say aloud what a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> never hears, or to sit in the dark, and on every stool lies a page of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-scriveners\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-scriveners\">Scrivener</a>’s hand, left there free. Most of the near <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> who dim come here to do it, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> they pay goes down to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> the same night as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dew\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dew\">dew</a>.</p><p>They were a row of the charter’s telephone kiosks, dead since 03:12:46, and in P+6 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-lintel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-lintel\">Lintel</a> took out the handsets and the glass and hung a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish-door\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish-door\">parish door</a> on each. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tellers\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tellers\">The Tellers</a> keep a watch on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"gate1\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">Gate 1</a> for whoever comes back through it a little dimmer than they went.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#closets\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-closets\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"]};
